window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y1v4-index"]=[{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner","w":"karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 1  karuizawa kei s soliloquy volume cold open  karuizawa s first person soliloquy  alone post shower at the mirror  no other character appears  and p 11 carries no prose   in the end  nothing changed even after i came to this school   no  that s wrong  maybe i never had any intention of changing   my life was destroyed because of that nightmarish day  i lost my youth  my friends  and even myself   the most important thing is protecting myself  i ll do whatever it takes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1\">Ch.1: Karuizawa Kei’s Soliloquy<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.10–11<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Volume cold open: Karuizawa’s first-person soliloquy, alone post-shower at the mirror; no other character appears, and p.11 carries no prose.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “In the end, nothing changed even after I came to this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “No, that’s wrong… Maybe I never had any intention of changing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “My life was destroyed because of that nightmarish day. I lost my youth, my friends, and even myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Opens by measuring herself against the class: she is certain “none of the boys or girls like me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Claims the knowing no longer hurts, then turns it outward: “Because for some reason, I want them to feel that way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> At the mirror she grips the sink and vomits at “that old wound on my side” — the page ties her self-loathing to an unnamed past and never says what happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “The most important thing is protecting myself. I’ll do whatever it takes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Closing self-assessment: “I’m a parasite, a weak creature that can’t survive on its own.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Translation defect kept as printed: “Why did I have to have to go through” — the verb is doubled.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank/short scan page: running footer only; no prose to cite.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.0: she reclaims the table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 0  the cabin reverie and the horikita bridge three days after the island test  the cruise ship respite  ayanokoji s cabin reverie  hirata s interruption  and the deck lunch that follows   sigh  if only i had the power to rotate the earth on its axis myself   i ll pass  i don t think i m on especially good terms with karuizawa s group   well  i don t particularly dislike the idea  but  didn t you already promise karuizawa   but even if i can bring you both together  things won t be that easy  horikita is difficult","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the cabin reverie and the Horikita bridge<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.12–20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Three days after the island test, the cruise-ship respite; Ayanokōji’s cabin reverie, Hirata’s interruption, and the deck lunch that follows.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sigh. If only I had the power to rotate the earth on its axis myself…”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’ll pass. I don’t think I’m on especially good terms with Karuizawa’s group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, I don’t particularly dislike the idea, but… Didn’t you already promise Karuizawa?”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The rule he entered school under: “Contact with anyone outside is forbidden until graduation.” Chabashira’s leverage rides on it — she threatened to expel him from this paradise unless he works toward Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> A “little devil” perched on his shoulder whispers that “It’s better to get them before they get you”; he spends a second imagining forcing Chabashira to resign, then returns to blank thinking.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rates the boys aboard as “beasts—sex-starved carnivores” waiting like predators while the girls chatter — his anthropology of the vacation mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Grades the friendship tiers: at the bottom strata, “low-level friends are only invited ten percent of the time” — and he is the lowly friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Asks after Karuizawa’s recovered underwear and is satisfied with Hirata’s quiet resolution of the fiasco.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Hirata’s invitation as carrying “some kind of ulterior motive” before the ask lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But even if I can bring you both together, things won’t be that easy. Horikita is difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Takes the go-between job while admitting he usually just goes along with whatever Horikita says — “I’ve never really forced my opinion on her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Executes his “Speedy Escape” the moment Karuizawa’s group closes ranks over Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Pressed into service as the Horikita bridge over lunch; he takes the ask but not the urgency.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Declines her group, then watches her reclaim Hirata anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.14, 20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The subject of Hirata’s request; he warns she will shut down if she senses manipulation.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"ch 2  the class a leverage  named twice named in ayanokoji s cabin reverie   the leverage that brought him to class a s track","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1\">Ch.2: the Class A leverage, named twice<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.12, p.34<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ayanokōji’s cabin reverie — the leverage that brought him to Class A’s track.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The threat that binds him: she “threatened to expel me from this paradise” unless he works toward Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator contrasts her with Mashima: where she seems “unmotivated and unnaturally uncooperative,” he is “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Still holds him with the Class A ultimatum three days after the island test.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p166-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the midnight point question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 0  he pulls ayanokoji to lunch ship cabin  he draws ayanokoji out of his sea gazing and steers him toward lunch  cancelling karuizawa s plan to do it   hmm  you haven t been in the room all this time  have you   you might make more friends if you were a little more proactive  ayanokouji kun  though i suppose it s none of my business   that s not true  though  i mean  you have sudou kun and the guys  and horikita san   i m planning to meet up with karuizawa san and the others at 12 30 to have lunch  do you want to come with  i think it ll be really fun   i can understand that you re feeling hesitant  that s exactly why i want you to rely on me   i can eat with karuizawa san and the others any time  but i haven t really had many opportunities to eat together with you  ayanokouji kun   thank you for helping on the deserted island  i m sorry i didn t thank you enough for helping to find the culprit  ayanokouji kun   even so  i m grateful to you for helping","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: he pulls Ayanokōji to lunch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.13–16<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ship cabin: he draws Ayanokōji out of his sea-gazing and steers him toward lunch, cancelling Karuizawa’s plan to do it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Hmm? You haven’t been in the room all this time, have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “You might make more friends if you were a little more proactive, Ayanokouji-kun. Though I suppose it’s none of my business.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “That’s not true, though. I mean, you have Sudou-kun and the guys, and Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m planning to meet up with Karuizawa-san and the others at 12:30 to have lunch. Do you want to come with? I think it’ll be really fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wears “that eternal, optimistic smile” and won’t leave a lone person alone; pushes past the refusals.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can understand that you’re feeling hesitant. That’s exactly why I want you to rely on me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can eat with Karuizawa-san and the others any time, but I haven’t really had many opportunities to eat together with you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls Karuizawa to cancel on the spot, despite Ayanokōji’s half-hearted protests.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you for helping on the deserted island. I’m sorry I didn’t thank you enough for helping to find the culprit, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, I’m grateful to you for helping.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Cancels their lunch without flinching; Ayanokōji expects her to blame him later, and he doesn’t seem to care.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 0  a passing mention in hirata s inventory named once at the cabin lunch  in hirata s list of the people who treat ayanokoji as a friend","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention in Hirata’s inventory<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.13<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once at the cabin lunch, in Hirata’s list of the people who treat Ayanokōji as a friend.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata’s line carries him: “you have Sudou-kun and the guys, and Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ch 2  2 0  a passing mention as the culprit named once as the underwear culprit  ayanokoji asks whether karuizawa got hers back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention as the culprit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.16<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the underwear culprit; Ayanokōji asks whether Karuizawa got hers back.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata confirms the fallout: naming her resolved things — “When she heard Ibuki-san was the culprit, things went smoothly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0–§3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 0  the ask  be the bridge to horikita top deck restaurant  over lunch he finally names his ask   ayanokoji as the bridge to horikita   honestly  there s something i d like your advice on   i wondered if you would act as a bridge to help reach horikita san  after all  class d will have to come together and work hard in the future  and i think horikita san will be indispensable   yes  i do understand  of course  horikita san only opens herself up to you  ayanokouji kun   i should probably reconsider how to do this  horikita san seems very fastidious and hypercritical  how do you manage to get along with her  ayanokouji kun   my plan was really short sighted   when ayanokoji calls the timing too soon   sorry  i invited you out to eat and made it all about me  well  let s eat  shall we","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.17–20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Top-deck restaurant: over lunch he finally names his ask — Ayanokōji as the bridge to Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Honestly, there’s something I’d like your advice on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I wondered if you would act as a bridge to help reach Horikita-san. After all, Class D will have to come together and work hard in the future, and I think Horikita-san will be indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yes. I do understand, of course. Horikita-san only opens herself up to you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Wants his own hand hidden — “Then, pretend I never spoke to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> “But I can’t come up with anything else right now. I don’t think I have the confidence to speak with Horikita-san, let alone persuade her. This is my last resort.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should probably reconsider how to do this. Horikita-san seems very fastidious and hypercritical. How do you manage to get along with her, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Has “over forty friends” yet is frustrated at missing a connection with one particular student.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My plan was really short-sighted.” (when Ayanokōji calls the timing too soon)<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. I invited you out to eat and made it all about me. Well, let’s eat, shall we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Notices Karuizawa approaching and shoots Ayanokōji a nonplussed look before the girls close ranks.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Wants her friendship first, then a working relationship, and lacks the confidence to ask her directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She arrives with her girls and takes the table back.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: he pulls Ayanokōji to lunch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 0  a hypothetical at the deck restaurant named once  hypothetically   what he and yamauchi would have done at the deck restaurant","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once, hypothetically — what he and Yamauchi would have done at the deck restaurant.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s aside: had they been there, they would have “foregone the food and feasted their eyes on the girls instead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 2  2 0  a hypothetical at the deck restaurant named once  hypothetically   what he and ike would have done at the deck restaurant","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once, hypothetically — what he and Ike would have done at the deck restaurant.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s aside: had they been there, they would have “foregone the food and feasted their eyes on the girls instead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: the neck-grab and the camera stimulus<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  2 0  she reclaims the table crash of the deck lunch  she arrives with her girls and reclaims hirata from the table ayanokoji just fled   ah  so you re here after all  hirata kun  let s eat lunch together","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: she reclaims the table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crash of the deck lunch: she arrives with her girls and reclaims Hirata from the table Ayanokōji just fled.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ah, so you’re here after all, Hirata-kun. Let’s eat lunch together!”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The girls pull chairs from another table, push Ayanokōji away, and circle Hirata — peaceful to noisy in seconds.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Happy and carefree in tone while overriding the cancellation; monopolising him is her default.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes the lunch he cancelled as if it were never made.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Karuizawa Kei’s Soliloquy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the fourth seat of the zodiac group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 1  the koenji corridor and sakura s call corridor on the third deck  koenji dripping from the pool  the bellhop s fourth warning  and ayanokoji s escape route   do you want something from me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.21–25<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Corridor on the third deck: Kōenji dripping from the pool, the bellhop’s fourth warning, and Ayanokōji’s escape route.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Do you want something from me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Throws the bellhop’s warning back at Kōenji — “I passed the ball, if you will” — to engineer his own escape.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the ship’s signboard map and fixes the layout in his head: nine decks plus a roof, guys on the third deck and girls on the fourth, the 24-hour lounge on the first.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes Sakura’s email call rather than kill time alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the cabin reverie and the Horikita bridge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 2  2 1  the wet corridor and the signature corridor by the pool  dripping wet in a bathing suit  a fourth warning from the bellhop  a signature demanded   ha ha ha  it appears you ve found me  eh   i don t dry myself off with a towel on principle ever since reaching the age of reason   do you have a pen and paper on hand   even though it s written on such a cheap notepad  it will certainly hold tremendous value in the future   please don t look so suspicious  i am the man who will carry japan s future on his back   oh ho  why  if it isn t little ayanokouji  hmm  what a coincidence   no  no  i ve no real business with you  i ve simply acknowledged you because we are schoolmates  also  though we are certainly not alike in terms of position  you are my roommate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the wet corridor and the signature<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.21–24<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Corridor by the pool: dripping wet in a bathing suit, a fourth warning from the bellhop, a signature demanded.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Ha ha ha! It appears you’ve found me, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I don’t dry myself off with a towel on principle ever since reaching the age of reason.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Do you have a pen and paper on hand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Signs the bellhop’s notepad “Kouenji Rokusuke” and presents it as a future-valuable gift.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even though it’s written on such a cheap notepad, it will certainly hold tremendous value in the future.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please don’t look so suspicious. I am the man who will carry Japan’s future on his back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Repeat offender — this is the fourth hallway stop; believes his autograph outranks the notepad and pen.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator’s standing assessment: “Kouenji was like poison.” Classmates steer clear; even Hirata would be brushed off.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flips his wet hair into Ayanokōji’s face without noticing.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh ho? Why, if it isn’t little Ayanokouji, hmm? What a coincidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, no, I’ve no real business with you. I’ve simply acknowledged you because we are schoolmates. Also, though we are certainly not alike in terms of position, you are my roommate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “little Ayanokouji”; confirms the cabin roommate pairing and splashes him mid-sentence.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou shinohara-satsuki ichihashi-ruri maezono ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"ch 2  2 2  the roommate appeal emails ayanokoji to the second deck and stammers through her roommate worry  flees when kushida appears   wah  a ayanokouji kun   n no  no  i m just kind of strangely nervous is all   ayanokouji kun  you re roommates with hirata kun  kouenji kun  and yukimura kun  right   oh  well  to tell you the truth  i i m a little worried about the people i m sharing a room with   i m not sure  i have mixed feelings  i do want to get along with them  but i also want to be alone  too  i m just hopeless  aren t i   oh  didn t i tell you  shinohara san  ichihashi san  and maezono san   i just thought any advice from you  ayanokouji kun  would be good   i i m sorry to just come to you for help like this out of the blue  you re so busy  ayanokouji kun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the roommate appeal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.25–28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Emails Ayanokōji to the second deck and stammers through her roommate worry; flees when Kushida appears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#ichihashi-ruri\">Ichihashi Ruri<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#maezono\">Maezono<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Wah! A-Ayanokouji-kun?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “N-no, no. I’m just kind of strangely nervous is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Ayanokouji-kun, you’re roommates with Hirata-kun, Kouenji-kun, and Yukimura-kun. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Nervous to the point of jolt-like surprise; her normally hunched posture straightens at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh. Well, to tell you the truth, I…I’m a little worried about the people I’m sharing a room with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not sure. I have mixed feelings. I do want to get along with them, but I also want to be alone, too. I’m just hopeless, aren’t I?”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh. Didn’t I tell you? Shinohara-san, Ichihashi-san, and Maezono-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I…just thought any advice from you, Ayanokouji-kun, would be good?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I-I’m sorry to just come to you for help like this out of the blue. You’re so busy, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> “retreated as fast as her legs would carry her” at Kushida’s arrival.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Rejection and flight; Kushida’s brightness lands as threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Names her as roommate one; the narration adds Shinohara won’t go out of her way for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichihashi Ruri<\/b> Roommate two — named only; no file yet (first appearance volume).<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Maezono<\/b> Roommate three — named only; no file yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Comes to him because “any advice from you…would be good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the bow stress-talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 2  sakura s worry  kushida s interrupt  the school message second deck hallway  sakura s roommate appeal  kushida s interruption  the school s test message  and the chat with horikita   you re worried because even though you want to get along with them  you don t think you can   it s no big deal  i don t mind it when you come to me for advice  whether i ll be of much help is another story   i m joking  don t you know by now that i m not the sort of person who joins in on stuff   did you get a message from the school just now   chat line  the corpus prints it bare after  i typed   yeah  i did   untagged chat reply  the thread has only these two   my designated meeting time is 18 00  what about yours   chat   mine says 20 40  that seems like a pretty big difference   untagged chat reply   because your time is earlier  i look forward to hearing your report   untagged chat reply  the narration marks her replies instant   understood   chat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.26–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-deck hallway: Sakura’s roommate appeal, Kushida’s interruption, the school’s test message, and the chat with Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You’re worried because even though you want to get along with them, you don’t think you can?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s no big deal. I don’t mind it when you come to me for advice. Whether I’ll be of much help is another story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m joking. Don’t you know by now that I’m not the sort of person who joins in on stuff?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Ship cabin roommates: Hirata, Kōenji, and Yukimura — Sakura states it; he doesn’t dispute it.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Compares messages with Kushida: his call is 18:00, hers 20:40, her room two doors down from his.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you get a message from the school just now?” (chat line; the corpus prints it bare after “I typed.”)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I did.” (untagged chat reply; the thread has only these two)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My designated meeting time is 18:00. What about yours?” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Mine says 20:40. That seems like a pretty big difference.” (untagged chat reply)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because your time is earlier, I look forward to hearing your report.” (untagged chat reply; the narration marks her replies instant)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Understood.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Horikita’s instant replies as unusual — she normally waits half a day, sometimes days, to read.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Keeps the Horikita chat to himself when Kushida draws near, deciding to wait and see.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Refuses her Class C outing, lets her see the phone, shares nothing about the chat.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Receives her roommate appeal; can only offer limited help.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  2 2  the hallway interrupt and the message compare exits a second deck room into the hallway mid meeting plan  interrupts sakura s appeal  then compares school messages with ayanokoji   huh  ayanokouji kun and sakura san  what are you doing here   ah  did i interrupt  i didn t mean to  i was supposed to meet up with some friends   i ve made plans to go see some girls from class c today  do you want to come  ayanokouji kun   oh jeez  come on  you surprised me a little  ayanokouji kun  you re funny","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the hallway interrupt and the message compare<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.27–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Exits a second-deck room into the hallway mid-meeting-plan; interrupts Sakura’s appeal, then compares school messages with Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Huh? Ayanokouji-kun and Sakura-san? What are you doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Ah, did I interrupt? I didn’t mean to. I was supposed to meet up with some friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I’ve made plans to go see some girls from Class C today. Do you want to come, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh jeez, come on. You surprised me a little. Ayanokouji-kun, you’re funny.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her true self “seemed puzzled by my response” when he says yes — the mask slips a little before the smooth recovery.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Without hesitation shows him her message: 20:40, a room two doors from his.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Draws nearer, curious about his chat with Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The bright entrance that sends Sakura fleeing; Kushida apologises to no evident purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Invites, reads his joke, shares her phone, watches his screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi shinohara-satsuki","q":"ch 2  2 2  named as sakura s roommate named as sakura s first roommate  with the narration s character sketch","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: named as Sakura’s roommate<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.27<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as Sakura’s first roommate, with the narration’s character sketch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Roommate; the narration sizes her up — close with Karuizawa, “like her boss, really” — reliable and unafraid of a fight, but relentless against people she doesn’t like, so she “probably wouldn’t go out of her way to befriend her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p174-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: the excuse name<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 2  the message chat chat only  ayanokoji messages her about the school s test notice  she replies instantly   yeah  i did   chat reply  the translation leaves the thread s lines untagged   mine says 20 40  that seems like a pretty big difference   chat   because your time is earlier  i look forward to hearing your report   chat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the message chat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.30–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chat only: Ayanokōji messages her about the school’s test notice; she replies instantly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yeah. I did.” (chat reply; the translation leaves the thread’s lines untagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Mine says 20:40. That seems like a pretty big difference.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Because your time is earlier, I look forward to hearing your report.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Replies instantly — against her usual half-day, sometimes days, reading lag.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Two further chat lines sit unassigned in the translation: “I’m curious about the difference in start times…” and “We can’t know anything for sure at this point.” The volume attribution list keeps them.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Off-page: Hirata’s whole lunch ask is about winning her over, routed through Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chat partner with the earlier slot; she defers his report.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action","w":"sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the zodiac briefing opens room 204 on the second deck  mashima s briefing table  sotomura and yukimura already seated  karuizawa as the late fourth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Room 204 on the second deck: Mashima’s briefing table, Sotomura and Yukimura already seated, Karuizawa as the late fourth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Takes the vacant seat beside Yukimura and waits out the unseen fourth member.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the setup as ominous — small groups, private rooms, a teacher who won’t take questions: “There was a storm coming, the curtain rising on a new test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Classmate at the table; the Professor greets him with “Ayanokouji-dono.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The roommate beside him; he stays quiet while Yukimura and Karuizawa trade blows.<span class=\"pg\">p.32, 36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The briefer: cold, unanswerable, “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The fourth member; she moves her chair away from him.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 2  2 3  the zodiac briefing briefs the four class d students in room 204  zodiac groups  thinking tested four ways   what are you doing  hurry and take a seat   we are still waiting on one more  please sit quietly   i believe you were told punctuality was key  and yet you re late  hurry and take your seat   sotomura  yukimura  ayanokouji  and karuizawa  from class d  without further ado  i will now explain the special test   i will not answer any questions at this time  be quiet and listen   in this special test  all the first year students will be divided into twelve groups based on the signs of the zodiac   society needs three fundamental qualities in order to progress  action  thinking  and teamwork  those with the necessary qualities will become wonderful adults   i ve already told you  i will not be answering any questions   you four gathered here will be in the same group  at this very moment  students in other rooms are receiving the same explanation you are   calm down  you two  yukimura  your concerns are groundless  the test hasn t yet begun  so you won t be affected  besides  your attitude has no bearing on this test","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Briefs the four Class D students in Room 204: zodiac groups, thinking tested four ways.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “What are you doing? Hurry and take a seat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “We are still waiting on one more. Please sit quietly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “I believe you were told punctuality was key, and yet you’re late. Hurry and take your seat”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sotomura, Yukimura, Ayanokouji, and Karuizawa, from Class D. Without further ado, I will now explain the special test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I will not answer any questions at this time. Be quiet and listen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In this special test, all the first-year students will be divided into twelve groups based on the signs of the Zodiac.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Names the four tested abilities: processing information, analyzing the situation, solving after clarifying, and creating new values through imagination.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Society needs three fundamental qualities in order to progress: action, thinking, and teamwork. Those with the necessary qualities will become wonderful adults.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve already told you. I will not be answering any questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You four gathered here will be in the same group. At this very moment, students in other rooms are receiving the same explanation you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, you two. Yukimura, your concerns are groundless. The test hasn’t yet begun, so you won’t be affected. Besides, your attitude has no bearing on this test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cold and unanswerable; the narrator pits him against Chabashira — she “unmotivated and unnaturally uncooperative,” he “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The comparison the narrator draws between the two homeroom instructors.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Warns her twice before shutting her questions down.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the handout and the four outcomes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 2  2 3  the professor at the briefing table already seated in room 204 beside yukimura when ayanokoji arrives for the zodiac briefing   so  one of the remaining two spots belongs to ayanokouji dono  i see  most agreeable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor at the briefing table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Already seated in Room 204 beside Yukimura when Ayanokōji arrives for the zodiac briefing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “So, one of the remaining two spots belongs to Ayanokouji-dono, I see! Most agreeable!”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Introduced as “The Professor”: overweight first-year in glasses, the male-otaku stereotype, deep in history and machinery — though his speech and inflection come off unintelligible, he somehow communicates.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Silent through the whole briefing and the Karuizawa–Yukimura quarrel; “The Professor and I stayed quiet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Greets him with the nerdy “Ayanokouji-dono.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The unexpected pairing — the narrator notes the Professor and Yukimura don’t normally sit together.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor’s interjections<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  odd company  first quarrel seated at mashima s table with the professor  first to spot that the gathering is odd   this is rather odd  isn t it  ayanokouji   how about you shut up and try listening  the test is probably going to start soon  if they dock our points because you keep blabbing  are you gonna take responsibility   even back on the deserted island  you dragged us all down  can you try not to cause any more problems","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: odd company, first quarrel<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32, p.36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Seated at Mashima’s table with the Professor; first to spot that the gathering is odd.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “This is rather odd, isn’t it? Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “How about you shut up and try listening? The test is probably going to start soon. If they dock our points because you keep blabbing, are you gonna take responsibility?”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Even back on the deserted island, you dragged us all down. Can you try not to cause any more problems?”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> First to lose patience with Karuizawa; point-anxious and practical.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Trades insults with her under the teacher’s eye.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Paired oddly at the table, by the narrator’s note.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  2 3  the fourth seat of the zodiac group fourth seat of the class d zodiac group  arrives to find three boys and a teacher  and questions it immediately   huh  what s going on  why are yukimura kun and these other guys here   w wait a minute  i don t understand  what do you mean  explain a test  the test was already over  right  also  what s the deal with these guys  this is really weird   jeez  all right  fine  i ll shut up   what do you mean by  test our thinking   i don t get what any of this means  can you explain it in a way that s easier to understand   these guys gross me out  why am i on a team together with boys  honestly  i hate it though being with hirata kun would be fine   huh  when and how exactly did i cause problems  you re pissing me off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the fourth seat of the zodiac group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.33–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fourth seat of the Class D zodiac group; arrives to find three boys and a teacher, and questions it immediately.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Huh? What’s going on? Why are Yukimura-kun and these other guys here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “W-wait a minute. I don’t understand. What do you mean, explain a test? The test was already over, right? Also, what’s the deal with these guys? This is really weird.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Jeez, all right. Fine, I’ll shut up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Studies the three boys, then lifts her chair and moves it away from Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean by ‘test our thinking’?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t get what any of this means. Can you explain it in a way that’s easier to understand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “These guys gross me out. Why am I on a team together with boys? Honestly, I hate it…though being with Hirata-kun would be fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? When and how exactly did I cause problems? You’re pissing me off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Barrages the teacher until told to be quiet twice; complies unhappily; blunt about the boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> His “you dragged us all down” lands; she fires back that he’s pissing her off.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Defies the cold briefer, then submits.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The only boy on the team she’ll tolerate.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: she reclaims the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the interrupter, the werewolf, the phone call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the four outcomes and the traitor rules still at mashima s table  the group roster  the handout of four outcomes  and the werewolf detour  all read through ayanokoji s eyes   karuizawa  if you don t change your attitude toward the teachers  it might leave a mark on your permanent record  that wouldn t be good  right  reads the traitor rules as flipping the test on its head  with answers accepted any time  no one would seriously aim for outcome  1  reduces the exam to four possibilities   the honest outcome  1  a wrong guess at the end  the traitor finding the vip  and the traitor misled   and wants to avoid the last one most of all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–49<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still at Mashima’s table: the group roster, the handout of four outcomes, and the Werewolf detour, all read through Ayanokōji’s eyes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Karuizawa, if you don’t change your attitude toward the teachers, it might leave a mark on your permanent record. That wouldn’t be good, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reads the traitor rules as flipping the test on its head: with answers accepted any time, no one would seriously aim for Outcome #1.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reduces the exam to four possibilities — the honest Outcome #1, a wrong guess at the end, the traitor finding the VIP, and the traitor misled — and wants to avoid the last one most of all.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Depressed hearing Karuizawa rank the three of them below Hirata, though he tries not to care.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Knows Ichinose from Class B and Ibuki from Class C off the printed roster; of Ibuki he thinks being in the same group “was a perverse kind of fate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Has never heard of the party game Werewolf — Karuizawa’s amazement lands on genuine ignorance.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Easily memorizes the prohibited-actions list: phone theft, threats for VIP information, impersonation by borrowed phone, and cross-class discussion until the exam ends — each punishable up to expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the school’s anonymity design means any school-sent message is “100% the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Warns her about her permanent record; she brushes it off.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The briefer he watches absorb Karuizawa’s interruptions without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the hallway split<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari sotomura-hideo hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  2 3  the interrupter  the werewolf  the phone call through the briefing she trades smirks with yukimura  interrupts mashima repeatedly  learns the four outcomes  and finally phones hirata   hmph   after ayanokoji s warning about her permanent record   ugh  jeez  this sucks  i can t deal with these three  hirata kun would have been so much better   gross  even if there were a hundred or two hundred of you  you still wouldn t be worth a single hair on hirata kun s head   to the professor   ugh  well  at any rate  i ll just report it to hirata kun later   okay  okay  i understand that we re being divided into these groups  but why is it only the four of us getting this explanation  i thought you d explain things after our entire group was gathered together   w wait a minute  what do you mean  i still don t get it at all  we re going to be grouped with students from other classes  isn t that crazy  though  aren t the other classes supposed to be the enemy   jeez  everyone s gonna be jealous of the vip  not being picked for it would be unfair  no matter what happens  that person still gets points  and if we get outcome  1  it s a million points   wait a second  ayanokouji kun  don t tell me you don t know about werewolf  whoa  i can t believe it   i m sorry  it s just  like  not having friends must be so sad   when his ignorance shows   well  you get together with your friends  and then you divide people up as either villagers or wolves  the one who survives at the end is th","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the interrupter, the werewolf, the phone call<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–50<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Through the briefing she trades smirks with Yukimura, interrupts Mashima repeatedly, learns the four outcomes, and finally phones Hirata.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Hmph.” (after Ayanokōji’s warning about her permanent record)<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ugh, jeez! This sucks! I can’t deal with these three! Hirata-kun would have been so much better!”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Gross. Even if there were a hundred or two hundred of you, you still wouldn’t be worth a single hair on Hirata-kun’s head.” (to the Professor)<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ugh. Well, at any rate, I’ll just report it to Hirata-kun later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, okay. I understand that we’re being divided into these groups, but why is it only the four of us getting this explanation? I thought you’d explain things after our entire group was gathered together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait a minute. What do you mean? I still don’t get it at all. We’re going to be grouped with students from other classes? Isn’t that crazy, though? Aren’t the other classes supposed to be the enemy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jeez, everyone’s gonna be jealous of the VIP! Not being picked for it would be unfair! No matter what happens, that person still gets points! And if we get Outcome #1, it’s a million points!”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Half-listens so hard her comprehension goes “abnormally bad” — the narration contrasts her with Sudō and Ike, who score poorly, versus her refusal to listen.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a second. Ayanokouji-kun, don’t tell me you don’t know about Werewolf? Whoa, I can’t believe it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. It’s just, like, not having friends must be so sad.” (when his ignorance shows)<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, you get together with your friends, and then you divide people up as either villagers or wolves. The one who survives at the end is the winner. Get it?” (explaining Werewolf)<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And that’s…on the other side of the handout, right? Is it okay if we turn it over?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Umm, umm. I kind of get it, but I kind of don’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, we can’t leave the room? How long do we need to stay in there?”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Agh. Well, this sounds kinda annoying, but I guess I do understand somewhat. Ugh. I just wish we had a test that was more fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ignores Yukimura’s huddle pitch, takes out her phone mid-hallway, and calls Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, hi, Hirata-kun? There was something I wanted to talk to you about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Trades barbs with him from the first smirks to the hallway dismissal.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Interrupts him four times; he answers without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The “hundred or two hundred of you” line lands on the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The call she makes the moment the briefing ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the fourth seat of the zodiac group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the Rabbit votes and Manabe’s phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 2  2 3  the handout and the four outcomes carries the briefing to its end  cross class groups  the printed roster  the vip handout  werewolf  and the meeting logistics   listen  your group assignments are a done deal  you cannot change them  to gain a good result on the test  you must get along   finished  please let me continue my explanation   it would appear that you cannot help but be concerned by this small gathering  therefore  i will try to provide an answer  this is neither a conspiracy against the students  nor is it harassment  it s rather simple  the groups don t consist of members from just one class  they are made up of about three to five individuals collected from each class  if we didn t explain things in advance  we would run the risk of confusion   you ve been competing until now  your school lives have only just begun  you shouldn t run around like a chicken with its head cut off this early  yukimura   right now  you shouldn t spend your energy on trying to understand this test  rather  focus on how to think  your group assignment is  rabbit  here is a list of the members  you will be required to return this list when you leave the room  if you feel it s necessary  i would recommend trying to memorize it now   don t worry  i will answer any questions you have  i believe you will be able to understand everything afterward  probably   the point of this test is to ignore the prior fraught relationships between classes a through d  if you do  you ll have a s","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the handout and the four outcomes<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–49<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Carries the briefing to its end: cross-class groups, the printed roster, the VIP handout, Werewolf, and the meeting logistics.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Listen. Your group assignments are a done deal. You cannot change them. To gain a good result on the test, you must get along.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Finished? Please let me continue my explanation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “It would appear that you cannot help but be concerned by this small gathering. Therefore, I will try to provide an answer. This is neither a conspiracy against the students, nor is it harassment. It’s rather simple. The groups…”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would appear that you cannot help but be concerned by this small gathering. Therefore, I will try to provide an answer. This is neither a conspiracy against the students, nor is it harassment. It’s rather simple. The groups don’t consist of members from just one class; they are made up of about three to five individuals collected from each class. If we didn’t explain things in advance, we would run the risk of confusion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve been competing until now? Your school lives have only just begun. You shouldn’t run around like a chicken with its head cut off this early, Yukimura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right now, you shouldn’t spend your energy on trying to understand this test. Rather, focus on how to think. Your group assignment is ‘Rabbit’. Here is a list of the members. You will be required to return this list when you leave the room. If you feel it’s necessary, I would recommend trying to memorize it now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I will answer any questions you have. I believe you will be able to understand everything afterward. Probably.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The point of this test is to ignore the prior fraught relationships between Classes A through D. If you do, you’ll have a shortcut.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From this point on, you are no longer acting as members of Class D, but rather as members of the Rabbit group. Whether you pass or fail this test depends on each group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Four outcomes only; handouts of the grade items may be verified on the spot but not taken, photographed, or copied.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The test runs from 8:00 a.m. day one’s message to 9:00 p.m. day four; two one-hour group meetings daily at set times and rooms; answers accepted only 9:30–10:00 p.m. the final night, by email, first submission per group counts, one answer per student, VIPs may not submit, results emailed 11:00 p.m.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Outcome #1: a correct final answer pays every group member 500,000 private points. Outcome #2: no or wrong final submission pays only the VIP 500,000.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This exam has one critical element. Understand it, and this test will not pose a problem. The key element is the existence of the VIP. There is only one VIP in the group. In this test, you’re after the name of the VIP. It’s that simple. For example, Yukimura, let’s say that you were chosen as VIP. The correct answer for the Rabbit group would be ‘Yukimura.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now then, as for Outcome #2… In the event that the VIP’s identity is not discovered before the end of the examination, and no one in your group found out the identity of the VIP or some even attempted to lie about the identity, then only the VIP will be awarded points, just as it says. He or she will receive 500,000 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you understand the explanation for the first two? If you do not, then we cannot continue.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Regarding the remaining outcomes, they are written on the reverse side of the handout. However, please wait a bit before turning the paper over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Very well, I will explain in simpler terms. Have you played the game Werewolf?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I said that there is only one VIP in the group, if the VIP is exposed right away, then Outcomes #3 and #4 will appear.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Outcome #3: an early correct answer by a non-VIP pays that student 500,000 private points and their class 50 class points, costs the VIP’s class 50, and ends the group’s test — a VIP-classmate’s early correct answer doesn’t count. Outcome #4: an early wrong answer by a non-VIP costs their class 50 class points and pays the VIP 500,000 plus 50 to the VIP’s class — a VIP-classmate’s early wrong answer doesn’t count.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school will take anonymity into account during this test. At the end, only the outcomes for each group and the increase or decrease in points for each class will be announced. In other words, we will not announce the names of the VIPs or those who submitted answers. Also, if you wish, you may have a temporary ID assigned to you, to which you can transfer points. It is also possible to divide points up and receive them that way. If you yourself remain quiet, there should be no fear of discovery after the test. Of course, if it’s not necessary for you to hide your identity, you may receive your points openly. That is perfectly fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Outcomes #3 and #4 are very different from the first two. That’s why they are listed on the reverse side of the sheet. With that, the explanation is complete.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There should also be a list of prohibited actions on the sheet. Make sure to examine it thoroughly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Prohibited: stealing phones, threats to confirm VIP information, using another’s phone to submit — up to expulsion; cross-class discussion until the exam ends — expulsion; school messages may not be copied, deleted, transferred, or modified.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Tomorrow, you will go to your designated room at 1:00 p.m. and again at 8:00 p.m. Your group’s name will be displayed on a nameplate… Be sure to introduce yourselves when you meet the other members for the first time. After you’ve entered, leaving the room during the examination is not permitted. Please use the restroom ahead of time. In the event that you feel ill or can’t endure it any longer, please contact your homeroom teacher immediately and make a request.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49-50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The explanation is written on the sheet. The discussion period is for one hour. Aside from self-introduction upon your initial meeting, you are free to use that time however you like. Once the hour has passed, you are free to remain in the room or to leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school is committed to fairness, so we will be strict and impartial. After the VIP has been selected, we will not accept any changes, not even if the VIP wants to be changed. In addition, copying, deleting, transferring, or modifying emails sent from the school is prohibited. Understand these points clearly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Flat, unchanging tone throughout; sharp-eyed when they reach for the paper — “It seemed like the exam had already begun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Absorbs her four interruptions without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Cuts his chicken-with-its-head-short speech down.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the phrasing he still hears<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 2  2 3  the professor s interjections three appearances inside the briefing day  the three heads quip  the confused handout  and the anime powered exit   heh  but you know  three heads are better than one  thus  if the three of us join together  we might be able to surpass the good hirata dono  my dear lady   this has turned into quite a bothersome ordeal  being partnered with a bitch like that  i mean   after karuizawa s call   that is certainly true  hmm  she s an unforgivable bitch  she s a bitch among bitches  wouldn t you say   agreeing with yukimura   i am terribly sorry  but i must decline your invitation  for you see  the love love alive anime calls  and i cannot afford to miss its siren song  i bid you farewell  hi ya","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor’s interjections<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37, p.41, p.51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Three appearances inside the briefing day: the three-heads quip, the confused handout, and the anime-powered exit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Heh. But you know, three heads are better than one. Thus, if the three of us join together, we might be able to surpass the good Hirata-dono, my dear lady,”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “This has turned into quite a bothersome ordeal. Being partnered with a bitch like that, I mean,” (after Karuizawa’s call)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “That is certainly true, hmm? She’s an unforgivable bitch. She’s a bitch among bitches, wouldn’t you say?” (agreeing with Yukimura)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Cocked his head over the handout alongside Karuizawa, “as if wracking their brains.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am terribly sorry, but I must decline your invitation. For you see, the Love Love Alive anime calls, and I cannot afford to miss its siren song. I bid you farewell. Hi-ya!”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration notes he often claims he wants the 2D world and that 2D women are perfect — which is why real girls like Karuizawa are rejected outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Echoes his exact “space cadets” line from minutes earlier, then turns down his huddle for anime.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Mocks her with the three-heads line, then insults her out of earshot.<span class=\"pg\">p.37, 51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor at the briefing table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the Professor in Rabbit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  the quarrel at the table spends the briefing trading barbs with karuizawa and absorbing mashima s rebuke   i  p pardon me   after mashima cuts him off   karuizawa  please  i m begging you  shut up and listen  i can t concentrate when you prattle on   you two are idiots  i ll explain it later  so don t keep bothering mashima sensei   shooting down karuizawa and the professor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–46<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spends the briefing trading barbs with Karuizawa and absorbing Mashima’s rebuke.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I… P-pardon me.” (after Mashima cuts him off)<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Karuizawa, please. I’m begging you, shut up and listen. I can’t concentrate when you prattle on”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “You two are idiots. I’ll explain it later, so don’t keep bothering Mashima-sensei.” (shooting down Karuizawa and the Professor)<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snorted derisively at Karuizawa without saying a word.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “seemed like he wanted to cozy up to school officials” — the narration’s read on why he polices the others’ questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The main target of his exasperation.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The teacher he stammers an apology to.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: odd company, first quarrel<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ichinose-honami","q":"ch 2  named on the rabbit roster twice named without a scene  on the printed rabbit group roster  and in kanzaki s portrait of a trusted class b boy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1\">Ch.2: named on the Rabbit roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.39, p.56<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Twice named without a scene: on the printed Rabbit group roster, and in Kanzaki’s portrait of a trusted Class B boy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed among the three Class B members of the Rabbit group — Ayanokōji knows her by name off the sheet.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kanzaki is described as the Class B student whom “Ichinose—Class B’s leader—seemed to trust.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Her trust is the credential the narration gives him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: taking the lead in Rabbit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 3  a passing mention in the comprehension sketch named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up karuizawa s refusal to listen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.43<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up Karuizawa’s refusal to listen.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The comparison: her problem “wasn’t that she scored poorly on tests like Sudou or Ike” — unlike them, she simply won’t listen.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: the contrast name<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 3  a passing mention in the comprehension sketch named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up karuizawa s refusal to listen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.43<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up Karuizawa’s refusal to listen.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The comparison: her problem “wasn’t that she scored poorly on tests like Sudou or Ike” — unlike them, she simply won’t listen.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention in Hirata’s inventory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p183-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.5–4.7: the Cow name and the warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  the failed huddle in the room and then the hallway  he probes ayanokoji  pitches a three man plan  and watches it dissolve   hey  ayanokouji  you ve been quiet  do you actually understand everything   for crying out loud  why on earth was i lumped in with a bunch of space cadets   said once in the room   why on earth was i lumped in with a bunch of space cadets   repeated in the hallway  word for word   i hate to say this  but if we have to be in the same group  we need to put up a unified front  a lot of things will depend on who the vip is  but for now  the four of us should discuss things   h hey  karuizawa  are you listening   maybe in the morning there ll be a notification that one of us was chosen as the vip  if one of us is chosen  it d be smart not to spread it around carelessly  we don t know who might be listening  let s get to a secure location before sharing info   to be honest  i really hate it  no matter what i do  she ll only drag us down   on karuizawa   karuizawa may be gone  but i want to talk about tomorrow  it makes sense to discuss it with just the three of us  let s go","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.49–51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the room and then the hallway: he probes Ayanokōji, pitches a three-man plan, and watches it dissolve.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Hey, Ayanokouji. You’ve been quiet. Do you actually understand everything?”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “For crying out loud, why on earth was I lumped in with a bunch of space cadets?” (said once in the room)<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Why on earth was I lumped in with a bunch of space cadets?” (repeated in the hallway, word for word)<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hate to say this, but if we have to be in the same group, we need to put up a unified front. A lot of things will depend on who the VIP is, but for now, the four of us should discuss things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “H-hey, Karuizawa. Are you listening?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe in the morning there’ll be a notification that one of us was…chosen as the VIP. If one of us is chosen, it’d be smart not to spread it around carelessly. We don’t know who might be listening. Let’s get to a secure location before sharing info.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50-51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I really hate it. No matter what I do, she’ll only drag us down.” (on Karuizawa)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa may be gone, but I want to talk about tomorrow. It makes sense to discuss it with just the three of us. Let’s go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sighs and shakes it off when the Professor declines and Ayanokōji doesn’t engage — “He didn’t seem to want to work with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Her phone call kills the huddle; he vents about her afterward.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The invitee who bows out for Love Love Alive.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Probes whether he understood the briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the hallway split leaving mashima s room  yukimura s huddle plan collapses when karuizawa calls hirata and the professor declines   for the most part  i guess  i d like you to explain the things i don t fully understand later  though   to yukimura  who asked whether he understood","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the hallway split<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.50–51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaving Mashima’s room: Yukimura’s huddle plan collapses when Karuizawa calls Hirata and the Professor declines.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “For the most part, I guess. I’d like you to explain the things I don’t fully understand later, though.” (to Yukimura, who asked whether he understood)<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Feigns incompleteness on purpose — “I wasn’t going to tell Hirata anything more” in the later hallway talk — and lets Yukimura’s discontent pass unnoticed.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Agrees the ship may be bugged, accepts Yukimura’s secure-location plan in principle, then reports the Rabbit rules to Horikita by chat and starts shaping a strategy alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The one classmate who tries to build a three-man huddle with him; Yukimura sighs and drops it.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 5  the katsuragi warning and the cold exit off screen first   ayanokoji reports the rabbit rules to her by chat   then on the second deck she faces katsuragi  holds against kanzaki s interlude  and turns her back on ryuen   yes  i am  and what exactly does that have to do with you   to katsuragi   you wanted to speak with me  funny  didn t you completely ignore me the other day   that s rather petty  from class a s perspective  are we such a big deal  i mean  there s a significant gap in points between us   you needn t concern yourself  class d has always been regarded as inferior  i d welcome any change in our reputation   what do you mean   when katsuragi calls the island win luck   we haven t gotten into college yet  i don t think you and i are so different  the school arbitrarily divided us into different classes  don t forget that   if we re going to continue this pointless conversation  i d prefer to just go inside  besides  it s about time   flipping her hair away from ryuen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.51, p.55–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Off-screen first — Ayanokōji reports the Rabbit rules to her by chat — then on the second deck she faces Katsuragi, holds against Kanzaki’s interlude, and turns her back on Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yes, I am. And what exactly does that have to do with you?” (to Katsuragi)<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You wanted to speak with me? Funny. Didn’t you completely ignore me the other day?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s rather petty. From Class A’s perspective, are we such a big deal? I mean, there’s a significant gap in points between us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Receives his chat report on the Rabbit group’s rules; her reply is not printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You needn’t concern yourself. Class D has always been regarded as inferior. I’d welcome any change in our reputation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean?” (when Katsuragi calls the island win luck)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We haven’t gotten into college yet. I don’t think you and I are so different. The school arbitrarily divided us into different classes. Don’t forget that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we’re going to continue this pointless conversation, I’d prefer to just go inside. Besides, it’s about time.” (flipping her hair away from Ryūen)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn’t back down before the Class A entourage; the narration credits her — weak-willed students would ingratiate themselves, she acts as she always does.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads her own new reputation: other classes now treat her selfishness as class concern and fear her as a hidden mastermind.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The pivot from his island-test indifference to a Class A threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Declines his rescue — “You needn’t concern yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Exits on him mid-provocation.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Both summoned to the 20:40 meeting (see Hirata’s row).<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the message chat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0: the Blue Ocean briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 4  the wake up and the scattered explanations just before 20 30 he wakes in the third deck cabin to hirata s apology  and they step out together toward the evening s meetings   can t really say  i haven t been thinking about the exam like you  horikita  and yukimura have  i m not smart  either  so i haven t really noticed much   deflecting hirata s request for observations   yeah  i think you re right  hirata  it would definitely be more efficient to explain the test to all the students at the same time  rather than dividing us into groups and doing it in stages  suspects the school s deliberately scattered briefings mean their  thinking  is already being tested","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Just before 20:30 he wakes in the third-deck cabin to Hirata’s apology, and they step out together toward the evening’s meetings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Can’t really say. I haven’t been thinking about the exam like you, Horikita, and Yukimura have. I’m not smart, either, so I haven’t really noticed much.” (deflecting Hirata’s request for observations)<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yeah, I think you’re right, Hirata. It would definitely be more efficient to explain the test to all the students at the same time, rather than dividing us into groups and doing it in stages.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Suspects the school’s deliberately scattered briefings mean their “thinking” is already being tested.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Walks him to the second deck while sharing nothing of substance.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the hallway split<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 4  the wake up and the scattered explanations in the third deck cabin he straightens his luggage  puts on his uniform  and wakes ayanokoji for the evening s meetings   i m sorry  did i wake you   would you like to come with me  i was thinking the school s message should be coming pretty soon   did you notice anything  ayanokouji kun  if it s okay  i d like you to share it with me   well  i was wondering why the explanations are so scattered  i thought maybe the school wanted to avoid the confusion and trouble that would come from explaining things in one large group  but after thinking about it  i don t believe it would take much more effort to announce the rules to everyone at once","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the third-deck cabin he straightens his luggage, puts on his uniform, and wakes Ayanokōji for the evening’s meetings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I’m sorry. Did I wake you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Would you like to come with me? I was thinking the school’s message should be coming pretty soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Did you notice anything, Ayanokouji-kun? If it’s okay, I’d like you to share it with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Already knows the test’s specifics — Yukimura told him over their meal — and several students have come to talk it through with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I was wondering why the explanations are so…scattered. I thought maybe the school wanted to avoid the confusion and trouble that would come from explaining things in one large group, but after thinking about it, I don’t believe it would take much more effort to announce the rules to everyone at once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Plans to ask a teacher directly about the staged briefings.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Wakes him, walks him down, gets only a deflection for his troubles.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> His inside source on the Rabbit rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 2  2 4  absent from the room named only as missing  when ayanokoji wakes in the cabin at 20 30  the narration notes the room s other occupants are gone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as missing: when Ayanokōji wakes in the cabin at 20:30, the narration notes the room’s other occupants are gone.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Neither Yukimura nor Kouenji were in the room.” — absent from the third-deck cabin while Hirata straightens his luggage.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the wet corridor and the signature<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 4  absent from the room named only as missing  when ayanokoji wakes in the cabin  neither he nor koenji is there","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as missing: when Ayanokōji wakes in the cabin, neither he nor Kōenji is there.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Absent from the third-deck cabin at 20:30 — Ayanokōji notes the room holds only himself and Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: from the convenient plan to Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 5  the 20 40 gathering at the second deck meeting place he watches katsuragi confront horikita  kanzaki intercede  ryuen prowl  and kushida arrive puzzled   who are those people   asking hirata to name the waiting students  notes katsuragi s entourage and horikita s changed standing  other classes now see her as  a puppet master  a mastermind who worked behind the scenes  credits horikita s cold shoulder resilience   the island win is his  but she took the spotlight to keep him hidden  expects a huge showdown between katsuragi and ryuen before the test begins  it doesn t come   well then  good luck   leaving hirata at the gathering","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the second-deck meeting place he watches Katsuragi confront Horikita, Kanzaki intercede, Ryūen prowl, and Kushida arrive puzzled.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Who are those people?” (asking Hirata to name the waiting students)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Notes Katsuragi’s entourage and Horikita’s changed standing: other classes now see her as “a puppet master, a mastermind who worked behind the scenes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well then, good luck.” (leaving Hirata at the gathering)<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Burns Morimiya and Tokitō’s names and faces into memory on Hirata’s tip, then keeps to the line without making a fuss.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Credits Horikita’s cold-shoulder resilience — the island win is his, but she took the spotlight to keep him hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Expects a huge showdown between Katsuragi and Ryūen before the test begins; it doesn’t come.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Stands by as Katsuragi threatens her class and Kanzaki pulls him off; impressed she won’t be shaken.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Watches the Class A leader pivot from ignoring Horikita to warning her.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Notes the demented chuckle and the docile lackeys trailing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Present when she wanders into the gathering, puzzled.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0: the 8:00 café and the Ryūen interrupt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 5  the 20 40 gathering second deck meeting place  he names the waiting students for ayanokoji  then stands inside the katsuragi horikita ryuen current   it doesn t seem like all of these people are in my group   that s morimiya kun  from class a  and that one near the elevator is tokitou kun  from class c   the well connected answer   yes  though if i m with you  kanzaki kun  and katsuragi kun  struggle has to be inevitable   answering kanzaki s sympathy   don t worry  no matter who is in my group  i ll do my best   to katsuragi  positive as always","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-deck meeting place: he names the waiting students for Ayanokōji, then stands inside the Katsuragi–Horikita–Ryūen current.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “It doesn’t seem like all of these people are in my group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “That’s Morimiya-kun, from Class A. And that one near the elevator is Tokitou-kun, from Class C.” (the well-connected answer)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yes. Though if I’m with you, Kanzaki-kun, and Katsuragi-kun, struggle has to be inevitable.” (answering Kanzaki’s sympathy)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. No matter who is in my group, I’ll do my best.” (to Katsuragi, positive as always)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Positive through the threat display; Kushida reads his steadiness as the sign that the battle will be grueling.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Addressed as the group’s Class A anchor.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> The Class B boy who spots him landed in trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She finds him amid the gathering and takes his composure for reassurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Both summoned to the same 20:40 meeting — the team Katsuragi named.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster and in the Ichinose comparison<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 2  2 5  the class a pivot on horikita at the 20 40 gathering he singles horikita out of the line  then holds court against her  kanzaki  and ryuen   unless i m mistaken  you re also in the group meeting at 20 40  yes   that s good news  i wanted to speak with you again  i m also in the 20 40 group  starting tomorrow  we will be working together   you re correct  i certainly haven t acknowledged anyone in class d until now  however  considering the incredible results from the last test  it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you  wouldn t you agree  you laid the groundwork to win  and succeeded handsomely   i don t know what the future might hold  but should class d overtake class c  know that class a would attack you without mercy   that s certainly true  however  we must be cautious  it s no laughing matter when those who have been perceived as weak and stupid begin to rise up  if one class manages to change its station  we must be vigilant  i would give the same warning to both classes b and c   however  just because you got lucky and won by complete chance doesn t make us equals   anyone could accomplish something like that out of pure luck  it s better that you don t grow arrogant and behave foolishly after a win that came about by chance  remember that the difference in our class points is still massive   that s a rather deplorable thing to say  especially when academic success is the most important factor in determining our futures  you realize that ja","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Class A pivot on Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–60<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the 20:40 gathering he singles Horikita out of the line, then holds court against her, Kanzaki, and Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “Unless I’m mistaken, you’re also in the group meeting at 20:40, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “That’s good news. I wanted to speak with you again. I’m also in the 20:40 group. Starting tomorrow, we will be working together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “You’re correct. I certainly haven’t acknowledged anyone in Class D until now. However, considering the incredible results from the last test, it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you. Wouldn’t you agree? You…”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re correct. I certainly haven’t acknowledged anyone in Class D until now. However, considering the incredible results from the last test, it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you. Wouldn’t you agree? You laid the groundwork to win, and succeeded handsomely.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what the future might hold, but…should Class D overtake Class C, know that Class A would attack you without mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s certainly true. However, we must be cautious. It’s no laughing matter when those who have been perceived as weak and stupid begin to rise up. If one class manages to change its station, we must be vigilant. I would give the same warning to both Classes B and C.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, just because you got lucky and won by complete chance doesn’t make us equals.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyone could accomplish something like that out of pure luck. It’s better that you don’t grow arrogant and behave foolishly after a win that came about by chance. Remember that the difference in our class points is still massive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a rather deplorable thing to say. Especially when academic success is the most important factor in determining our futures. You realize that Japan is often referred to as an academic society?” (to Ryūen)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t let you bring your awful attitude to this test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, it doesn’t matter. Since we’re in the same group now, we’ll be able to talk at length.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you okay, Hirata? I think this is going to be an especially grueling battle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and collected to a degree that reads as college-age; “most had already acknowledged him as their leader” — the Class A entourage glares on cue.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Dismissive gesture “like he was brushing dirt off his clothes” while calling the island win luck.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The pivot from island-test indifference to a formal Class A threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Brushed off by him, then trading academic-ability arguments with Ryūen in front of him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The “Beauty and the Beast” provocation and the awful-attitude standoff.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Names him the group’s grinding battle ahead.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named as the island strategist and the no-discussion plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 2  2 5  the class b interlude walks quietly past katsuragi s entourage to pull the heat off horikita  then greets hirata s arrival   i don t much like ganging up on people  or threatening other classes   you don t need to waste time on katsuragi  he s just trying to get to you   to horikita  gentlemanly despite not being on good terms with her   hirata  looks like you landed in a troublesome group   oh  i don t think so   when hirata says struggle with him  kanzaki  and katsuragi is inevitable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Class B interlude<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.56–57<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks quietly past Katsuragi’s entourage to pull the heat off Horikita, then greets Hirata’s arrival.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “I don’t much like ganging up on people, or threatening other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “You don’t need to waste time on Katsuragi. He’s just trying to get to you.” (to Horikita, gentlemanly despite not being on good terms with her)<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Hirata, looks like you landed in a troublesome group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, I don’t think so.” (when Hirata says struggle with him, Kanzaki, and Katsuragi is inevitable)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Honest type — long hair without slacker energy; the narration notes Ichinose, Class B’s leader, seems to trust him, and that he faced Horikita once during the summer vacation and knows her intellect.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Rescues her from the gang-up, declined without heat.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Interrupts his threat display; later stands by through the Ryūen exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Reads his group as trouble at a glance.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named as the Class B leader who trusts him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 2  2 5  the walk through provocation arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys  sizes up the pond  and picks a fight with katsuragi   well  well  so many fish in this pond  i ve come to take a look for myself   unfortunately  it looks like i m with you   to katsuragi s question whether he belongs to the meeting   how about you put on a little show for me  what do you think of beauty and the beast   looking at both horikita and katsuragi  then letting out a demented little chuckle   academic ability  how droll  that kind of thing is meaningless   hmm  awful attitude  what in the world are you talking about  i can t possibly imagine  can you perhaps tell me how i am  in fact  awful","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the walk-through provocation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.57–60<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys, sizes up the pond, and picks a fight with Katsuragi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Well, well. So many fish in this pond. I’ve come to take a look for myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Unfortunately, it looks like I’m with you.” (to Katsuragi’s question whether he belongs to the meeting)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “How about you put on a little show for me? What do you think of Beauty and the Beast?” (looking at both Horikita and Katsuragi, then letting out a demented little chuckle)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Academic ability? How droll. That kind of thing is meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm? Awful attitude? What in the world are you talking about? I can’t possibly imagine. Can you perhaps tell me how I am, in fact, awful?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gestured to his crew as if to ask whether Katsuragi’s argument was believable; “their response mechanical.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His three followers wear terrified looks and move docile — “more like a king and his servants.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The academic-society argument ends in a cold stalemate.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She flips her hair and turns her back on him to go inside.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  2 5  the puzzled arrival wanders into the 20 40 gathering without understanding the group structure  then reads the room fast enough to keep up   huh  hirata kun  oh  ayanokouji kun  too  what are you all doing here   hmm  group  i don t understand  i did get an email telling me to come here at this time  wow  there really are some amazing people here  huh   um  well  so  it feels like a lot of really difficult things are about to come our way   ah ha  don t worry  it s okay  like hirata kun said  all i can do is my best  oh  i haven t really had many chances to talk with katsuragi kun and ryuuen kun yet  i d like to get along with you all  too   speaking to everyone present","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.60–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wanders into the 20:40 gathering without understanding the group structure, then reads the room fast enough to keep up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Huh, Hirata-kun? Oh, Ayanokouji-kun, too? What are you all doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Hmm? Group? I don’t understand. I did get an email telling me to come here at this time… Wow, there really are some amazing people here, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Um, well. So, it feels like a lot of really difficult things are about to come our way,”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Somewhat taken back yet respectful of everyone gathered; by fragments of conversation she begins to grasp the situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah ha! Don’t worry, it’s okay! Like Hirata-kun said, all I can do is my best. Oh, I haven’t really had many chances to talk with Katsuragi-kun and Ryuuen-kun yet. I’d like to get along with you all, too.” (speaking to everyone present)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Delivers the last line without anxiety, disgust, displeasure, or joy in her voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes his composure as her anchor.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Names him as someone she hasn’t talked to yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Names him the same way, in the same breath.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Present for her cold exit.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the hallway interrupt and the message compare<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 0  the 8 00 cafe and the ryuen interrupt blue ocean cafe on the ship s deck at 7 55   he meets horikita for the 8 00 vip message  then ryuen and ibuki sit down uninvited and pick at the island result until the coffee is done   i was waiting for an hour   teasing horikita  she arrived before the designated time anyway   i see  this really seems like an inevitable grouping   reading horikita s dragon list   but there s probably a gap between me and the professor  same as you and hirata  there are too many details that don t fit the score theory   i suppose neither of us was chosen  then   yeah  if you re chosen  then you could lead your group to any of the outcomes   there are some things i can t yet see  like how some of the students i don t know will react  i won t know until i meet with them directly  but i thought of a way to lead us to victory   me too  can t wait to see what you do with your group  i answered   answering horikita s wish to see his results   ryuuen  i answered   his answer to who he is most wary of   of course  considering he s only a first year student  he s excellent  if you d asked me who the most excellent student was  then katsuragi would ve been my answer  but if you re asking who i m wary of  then it s ryuuen  by a mile  i answered   i think we were being spied on  him suddenly meeting up with us is too convenient  i said   maybe she was forced to keep an eye on us  or maybe she just happened to see us by chance  if that s the case  it would","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\">Ch.3 §3.0: the 8:00 café and the Ryūen interrupt<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.63–77<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Blue Ocean café on the ship’s deck at 7:55 — he meets Horikita for the 8:00 VIP message, then Ryūen and Ibuki sit down uninvited and pick at the island result until the coffee is done.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I was waiting for an hour.” (teasing Horikita; she arrived before the designated time anyway)<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I see. This really seems like an inevitable grouping,” (reading Horikita’s Dragon list)<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “But there’s probably a gap between me and the Professor, same as you and Hirata. There are too many details that don’t fit the score theory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the Dragon roster as a “dream team” of class representatives — Katsuragi, Kanzaki, Ryuuen — and a death match; notes Kōenji’s abundance would not be contributed.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose neither of us was chosen, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. If you’re chosen, then you could lead your group to any of the outcomes,”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Weighs the VIP’s edge at 500,000 points and calls the school’s “no disadvantages” line a lie — without the VIP in the class the point gap widens.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are some things I can’t yet see, like how some of the students I don’t know will react. I won’t know until I meet with them directly. But I thought of a way to lead us to victory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me too. Can’t wait to see what you do with your group,” I answered. (answering Horikita’s wish to see his results)<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ryuuen,” I answered. (his answer to who he is most wary of)<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Considering he’s only a first-year student, he’s excellent. If you’d asked me who the most excellent student was, then Katsuragi would’ve been my answer. But if you’re asking who I’m wary of, then it’s Ryuuen, by a mile,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Marks Mashima’s earlier “after thorough consideration” phrasing as proof the VIP was chosen by a rule, not a roll.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Silences Horikita with a finger on her lips the moment Ryūen’s shadow appears.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think we were being spied on. Him suddenly meeting up with us is too convenient,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe she was forced to keep an eye on us, or maybe she just happened to see us by chance. If that’s the case, it would help us,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A mistake,” I muttered. (after Ryūen’s “someone just like him” line lands too easily)<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think we’re done for the time being. I’m still sleepy, so I’m going to head back to my room,” I muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Works the whole café as cover: feeds Horikita the strategy he will not show Ryūen, then reads the encounter as a possible leak and files it away.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The morning partner; he teases, trades wary-lists, and parts with her report request.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Faces the man he called his top wary name; knows Ryūen suspects him and that the meeting itself may have given the hint away.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> She is his Rabbit groupmate and, he suspects, Ryūen’s lookout.<span class=\"pg\">p.68, 76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Names him the most excellent first-year, but not the one he fears.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: observing the Rabbit group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou sakayanagi-arisu horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 0  the blue ocean briefing meets ayanokoji at the empty blue ocean cafe an hour early  hands over her memorized dragon group list at 8 00  and holds the table through ryuen s interrupt   you re rather early   that s not my problem  as i ve still arrived before the designated time  besides  how would i know if you d been waiting even ten hours or more   you mean ichinose san being in your group  don t you  i suppose only the class b students know if she s really excellent or not  a leader s qualities and level of excellence aren t necessarily directly proportional  said horikita   from what we can deduce  i wonder if there s a certain method they re using to sort us into the twelve groups  ayanokouji kun  your grades are very similar to karuizawa san s  are they grouping us based on our scores  oh  but yukimura kun has high academic ability  and so does kouenji kun  they re at the top of the class  said horikita   no  we weren t chosen  i m not sure if we should be happy or sad   even so  i don t like how they wrote it  it s like they re saying i m not qualified to be the vip   i look forward to your results  said horikita   for the sake of reference  who are you most wary of  based on how things have been going  i wanted your thoughts  said horikita   that was fast   on his instant  ryuuen   what about katsuragi kun  it s because of him that class a managed to quickly hold down that prime spot on the island  isn t he someone worth watching   i m curious about some thi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\">Ch.3 §3.0: the Blue Ocean briefing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.63–77<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ayanokōji at the empty Blue Ocean café an hour early, hands over her memorized Dragon group list at 8:00, and holds the table through Ryūen’s interrupt.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You’re rather early.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s not my problem, as I’ve still arrived before the designated time. Besides, how would I know if you’d been waiting even ten hours or more?”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You mean Ichinose-san being in your group, don’t you? I suppose only the Class B students know if she’s really excellent or not. A leader’s qualities and level of excellence aren’t necessarily directly proportional,” said…”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>42 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator calls her one of the very few people at this school he could call a friend — and a thorn because she knows something about his hidden life.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands Ayanokōji a slip of paper: the Dragon roster she wrote and memorized, biased “to the point where I can’t imagine it’s a coincidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean Ichinose-san being in your group, don’t you? I suppose only the Class B students know if she’s really excellent or not. A leader’s qualities and level of excellence aren’t necessarily directly proportional,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From what we can deduce, I wonder if there’s a certain method they’re using to sort us into the twelve groups? Ayanokouji-kun, your grades are very similar to Karuizawa-san’s. Are they grouping us based on our scores? Oh, but Yukimura-kun has high academic ability, and so does Kouenji-kun. They’re at the top of the class,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, we weren’t chosen. I’m not sure if we should be happy or sad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, I don’t like how they wrote it. It’s like they’re saying I’m not qualified to be the VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I look forward to your results,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the sake of reference, who are you most wary of? Based on how things have been going, I wanted your thoughts,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was fast.” (on his instant “Ryuuen”)<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about Katsuragi-kun? It’s because of him that Class A managed to quickly hold down that prime spot on the island. Isn’t he someone worth watching?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m curious about some things concerning the VIP’s identity. Even after reading the message and thinking about it, did you notice any unnatural-sounding phrases in the school’s email? And the strict—” Horikita said. (cut off by Ayanokōji’s finger)<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve warned you not to call me by my first name, Ryuuen-kun. Also, considering you were a turncoat who only pretended to be our friend, it’s odd you’d show your face, Ibuki-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As if I would tell you. Perhaps you’d like to tell us about your message?” Horikita responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have nothing to tell you,” Horikita responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Regrettably, I must decline your offer. Violent actions are considered a violation of the test rules. If you do happen to strike me, I will not hesitate to report it to the school. At any rate, please feel free to do whatever you please,” she said flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since we’re all together, how about we have some coffee? It seems a good time to enjoy a nice cup,” Horikita offered.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration credits her acting: she never shakes, and probably does not think of it as acting.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s understandable. He couldn’t have guessed that someone from Class D would do so well. Isn’t that why you and Ibuki-san are here? You came to check on me. Am I wrong?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course,” Horikita answered, sipping her coffee. She seemed at ease, which was unusual.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Think whatever you like. Though I wonder…how did you figure out my strategy? You only saw the results of the test. How do you know the way in which points were gained and lost? Those details are supposed to be unknown,” countered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think that was hard to deduce? Any idiot could have figured that out if they thought about it for a minute. Even Katsuragi-kun, who you’ve been making fun of,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it possible that I’d simply taken the proper precautions? Preparing for the unknown is absolutely basic logic. The moment Ibuki-san met Class D, I took all possibilities into account. You were so confident, but your argument ended up being flimsy. You’ve said nothing surprising,” responded Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m afraid I can’t understand you at all. I have no close friends. The closest I have would be Ayanokouji-kun here, and he’s always dragging me down. I’d be hard-pressed to say that he’s working with me. Sad, but true,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Draws fire onto Ayanokōji to make him look useless — “Well done,” the narration says — while denying the second-leader theory.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, if we did change leaders, he wouldn’t be the most likely candidate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’m sorry, but what you’re saying is complete nonsense. … Does it embarrass you that a girl managed to see through your … schemes?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.73-74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My goodness, that was rather thoughtful,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It sounds like you really want to believe that we have a secret weapon in our class,” observed Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snaps when Ryūen photographs her without permission: “Don’t take my photo without permission!”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, isn’t that a good thing? I don’t particularly care. Besides, if you just arbitrarily jump to conclusions, why bother badgering me to confirm them?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me ask you something. I know it hurts that I saw through you, but why are you so fixated on me? Aren’t you concerned about anyone else? Like Ichinose-san, or Katsuragi-kun? Going by the rumors, there’s someone named Sakayanagi, too. Shouldn’t the people in the classes above C be your concern? You should be able to at least answer that, I think,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not really. It’s just that I hate your sarcastic way of speaking. I’ve always aimed to reach Class A, so I assumed I’d be attracting a lot of attention,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? I think he just doesn’t like that I found him out, and wanted to trick me into revealing the truth. I can’t imagine he narrowed down the list of potential candidates to you. Besides, even if he knew your identity, you’d be the only one in trouble,” replied Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re overthinking things. No one thinks you’re involved. Despite what he said, he thinks you’re an ordinary person, considering your lackluster achievements in the first semester,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Discussion is likely useless from here on out. We’ll go our separate ways. Anyway, excellent work. If you make any progress, give me a report.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The morning partner; hands him the list, takes his wary-name, and closes with a standing report request.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The full confrontation — first name, spy, island result, photo — and she never leaves the seat until he does.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Names the turncoat, declines the rematch on rules, and offers her coffee.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The dream-team anchor, the worth-watching rival, and the man Ryūen says still credits her with the island win.<span class=\"pg\">p.64, 67, 70, 72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Dragon groupmate named on her list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Dragon groupmate named on her list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The rumoured name she throws at Ryūen to break his focus.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the confused-call message<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 3  named on the dragon roster and in the ichinose comparison roster line only in the cafe half  p 84 he appears as a comparison point inside the rabbit room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster and in the Ichinose comparison<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64, p.84<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Roster line only in the café half; p.84 he appears as a comparison point inside the Rabbit room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Dragon groupmate with Kushida — “both excellent students, and representatives of our class”; with Horikita they are the strongest hand Class D could deal.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose’s persuasion is contrasted with his and Kushida’s: even they “might find themselves outmatched, despite their overabundance of friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the biased list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The other Class D name on the Dragon roster.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named in her praise as a floor under her people-work.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5: the trusted conduit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 3  named on the dragon roster one roster line   class b s dragon seat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One roster line — Class B’s Dragon seat.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed among Horikita’s Dragon group (Class B: Andou, Kanzaki, Tsube); Ayanokōji flags him as one of the class representatives that makes the list a dream team.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the biased list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the Class B interlude<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p143-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the Dragon deadlock<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru machida-kouji ichinose-honami katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 3  named as the island strategist and the no discussion plan never in the room this half   he anchors horikita s dragon list  ryuen s cafe autopsy  and the whole rabbit debate as the man whose fairness strategy machida speaks for","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: named as the island strategist and the no-discussion plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64–67, p.70–76, p.85–88<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Never in the room this half — he anchors Horikita’s Dragon list, Ryūen’s café autopsy, and the whole Rabbit debate as the man whose fairness strategy Machida speaks for.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> First name on Horikita’s Dragon roster — Class A, with Nishikawa, Matoba and Yano.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Ayanokōji’s answer to “who are you most wary of”: Katsuragi is the most excellent first-year, Ryuuen the one he fears — “by a mile.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ryūen reports Katsuragi was “rather cautious” of Horikita after the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Still thinks Horikita planned the whole island win; Ryūen says Katsuragi “probably didn’t know” the points flow and that Katsuragi “thinks you planned the whole thing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ryūen: “Neither Katsuragi nor Ichinose is my enemy. If I wanted to crush them, I could do it any time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The Rabbit room learns his proposal by name through Machida: don’t discuss at all, let the test pass calmly, equal points for every class.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The fairness argument Machida voices — VIPs distributed evenly because the school hates unfairness, island proof — is attributed to Katsuragi’s read of the test’s “trick.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Narration: his plan is the ultimate defensive move; if a VIP is in Class A, finding them becomes exceptionally difficult.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate, worth-watching rival, and the island winner he still misreads.<span class=\"pg\">p.64, 67, 70, 72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The café theme — Ryūen quotes his caution and his wrong leader call.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Named as the author of the no-discussion strategy.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The opponent who names and dismantles the plan in his absence.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the Class A pivot on Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the calm image and the surprise reaction<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 3  the grade theory name check two mentions in the cafe grade discussion   abundance without contribution  then top of class scores","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64–65<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two mentions in the café grade discussion — abundance without contribution, then top-of-class scores.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji: “In terms of latent ability, Kouenji had an abundance, but he probably wouldn’t contribute any of it to the team. I didn’t know what group he was in.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita’s score theory: “Yukimura-kun has high academic ability, and so does Kouenji-kun. They’re at the top of the class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The narrator who doubts he would ever help a team.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Named in her grouping hypothesis.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5: push-ups, refusal, and the Monkey exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 3  named on the dragon roster one roster line in horikita s hand   class d s other two dragon members with her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One roster line in Horikita’s hand — Class D’s other two Dragon members with her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed with Hirata Yousuke as the Class D pair; Ayanokōji calls them “both excellent students, and representatives of our class” and the strongest hand Class D could deal.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the biased list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the same line.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5–§3.6: the VIP name and the starlit hug<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 3  the phrasing he still hears one backward glance at her briefing inside ayanokoji s vip message reading","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1\">Ch.3: the phrasing he still hears<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One backward glance at her briefing inside Ayanokōji’s VIP-message reading.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> “Mashima-sensei had said something to the same effect. The VIP had been chosen based on certain considerations. There was something about the chosen that set them apart.” — Ayanokōji folds Mashima’s words into the email’s “After thorough consideration.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His reading of the VIP rule still runs on her briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the handout and the four outcomes<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p121-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.6: the teachers’ sofa<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  3 0 3 1  the cafe shadow and the rabbit holdout walks into blue ocean at ryuen s side as the island spy horikita caught  later sits silent through the whole rabbit first discussion until ichinose calls her name   i m not so stupid that i d let someone like her see through me  things were simply more difficult because of my fever   on losing to horikita   in that case  let s have a rematch  she challenged   so what about sakayanagi  ibuki asked that  not horikita  she wanted to confirm that information herself  apparently   whatever  i don t really have anything to add  said ibuki","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">Ch.3 §3.0–§3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.68–75, p.88<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks into Blue Ocean at Ryūen’s side as the island spy Horikita caught; later sits silent through the whole Rabbit first discussion until Ichinose calls her name.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “I’m not so stupid that I’d let someone like her see through me. Things were simply more difficult because of my fever.” (on losing to Horikita)<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “In that case, let’s have a rematch,” she challenged.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “So what about Sakayanagi?” Ibuki asked that, not Horikita. She wanted to confirm that information herself, apparently.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Closes the distance on Horikita ready to lunge, then stops — rules, and Ryūen’s leash, hold her back; “Tch!”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Clearly detests working beneath Ryūen, yet is exceptionally talented — the precise reason he chose her as the Class D spy.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The one question she puts to Ryūen all morning; he goes silent before answering.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sits “a little further away, as if isolating themselves” in the Rabbit circle — same posture as Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ayanokōji expected a fight with Karuizawa over the stolen underwear; Ibuki shows no tiredness and no revenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whatever. I don’t really have anything to add,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sole Class C holdout on the Katsuragi no-discussion vote — arms crossed since the test began, she does not move and does not speak until called; the others take it as her normal way.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His lackey on the reconnaissance walk; she detests the leash but keeps it.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The spy she failed against; rematch refused on rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The girl whose underwear she stole on the island — they share the Rabbit room without speaking.<span class=\"pg\">p.80, 88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Answers only when Ichinose asks her by name.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention as the culprit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 3  3 0  the cafe provocation walks into blue ocean with ibuki mid horikita briefing  straddles a vacant seat  and spends the coffee working the island result until he leaves with his lackey   nice weather  eh suzune  you having breakfast with this clingy beta male   you should have received the message already  what were the results  were you chosen as the vip   i suppose you wouldn t give anything away  but that doesn t matter  according to my information  there s no way that your farcical bumbling on the island should ve led to victory  said ryuuen   yesterday  it seemed katsuragi was rather cautious of you  he said   heh  well  i won t deny that  i came here to measure your abilities for myself  he answered   katsuragi and i think differently  when i m dealing with someone  i like to keep an eye on them   i m remembering the test on the island  the result  the process that led to it  there are only certain types of people who would ve been able to conceptualize and execute a plan like that  a girl like you is far too serious minded to have come up with it  reasoned ryuuen   katsuragi probably didn t know   his read on who grasped the points flow   at the end of the test  i wrote down your name as leader  but that was wrong  there s just one reason why that was wrong  your class leader changed right before the test ended  the only explanation  mused ryuuen   ah  however  katsuragi thinks you planned the whole thing  but was that really the case  in my opinion  you becomi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.68–75<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks into Blue Ocean with Ibuki mid-Horikita-briefing, straddles a vacant seat, and spends the coffee working the island result until he leaves with his lackey.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Nice weather, eh Suzune? You having breakfast with this clingy beta male?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “You should have received the message already. What were the results? Were you chosen as the VIP?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I suppose you wouldn’t give anything away, but that doesn’t matter. According to my information, there’s no way that your farcical bumbling on the island should’ve led to victory,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yesterday, it seemed Katsuragi was rather cautious of you,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh. Well, I won’t deny that. I came here to measure your abilities for myself,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi and I think differently. When I’m dealing with someone, I like to keep an eye on them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m remembering the test on the island. The result. The process that led to it. There are only certain types of people who would’ve been able to conceptualize and execute a plan like that. A girl like you is far too serious-minded to have come up with it,” reasoned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi probably didn’t know.” (his read on who grasped the points flow)<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At the end of the test, I wrote down your name as leader, but that was wrong. There’s just one reason why that was wrong: Your class leader changed right before the test ended. The only explanation,” mused Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. However, Katsuragi thinks you planned the whole thing. But was that really the case? In my opinion, you becoming the leader and then retiring were both unexpected. Besides, I had my own strategy in place. I had Ibuki infiltrate your class to find out the leader’s identity. You did nothing to counter that strategy at first,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The key question is who replaced you as leader. Personally, I think the second leader was pulling your strings from behind the scenes during the entire test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Speaks to Horikita but watches Ayanokōji the whole time — “If I appeared shaken for even an instant, he’d pounce.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose that’s expected of a clingy tagalong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That guy with you is considerably smart. Despite that, he hasn’t achieved anything significant, or gotten high grades. He has some excellent qualities, though I have my doubts,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see your point. I never imagined you’d trip me up. I’ll admit it. The results of the test shocked me,” answered Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s too bad. I love surprise attacks, foul play, and subterfuge. That level of strategy was totally unexpected, but your victory high will soon come to an end. Whether it’s you, Suzune, or someone pulling the strings behind the scenes, you’re stupid. You’ve already made your best move. Class D is one or two steps behind the other classes in points. The challenge will only heat up from here. You already played your trump card during the survival test, when the game was just getting started. You couldn’t see what was in front of or behind you. I don’t think you’ll find this round as easy as last time. Tell that to whoever helped you ace the test,” warned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What can I say? I’m quite merciful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snaps a photo of Horikita without asking, studies the sour expression, and pockets the phone satisfied.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone in Class D other than you is quite clever. There’s no mistake about that,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A conversation reveals many subtle things. I’m glad I could talk with you, Suzune. It’s a game to me. I’ll discover who among you is making moves behind the scenes. Everyone, including your clingy friend here, is a target,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I already know their abilities, to some extent. Neither Katsuragi nor Ichinose is my enemy. If I wanted to crush them, I could do it any time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m saving her for the final course. It’d be a waste to eat her now. Let’s go, Ibuki.” Ryuuen stood and left with his lackey. (on Sakayanagi)<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The whole visit is reconnaissance: measure Horikita, float the hidden-second-leader theory, and leave without confirming anything — narration says he only wanted to chat and pass the time amusing himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The target of the visit; he needles her, photographs her, and walks off still doubting her.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Brings her as the visible lackey and cuts her off when she would snap back.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sizes him up as smart-but-inert and keeps him in the target set without ever addressing him directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.68, 73–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The rival whose caution and island read he quotes back at Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.70, 72, 75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Saved “for the final course” — he will not spend her now.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the walk-through provocation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p75-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu","q":"ch 3  the rumoured name in the cafe twice named in the ryuen horikita coffee  never present   so what about sakayanagi  ibuki asked that  not horikita  she wanted to confirm that information herself  apparently   the question is ibuki s  recorded here because the answer is about arisu   i m saving her for the final course  it d be a waste to eat her now  let s go  ibuki  ryuuen stood and left with his lackey","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html#sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p75-1\">Ch.3: the rumoured name in the café<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.75<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Twice named in the Ryūen–Horikita coffee, never present.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “So what about Sakayanagi?” Ibuki asked that, not Horikita. She wanted to confirm that information herself, apparently. (the question is Ibuki’s; recorded here because the answer is about Arisu)<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “I’m saving her for the final course. It’d be a waste to eat her now. Let’s go, Ibuki.” Ryuuen stood and left with his lackey.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Horikita’s setup: “Going by the rumors, there’s someone named Sakayanagi, too. Shouldn’t the people in the classes above C be your concern?” — Ryūen’s focus is called downright obsessive until this name breaks it.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The man who will not spend her yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The one who puts the rumoured name in the air.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p158-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the absent faction leader<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami machida-kouji hamaguchi-tetsuya manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 1  observing the rabbit group meets yukimura and the professor outside the rabbit room  then sits through the first group discussion as ichinose and machida trade katsuragi s no discussion plan   no  i don t have a favorite speech pattern or anything  not especially  anyway  i answered   to the professor s moe dialect question   well  professor  what about you  do you have a speech pattern you like  i asked   it s nothing  i said   on why karuizawa and ibuki sit apart   he expected a fight over the stolen underwear   i agree  too  we re a group  like you said  and we could all use some private points  if it s possible  i d like us to work together  what do you say  professor   i mean  the strategy s fine  besides  i think most people here agree  and i ve never been good at talking  i answered","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: observing the Rabbit group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.78–93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Yukimura and the Professor outside the Rabbit room, then sits through the first group discussion as Ichinose and Machida trade Katsuragi’s no-discussion plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “No, I don’t have a favorite speech pattern or anything. Not especially, anyway,” I answered. (to the Professor’s moe-dialect question)<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, Professor, what about you? Do you have a speech pattern you like?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s nothing,” I said. (on why Karuizawa and Ibuki sit apart — he expected a fight over the stolen underwear)<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Follows the Professor’s dialect ranking as a way to kill time before the room fills.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the eleven-person circle, the class clusters, and that Karuizawa and Ibuki isolate themselves; recognizes the Class A boy who once offered him a deal to betray Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Jumps into the opening vote to bind the Professor on camera: “What do you say, Professor?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I agree, too. We’re a group, like you said, and we could all use some private points. If it’s possible, I’d like us to work together. What do you say, Professor?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Ichinose’s “assume that no one here is the VIP” as a narrowing question and clocks the answer order — Ichinose, Karuizawa, Yukimura, Manabe, Hamaguchi — as the first suspect list.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I mean, the strategy’s fine. Besides, I think most people here agree, and I’ve never been good at talking,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Publicly backs Katsuragi’s plan while privately sure it is hiding something; lays low for the rest of the session.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judges the room’s low-communication types as reactive and refuses to get impatient.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Watches her take the lead, tests her with the Professor, and is last in her roll call.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Sits through the Class A pitch and the silent withdrawal.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Notes the Class B counter that holds the middle of the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Present when she turns on Karuizawa with the Rika charge.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Shares the room with her; sees her vote, her bluntness, and the phone slap that ends the half.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Walks in with him; tracks his swing from the convenient plan to Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 86–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The dialect small-talk partner outside, then the vote he drags the Professor into.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0: the 8:00 café and the Ryūen interrupt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the first discussion breaks up<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko machida-kouji manabe-shiho sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 3  3 1  the professor in rabbit meets ayanokoji and yukimura outside the rabbit room full from three heavy lunches  then sits through the first discussion as the otaku who votes the convenient way   sorry to keep you waiting  urrp  urp  if you eat three heavy meals for lunch  you ll naturally have a full belly  i considered going on a diet  but it seemed futile  said the professor   if you re not at full strength  there ll be trouble  it s like choosing a higher difficulty setting in a video game  wouldn t you say  the professor responded   oh ho  hmm  dost thou not care for my linguistic idiosyncrasies  well then  yukimura dono  what wouldst thou like  the professor seemed like he wanted to antagonize yukimura   from now on  i shall be like the protagonist who appears weak  but secretly has massive strength  i normally have no motivation  but i ll become a completely op cheater with enough power to destroy the entire world  i mean  i m just following the current trends  the professor mused   ayanokouji  there s something i wish to ask you  please give me a straight answer  said the professor   i ve considered what kind of speech patterns you might like  of course  a pleasant dialect that a cute heroine character uses would be good  said the professor   have you perhaps encountered a speech pattern that felt moe  the professor asked   of course  i ll rank them  in third place would be  even if you say so  kudo  that s the old stand by  the kansai ben  it tends to give a so","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the Professor in Rabbit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.78–88<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ayanokōji and Yukimura outside the Rabbit room full from three heavy lunches, then sits through the first discussion as the otaku who votes the convenient way.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Sorry to keep you waiting! Urrp! Urp! If you eat three heavy meals for lunch, you’ll naturally have a full belly. I considered going on a diet, but it seemed futile,” said the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “If you’re not at full strength, there’ll be trouble. It’s like choosing a higher difficulty setting in a video game, wouldn’t you say?” the Professor responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Oh ho! Hmm, dost thou not care for my linguistic idiosyncrasies? Well then, Yukimura-dono, what wouldst thou like?” The Professor seemed like he wanted to antagonize Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From now on, I shall be like the protagonist who appears weak, but secretly has massive strength. I normally have no motivation, but I’ll become a completely OP cheater with enough power to destroy the entire world. I mean, I’m just following the current trends!” the Professor mused.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji. There’s something I wish to ask you. Please give me a straight answer,” said the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve considered what kind of speech patterns you might like. Of course, a pleasant dialect that a cute heroine character uses would be good,” said the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Have you perhaps encountered a speech pattern that felt moe?” the Professor asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. I’ll rank them. In third place would be ‘Even if you say so, Kudo!’ That’s the old stand-by, the Kansai-ben! It tends to give a somewhat tough or crude impression, but it’s the obvious choice. It’s an essential dialect. In second place is the beautiful girl from a snowy country, the Hokkaido-ben! When they say, ‘Oh, sorry for the trouble, thanks,’ and stuff like that, it just makes me swoon! Those unique phrases are so moe they make me want to die! It also gets points because it’s not used very widely in the 2D world!” exclaimed the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Dourururururururu… Coming in first place, jumping from little girls to the older sister, the universal Hakata-ben! … Those are the best three by far!” the Professor shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.79-80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The dialect ranking is pure2D fandom; Ayanokōji understands almost none of it and only kills time listening.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’ll cooperate. I want points,” he answered. (Ayanokōji’s call-on; narration notes the mysterious-character tone is new)<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t Class A’s strategy fine, though? I cannot say that I can find any problems with it. Once the exam ends, the classes can talk amongst themselves and share the points,” said the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Has slipped back to his normal nerdy tone; his line seeds the Class C hand votes.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Raises his hand early for the no-discussion plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The hallway dialect partner, then the student he answers on cue.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Antagonises him with the faux-archaic bit until Yukimura storms off.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Votes with the Class A pitch he praises.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> His sentiment “spread to Class C” and she agrees next.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor’s interjections<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: hunger and the Sunrise gag<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"machida-kouji ichinose-honami sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 3  3 1  from the convenient plan to ichinose storms off the professor s dialect bit  briefs the room hard  then swings through the rabbit discussion   convenient plan first  ichinose s downside last   stop talking like that  it s weird  said yukimura   whatever  i don t care  just talk normal   the time for screwing around ended yesterday  from here on out  we need to fight for ourselves and for our classes  yukimura directed that statement toward the professor  but i nodded in acknowledgement   there won t be any negatives  you mean   prompted by machida s four outcomes walk   a hidden downside  what in the world could that be  asked yukimura  sounding flustered  it didn t seem he d considered that point yet   i agree  we can t allow class a to keep securing the lead  added yukimura   i can t trust you  muttered yukimura   rejecting ichinose s alliance offer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: from the convenient plan to Ichinose<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.78–92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Storms off the Professor’s dialect bit, briefs the room hard, then swings through the Rabbit discussion — convenient plan first, Ichinose’s downside last.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Stop talking like that. It’s weird,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Whatever, I don’t care. Just talk normal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “The time for screwing around ended yesterday. From here on out, we need to fight for ourselves and for our classes.” Yukimura directed that statement toward the Professor, but I nodded in acknowledgement.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Storms away from the Professor’s faux-archaic provocation; the other two hurry after him.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There won’t be any negatives, you mean?” (prompted by Machida’s four-outcomes walk)<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A hidden downside? What in the world could that be?” asked Yukimura, sounding flustered. It didn’t seem he’d considered that point yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Face visibly stiffens when Ichinose shows the Class A always-proposes-this pattern — “like he wondered how he could have missed such a simple thing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I agree. We can’t allow Class A to keep securing the lead,” added Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t trust you,” muttered Yukimura. (rejecting Ichinose’s alliance offer)<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The swing of the half: votes with the convenient Class A plan, flinches at the hidden downside, then refuses Ichinose anyway — he wanted to avoid Class D getting the short end and could not commit to trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> First the Class A plan’s beneficiary, then its questioner.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Flips to her side on the class-gap point, then rejects her alliance on trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The dialect sparring partner; they walk into Rabbit together.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Hallway companion; one of the names Machida uses to teach the outcomes.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.5: strategy talk and the Kouenji explosion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho ibuki-mio ichinose-honami machida-kouji karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 3  3 1  the rabbit votes and manabe s phone enters the rabbit room with ayanokoji s party  isolates herself beside ibuki  votes bluntly through the strategy debate  and ends the half by knocking manabe s phone out of her hand   what the heck are you talking about  isn t that obvious  snapped karuizawa   umm  the outcome where someone figures out the vip s identity and then betrays the group  she said   answering machida s which outcome to avoid   i  to be completely honest  i m annoyed  even though you say we ll get points  whether i get any points is a separate issue  but we may get points even if we do have a discussion  i don t want to waste time fighting over what we re doing  i just want this test to be over so we can have fun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the Rabbit votes and Manabe’s phone<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.80–93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Enters the Rabbit room with Ayanokōji’s party, isolates herself beside Ibuki, votes bluntly through the strategy debate, and ends the half by knocking Manabe’s phone out of her hand.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “What the heck are you talking about? Isn’t that obvious?” snapped Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Umm. The outcome where someone figures out the VIP’s identity and then betrays the group?” she said. (answering Machida’s which-outcome-to-avoid)<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I… To be completely honest, I’m annoyed. Even though you say we’ll get points, whether I get any points is a separate issue. But we may get points even if we do have a discussion… I don’t want to waste time fighting over what…”<span class=\"pg\">p.88–89<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line “Ugh. No matter how you look at it, we really do have the worst team.” sits immediately before “Karuizawa entered the room” with no speaker tag — the translation leaves it unassigned; her entrance follows on the same page.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Casts her eyes away on entry and sits “a little further away, as if isolating themselves”; Ayanokōji expected the Ibuki underwear fight and gets none.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her bluntness accidentally builds the room’s hierarchy — the dam bursts and Yukimura, Manabe, then Hamaguchi pile on.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I… To be completely honest, I’m annoyed. Even though you say we’ll get points, whether I get any points is a separate issue. But we may get points even if we do have a discussion… I don’t want to waste time fighting over what we’re doing. I just want this test to be over so we can have fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The other students are astonished by the honesty; she wants the test over so they can have fun, not points talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Looks up from her phone when Manabe opens with the Rika charge, denies knowing any Rika, then knocks the camera-phone out of Manabe’s hands — more force than she meant.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The Class C girl who brings the summer café bullying story to her face.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Sits apart from the same girl she wronged on the island; neither starts it.<span class=\"pg\">p.80, 88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> First loud yes to Outcome #1, then the honest non-answer Ichinose has to work around.<span class=\"pg\">p.82, 88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Answers his outcomes walk, then is named in his Class A vote count.<span class=\"pg\">p.86, 89<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the interrupter, the werewolf, the phone call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the phone fight resolves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"machida-kouji hamaguchi-tetsuya katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami","q":"ch 3  3 1  taking the lead in rabbit stands into the awkward first discussion  runs introductions over machida s objection  then leads the room against katsuragi s no discussion plan   your attention  please  i don t know most of you  but i think we ought to introduce ourselves  after all  there are probably people here who haven t met before  she said   well  if that s how you feel  machida kun  i can t force you to do anything  however  a microphone might have been installed somewhere in the room to record everything we re saying  don t you think  if that s true  it may not be an issue for just the people who don t introduce themselves  the entire group might end up shouldering the blame  warned ichinose   hey there  ayanokouji kun  looks like we re in the same group  i m looking forward to working with you  said ichinose   now that we ve finished  how do you think we should proceed  please tell me if anyone disagrees with my taking the lead  said ichinose   well  since it looks like no one especially wants the spot  i ll take the lead  to begin with  i think if there s any point that people don t understand or are worried about  we should all discuss it  if we don t  the situation will get worse over time  does anyone have any questions   there s something i d like to talk to you all about  i d like you all to assume that no one here is the vip  and i d like for us all to work together and clear this exam  in other words  i want to know if you think our best option is to p","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: taking the lead in Rabbit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.81–92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands into the awkward first discussion, runs introductions over Machida’s objection, then leads the room against Katsuragi’s no-discussion plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Your attention, please! I don’t know most of you, but I think we ought to introduce ourselves. After all, there are probably people here who haven’t met before,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Well, if that’s how you feel, Machida-kun, I can’t force you to do anything. However, a microphone might have been installed somewhere in the room to record everything we’re saying, don’t you think? If that’s true, it may not be…”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Hey there, Ayanokouji-kun. Looks like we’re in the same group! I’m looking forward to working with you,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>36 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Immediately volunteers as leader — the narration says it wasn’t easy to pull a group together, “but Ichinose didn’t seem to dislike her role. If anything, she seemed to be having fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, if that’s how you feel, Machida-kun, I can’t force you to do anything. However, a microphone might have been installed somewhere in the room to record everything we’re saying, don’t you think? If that’s true, it may not be an issue for just the people who don’t introduce themselves. The entire group might end up shouldering the blame,” warned Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now that we’ve finished, how do you think we should proceed? Please tell me if anyone disagrees with my taking the lead,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, since it looks like no one especially wants the spot, I’ll take the lead. To begin with, I think if there’s any point that people don’t understand or are worried about, we should all discuss it. If we don’t, the situation will get worse over time. Does anyone have any questions?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s something I’d like to talk to you all about. I’d like you all to assume that no one here is the VIP, and I’d like for us all to work together and clear this exam. In other words, I want to know if you think our best option is to pursue Outcome #1,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The opening question doubles as a trap: whoever agrees loudly is not the VIP, and the narration clocks her, Karuizawa, Yukimura, Manabe, then Hamaguchi as the first answer order.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe that question was too harsh?” mused Ichinose. She smiled bitterly.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d rather not do this, but think of it this way. Sometimes we may need to make decisions based on a majority vote. People will most certainly be suspicious of those who don’t want to answer the questions, and the group might turn against them. What do you say to that?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please don’t misunderstand me. I just want to talk. You may answer however you please, but I want everyone to step up to the plate in this test. In other words, I want you to participate,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration contrasts her with Horikita: same logic, but Ichinose can bring people together — tactical action with the group’s approval; not even Katsuragi or Ryūen match it, maybe not even Hirata and Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is there another way, then?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you mind enlightening us?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi-kun? I see,” said Ichinose. (the instant she hears the name she understands the pitch)<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose so. It’s not a bad thing if the school is the only loser,” replied Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, it’s going to be unexpectedly difficult. It might even be more difficult than solving the test through discussion. If you don’t doubt your partner, you won’t betray him or her. All the first-year students would have to adhere to that. Because the school guarantees the VIP’s anonymity, you’re asking for trust amongst your classmates. It’d be great if the VIP stepped forward and the points were shared equally with the class, but couldn’t the VIP just monopolize all of those points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. So, do we agree it’s as Machida-kun says? Each individual class can deal with the problem after the test has ended?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like everyone’s opinions. Would that be all right? First, those who agree with the plan, please raise your hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. Lastly, we have one more person to ask.” Ichinose turned to me. “What do you think, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Machida-kun. Katsuragi-kun’s strategy certainly isn’t bad. With it, there’s no need to doubt, lie to, or hurt anyone. In the end, we’d receive an equal number of points. I understand the reason why many would follow this plan. However, I want you to consider something carefully. I can’t think of any downsides to this strategy, but wouldn’t you say that being in Class A allows you to propose such a strategy? There may be downsides we don’t see yet,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration compares her to a submarine that surfaces without a splash — the comeback is swift and incredible.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we assume that the classes all have an equal number of VIPs, … However, wouldn’t it be unfair to the lower level classes to make them throw … away this chance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.89-90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We don’t know how many special tests we’ll have before graduation, and the difference between Class A and the rest is remarkably clear. Class A also proposed the extreme idea of aligning all the classes back on the island. If Class A continues to recommend this strategy every time we have a test, our class positions will never change,” Ichinose continued.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t just throw away a precious opportunity. Not even if your strategy yields solid results,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You said this wouldn’t narrow the gap between classes, but that’s not correct. There are four students from Class D, and four from Class C in our group. There are three from B and three from A. In other words, if we clear the test with the first outcome, it’s possible for the lower classes to close the gap between themselves and the higher classes, wouldn’t you agree?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we don’t follow my strategy, we let Class A lead unopposed. … happened to be in Class A,” responded Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.90-91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now then, what should we do?” Ichinose faced the other three classes, who were still sitting around in a circle. “I wanted to avoid excluding anyone, but there’s nothing we can do if that’s your class policy. If you want to participate, just let me know,” she said gently.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. If Rabbit’s VIP is in Class A, trying to narrow down the list of suspects won’t be easy. But in terms of sheer probability, there’s a three in four chance that the VIP’s in one of the other classes. Besides, even if we don’t know who the VIP is, if we at least know where that person is, we’ll have some options. Right?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think it’s necessary for us to think that far ahead. Let’s just start by finding out which class the VIP is in,” replied Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is just a spur-of-the-moment idea. If we work together, we’ll come up with even better ideas later. The test’s only just begun. I think it might be better to wait a bit and take our time before deciding whose plan we’ll move forward with,” Ichinose added.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her real aim is not the VIP name but the VIP’s class — narrow which class first, keep the lower classes’ chance to close the gap, and leave the door open for a later alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The debate partner: introductions, the no-discussion pitch, the silent Class A withdrawal.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Her Class B lieutenant — “We leave everything to you, Ichinose-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Names and dismantles his strategy without him in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Greets him by name, then calls on him last in the vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.81, 89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Pulls him toward the downside argument, then takes his trust refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Works around her bluntness and her honest non-answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.82, 88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.2: named on the Rabbit roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: bystander, closer, and the Machida bait<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p81-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hamaguchi-tetsuya katsuragi-kouhei karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko machida-kouji","q":"ch 3  3 1  the class a no discussion pitch opens the rabbit discussion by objecting to introductions  then fronts katsuragi s  don t talk  strategy until class a withdraws to the corner of the room   is it really necessary to introduce ourselves  though  i don t think the school seriously meant that  i think it s fine if only the people who want to introduce themselves do it  right   ichinose  that question was unfair  wouldn t you say  if you say something like   assume that no one here s the vip  aren t you subtly calling the vip a villain  besides  no normal person would announce that they re going to betray anyone   that s most certainly true  in that case  i think all of us from class a will remain silent  machida crossed his arms  the other two people from class a seemed to share his attitude   nothing to offer  that s not the case at all  said machida   will this test really be settled through discussion  though  will you really discover the vip through talking  or are you going to bow your head and ask the vip to help you   there is  there s a way to clear this test easily  and come out on top  machida replied without the slightest hesitation or anxiety   of course  as a group  we ought to share valuable information  said machida   his fake altruism  per the narration   i recommend that we don t discuss things at all  he said  speaking loudly enough for everyone to hear   yes  the shortcut to victory is to avoid extraneous discussion  replied machida   it doesn t matt","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p81-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html#sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p81-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the Class A no-discussion pitch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.81–91<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Opens the Rabbit discussion by objecting to introductions, then fronts Katsuragi’s “don’t talk” strategy until Class A withdraws to the corner of the room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “Is it really necessary to introduce ourselves, though? I don’t think the school seriously meant that. I think it’s fine if only the people who want to introduce themselves do it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “Ichinose, that question was unfair, wouldn’t you say? If you say something like, ‘assume that no one here’s the VIP,’ aren’t you subtly calling the VIP a villain? Besides, no normal person would announce that they’re going to…”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “That’s most certainly true. In that case, I think all of us from Class A will remain silent.” Machida crossed his arms. The other two people from Class A seemed to share his attitude.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ichinose, that question was unfair, wouldn’t you say? If you say something like, ‘assume that no one here’s the VIP,’ aren’t you subtly calling the VIP a villain? Besides, no normal person would announce that they’re going to betray anyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing to offer? That’s not the case at all,” said Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will this test really be settled through discussion, though? Will you really discover the VIP through talking? Or are you going to bow your head and ask the VIP to help you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration senses someone else behind Machida pulling the strings — Class A’s policy is already decided and he is not the power in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is. There’s a way to clear this test easily, and come out on top,” Machida replied without the slightest hesitation or anxiety.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. As a group, we ought to share valuable information,” said Machida. (his fake altruism, per the narration)<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I recommend that we don’t discuss things at all,” he said, speaking loudly enough for everyone to hear.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. The shortcut to victory is to avoid extraneous discussion,” replied Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t matter what class the VIP is in. You can most definitely win if you don’t talk. That was Katsuragi-san’s proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are only four possible outcomes. You all should know what those are. Consider. Which outcome do you think we should absolutely avoid?” asked Machida. He turned toward Karuizawa, as if choosing her to answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. If a traitor emerges, that will be our downfall. Whether the traitor discovers the person or not, we lose. But what if we flip things around?” asked Machida. This time, he looked to Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. There are no consequences in the two remaining outcomes. Our class points won’t rise or fall much. However, we’d gain a lot of private points. The only one who suffers in this scenario is the school. So there’s no need to try finding the VIP. If we talk, we’ll start suspecting someone of being the VIP, and then someone might make a mistake,” said Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Think about it. The school wouldn’t distribute the VIPs unfairly. … There’s no doubt that Classes A through D are starting equally,” Machida responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.86-87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you understand it now. If we talk amongst ourselves, we create doubt, which will tear us apart. As a result, our relationship as a group will crumble. We certainly could discover the VIP, but that strategy could inspire a traitor who wants victory for him or herself. There’s really no need for us to overthink things,” said Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We in Class A have established complete trust amongst ourselves. We’re not at all worried about that. Private issues ought to be solved by that private group,” answered Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s decided,” said Machida. (before Ichinose’s counter lands)<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, Ichinose. I understand what you’re trying to say, but if we follow along with what you’re proposing, there’ll be only one possible outcome. Only if everyone answers correctly will everyone in the group get a large number of points. The outcome you want isn’t going to happen. Or do you intend to discover the VIP’s identity through discussion, and then have Class B betray the rest of us? You just asked everyone if they wanted the first outcome. You aren’t very trustworthy, wouldn’t you say?” countered Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true. But would B, a higher-level class, accept such a thing? There’s no benefit to sacrificing your class so that the classes below gain something,” Machida said.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you oppose our proposal. Please remember that Class A has already committed to its decision. No matter what, we will discuss anything. You may talk amongst yourselves about whatever you wish,” Machida answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The three Class A students stand and go to the corner of the room — the demonstration of separation, planning to spend the rest of the time as they wish.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Runs the whole pitch as Katsuragi’s mouth: fair VIP distribution, no talk, no doubt, private issues private — then freezes Class A out of the circle the moment Ichinose refuses.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The debate opponent; her majority-vote warning and submarine counter are what force the corner withdrawal.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> The Class B boy who refuses to let the silence stand and keeps pressing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Attributes the whole strategy to him by name — “That was Katsuragi-san’s proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Uses her for the first outcomes answer, then counts her in the room’s math.<span class=\"pg\">p.86, 89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Prompts him for the negatives answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: the fair intervention and the second-gathering snicker<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p82-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami machida-kouji katsuragi-kouhei hamaguchi-tetsuya","q":"ch 3  3 1  the class b counter first class b hand in the rabbit room  then the steady counter to machida s silence until he and ichinose hold the middle of the circle   i agree  of course  we re a group  and it s only natural for us to cooperate  said tetsuya   isn t that a perfectly valid question  though  ichinose san didn t threaten us  she didn t order us to answer  if you don t want to  you don t have to respond  he said   no  i think that your question was valid  ichinose san  their wariness   if you simply refuse to engage  then i m unconvinced you can offer anything of value  hamaguchi said   i don t know specifically why ichinose san asked that question  however  this test requires us to come to a solution through discussion  if the students from class a want to sit in silence  then we ll have to carry on without you  at the very least  why not tell us what you think we should be discussing   well  that s a rather unique idea  how exactly will we come out on top without discussing things  though  do you think we should let the vip remain anonymous  and quit while we re ahead  hamaguchi spoke up  looking mildly irritated   i can t believe this  if anything  i m starting to believe that the vip is someone from class a  are you just sharing information with the vip and taking measures to protect him or her  hamaguchi asked   i do see what you re saying  but if we don t know which class the vip belongs to  the point gap between classes could be widened further  what if t","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p82-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html#sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p82-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the Class B counter<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.82–90<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">First Class B hand in the Rabbit room, then the steady counter to Machida’s silence until he and Ichinose hold the middle of the circle.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “I agree, of course. We’re a group, and it’s only natural for us to cooperate,” said Tetsuya.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “Isn’t that a perfectly valid question, though? Ichinose-san didn’t threaten us. She didn’t order us to answer. If you don’t want to, you don’t have to respond,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “No, I think that your question was valid, Ichinose-san. Their wariness … If you simply refuse to engage, then I’m unconvinced you can offer anything of value,” Hamaguchi said.<span class=\"pg\">p.83-84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Introduced as Hamaguchi Tetsuya — thin, somewhat androgynous, blue smooth hair; his early yes helps Ichinose’s opening trap work.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coolly brushes aside all of Class A’s criticism; Machida isn’t fazed, having expected it.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know specifically why Ichinose-san asked that question. However, this test requires us to come to a solution through discussion. If the students from Class A want to sit in silence, then we’ll have to carry on without you. At the very least, why not tell us what you think we should be discussing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration: “Hamaguchi was right.” Machida knows it and keeps his arms crossed.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s a rather unique idea. How exactly will we come out on top without discussing things, though? Do you think we should let the VIP remain anonymous, and quit while we’re ahead?” Hamaguchi spoke up, looking mildly irritated.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t believe this. If anything, I’m starting to believe that the VIP is someone from Class A. Are you just sharing information with the VIP and taking measures to protect him or her?” Hamaguchi asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I do see what you’re saying. But if we don’t know which class the VIP belongs to, the point gap between classes could be widened further. What if the VIP’s identity is extremely biased, and all VIPs are only chosen from one or two classes? That class would get millions of points. Although our class points won’t be affected, I’m sure everyone understands the importance of private points,” responded Hamaguchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The private-points argument the narration calls valid — and notes it wasn’t going to work against Katsuragi’s fairness read anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s certainly true that the school has made a point of emphasizing its commitment to fairness. If we believe that, then you’d be right,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We leave everything to you, Ichinose-san,” he replied. (trust from Class B called unshakeable; the other two B students nod)<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We agree with Ichinose-san,” said Hamaguchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The lieutenant — answers for Class B and defers the rest to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The running opponent on introductions and the no-discussion pitch.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Argues against the strategy attributed to him without naming him again after p.85.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the Class B off-switch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p82-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo ichinose-honami manabe-shiho","q":"ch 3  3 1  class c alignment and the rika charge follows karuizawa into the rabbit room s first yes  votes the convenient plan with the class c block  then crosses the circle to confront karuizawa with a summer story   i agree  everyone sharing the same answer would be the most rewarding result  but if anyone lied or betrayed us  we d be doomed  finding the vip just isn t realistic   even if the vip s in class a  would we be able to identify them  wouldn t that be difficult  she asked   refusing ichinose s alliance offer   hey  you re karuizawa san  right  there s something i wanted to ask you  said manabe   i might be mistaken  but did you have a fight with rika earlier in the summer   she s a girl from our class who wears glasses  she has her hair up in a bun  like a dango  remember her   isn t that strange  though  i m sure we heard about it  we heard that rika was bulled by a class d girl named karuizawa  rika told us you cut in line and pushed her aside when she was waiting at the cafe   the translation prints  bulled  as shown   no  not really  i m just checking to see if it s true  if it is true  though  i d like you to apologize  rika is the kind of girl to bottle everything up and stay quiet  so it s up to us to help her deal with situations like this   you won t mind if we check with rika then  will you  i mean  if it wasn t you  karuizawa san  then there won t be any problem  right  asked manabe","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p82-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p82-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: Class C alignment and the Rika charge<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.82–93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Follows Karuizawa into the Rabbit room’s first yes, votes the convenient plan with the Class C block, then crosses the circle to confront Karuizawa with a summer story.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “I agree. Everyone sharing the same answer would be the most rewarding result, but if anyone lied or betrayed us, we’d be doomed. Finding the VIP just isn’t realistic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Even if the VIP’s in Class A, would we be able to identify them? Wouldn’t that be difficult?” she asked. (refusing Ichinose’s alliance offer)<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Hey, you’re Karuizawa-san, right? There’s something I wanted to ask you,” said Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her line is what spreads the Professor’s sentiment through Class C; the Class C block then raises for the no-discussion plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I might be mistaken, but…did you have a fight with Rika earlier in the summer?”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s a girl from our class who wears glasses. She has her hair up in a bun, like a dango. Remember her?”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t that strange, though? I’m sure we heard about it. We heard that Rika was bulled by a Class D girl named Karuizawa. Rika told us you cut in line and pushed her aside when she was waiting at the café.” (the translation prints “bulled” as shown)<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, not really. I’m just checking to see if it’s true. If it is true, though, I’d like you to apologize. Rika is the kind of girl to bottle everything up and stay quiet, so it’s up to us to help her deal with situations like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You won’t mind if we check with Rika then, will you? I mean, if it wasn’t you, Karuizawa-san, then there won’t be any problem, right?” asked Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Turns her phone’s camera toward Karuizawa after the denials — then the phone is knocked out of her hands.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The victim is named only “Rika”; no surname is printed on this page.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Brings the summer café bullying story to her face and gets the phone slap for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Votes the same way after his line lands on Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> First aligns with the convenient plan, then refuses the alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.88, 92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: beaten back, then handed the fuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei sakura-airi yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 2  the first discussion breaks up watches the manabe karuizawa phone fight resolve through machida s intervention  then leaves with the group and decides to pull sakura for a second opinion on the test   well  we re heading back  too  i want to talk to hirata about some things  i said   cover for slipping away   hey  yukimura  wasn t karuizawa acting strangely  i asked   hmm  perfect timing  i murmured   sakura s instant message","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the first discussion breaks up<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–97<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the Manabe–Karuizawa phone fight resolve through Machida’s intervention, then leaves with the group and decides to pull Sakura for a second opinion on the test.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, we’re heading back, too. I want to talk to Hirata about some things,” I said. (cover for slipping away)<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hey, Yukimura. Wasn’t Karuizawa acting strangely?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hmm. Perfect timing,” I murmured. (Sakura’s instant message)<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays out of the middle of Manabe’s glare — “I didn’t want to get caught in the middle of anything, so I averted my eyes and got out of there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wants opinions from people other than Hirata and Horikita — “I’d probably gain insight after learning more about Sakura’s group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Keeps clear of her after the phone slap.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Reads the fear under her tough-girl act as off, then asks Yukimura about it.<span class=\"pg\">p.94, 97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Answers her meet-up message and heads for the bow.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Asks him first about Karuizawa’s mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: observing the Rabbit group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the bow with Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  3 1  the outsider s verdict watches the manabe karuizawa picture fight from the circle and speaks once  as an outsider   stupid  said ibuki   that s right  this absolutely has nothing to do with me  so i said what i thought as an outsider","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–95<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the Manabe–Karuizawa picture fight from the circle and speaks once, as an outsider.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “Stupid,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “That’s right. This absolutely has nothing to do with me. So I said what I thought as an outsider.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Crosses her arms and looks away; Manabe does not confront her — the narration reads a clear Class C hierarchy with Ibuki above Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Looks scornfully over at Manabe, showing her contempt, while the other Class C girls laugh at Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Above her in the Class C pecking order.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The only Class C voice that does not pile on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0–§3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: not at the shade meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"machida-kouji ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko hamaguchi-tetsuya ichinose-honami","q":"ch 3  3 2 3 4  bystander  closer  and the machida bait watches the phone fight as a bystander judging who is right  closes the first session kindly  leads the gloomy second gathering and works machida through yukimura and karuizawa   well  we have five more discussion periods left  how about we bring this session to a close  ichinose spoke kindly   well  this is the second time we ve gathered like this  don t you think we should start having open  honest conversation  we ll only meet so many times  reasoned ichinose   you know  life on a ship s not bad  it s really fun  right  even though we have to get together twice a day  we re still free to chat and use our phones  it s not like class  said ichinose   right  so  that s why we need to get more comfortable  we need to talk like we re all friends  don t you think it s hard  putting up walls like that  machida kun and the others always look so stern  you know   but couldn t i say the same thing of you  machida kun  can you really trust your allies  asked ichinose   really  you know what they say  an ounce of prevention is worth a pound of cure  are you trying to tell me that no one in your class would want even one extra point  it s not like the school will be bothered if you get more  replied ichinose   hmm  i suppose this is going to be tough  what do you think  ayanokouji kun   to him after class a leaves   it s far too soon to give up  let s work hard together  ichinose seemed determined to do her best   well  even if we ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: bystander, closer, and the Machida bait<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94, p.96, p.106–110<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the phone fight as a bystander judging who is right; closes the first session kindly; leads the gloomy second gathering and works Machida through Yukimura and Karuizawa.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Well, we have five more discussion periods left. How about we bring this session to a close?” Ichinose spoke kindly.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Well, this is the second time we’ve gathered like this. Don’t you think we should start having open, honest conversation? We’ll only meet so many times,” reasoned Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “You know, life on a ship’s not bad. It’s really fun, right? Even though we have to get together twice a day, we’re still free to chat and use our phones. It’s not like class,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> “Ichinose watched it unfold, a bystander. It was as if she was trying to determine who was right and wrong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the lead again; wished for peace; Class B ready to ally without hesitation — “Ichinose and her friends should have been striving for a Class B victory,” yet she pushes cross-class talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right? So, that’s why we need to get more comfortable. We need to talk like we’re all friends. Don’t you think it’s hard, putting up walls like that? Machida-kun and the others always look so stern, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But couldn’t I say the same thing of you, Machida-kun? Can you really trust your allies?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? You know what they say: An ounce of prevention is worth a pound of cure. Are you trying to tell me that no one in your class would want even one extra point? It’s not like the school will be bothered if you get more,” replied Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Smiles at Machida’s “That’s stupid” — she’d “certainly gotten a response out of him”; the narration calls the Yukimura–Karuizawa pair her information-collecting tools and wonders when Machida will notice the ploy.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm. I suppose this is going to be tough. What do you think, Ayanokouji-kun?” (to him after Class A leaves)<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s far too soon to give up. Let’s work hard together!” Ichinose seemed determined to do her best.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, even if we keep having these discussions, I don’t think anyone will come out and say they’re the VIP. The benefits of staying hidden are just too great, same as the downsides for being discovered. At this rate, Class A’s worst-case scenario prediction will probably come true,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator: calmer, wittier, clearer than he’d thought; if she were his classmate he would have had a crush — “She was just that charming” — rivaling Kushida in popularity.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The baited Class A debater.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Pulls him into the walk-out talk without putting him on the spot earlier.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Uses her complaint as the opening for the comfort speech.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The other half of the information pair.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Closes the session with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: taking the lead in Rabbit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: cards, the castle gate, and the deck pledge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho machida-kouji ibuki-mio karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 3  3 1  the phone fight resolves after the slap  both sides claim the other is wrong  machida talks manabe down  karuizawa apologises for the stepped foot  and the friction is filed for later   that s what i should be saying  don t just take pictures of me without permission  i already told you that you had the wrong person  karuizawa snapped   i don t know  just ask the school for a new one  answered karuizawa   on whether the phone is broken   what  are you saying i m the bad guy here  asked karuizawa   but i don t want you to   no  i don t want you to  come on  please  say something to her  karuizawa pleaded  for some reason  she turned to machida  begging him to intervene   i won t forgive you if you take my picture without permission  what do you think  machida kun   come on  lay off me  thank you  machida kun  said karuizawa   well  i m going to head back aaah   exhausted rise that becomes the foot step","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the phone fight resolves<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the slap, both sides claim the other is wrong; Machida talks Manabe down, Karuizawa apologises for the stepped foot, and the friction is filed for later.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “That’s what I should be saying! Don’t just take pictures of me without permission. I already told you that you had the wrong person,” Karuizawa snapped.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I don’t know! Just ask the school for a new one,” answered Karuizawa. (on whether the phone is broken)<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “What? Are you saying I’m the bad guy here?” asked Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I don’t want you to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her words are “surprisingly weak” — some fear mixed in with the tough-girl act; Ayanokōji files it as maybe imagination.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I don’t want you to! Come on. Please, say something to her,” Karuizawa pleaded. For some reason, she turned to Machida, begging him to intervene. “I won’t forgive you if you take my picture without permission. What do you think, Machida-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, lay off me. Thank you, Machida-kun,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Looks up at Machida “her eyes full of gratitude”; the narration floats a new-love joke — she already has Hirata — then files the Class C friction as future trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’m going to head back—Aaah?!” (exhausted rise that becomes the foot-step)<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pitched forward, staggered onto Manabe’s foot, apologised quickly and left — “Ah, I didn’t mean to do that. I’m sorry,” Karuizawa mumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The fight, the forgiveness-ask, and the accidental foot-step on the way out.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The Class A boy she begs and thanks.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Ibuki’s scorn for Manabe is the only Class C support she gets.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the Rabbit votes and Manabe’s phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p107-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the background-character file<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei machida-kouji ibuki-mio manabe-shiho","q":"ch 3  3 1 3 4  beaten back  then handed the fuse after the phone is knocked down  presses the picture demand with two class c girls  loses to machida s fairness argument  takes the stepped foot  then meets ayanokoji s elevator lie   what the hell  shouted manabe   what ll you do if my phone s broken  shouted manabe   i have some really precious photos stored on that phone  though   if it wasn t you  you wouldn t get all angry and deny it like that  right  let us take your picture  said manabe   perhaps the reason you re denying it so much is because it s true  asked manabe   anyway  just let me take your picture  shouted manabe   m machida kun  this has nothing to do with you  answered manabe   ouch  shouted manabe   when karuizawa steps on her foot   hey  what the hell  shouted manabe   yelling at the room as they leave","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: beaten back, then handed the fuse<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–96, p.110–111<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the phone is knocked down, presses the picture demand with two Class C girls, loses to Machida’s fairness argument, takes the stepped foot, then meets Ayanokōji’s elevator lie.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “What the hell?!” shouted Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “What’ll you do if my phone’s broken?” shouted Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “I have some really precious photos stored on that phone, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it wasn’t you, you wouldn’t get all angry and deny it like that, right? Let us take your picture,” said Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Perhaps the reason you’re denying it so much is because it’s true?” asked Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Points her phone camera at Karuizawa to force the picture while two other Class C girls laugh; Ibuki’s “Stupid” is the only pushback and Manabe does not confront her — Class C hierarchy, Ibuki above her.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, just let me take your picture!” shouted Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “M-Machida-kun, this has nothing to do with you,” answered Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Backed down by Machida’s fairness argument without being wholly convinced.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ouch!” shouted Manabe. (when Karuizawa steps on her foot)<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, what the hell?!” shouted Manabe. (yelling at the room as they leave)<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The picture target and the foot that lands on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The Class A arbiter who stops her.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Scorned as an outsider; the hierarchy keeps Manabe from answering back.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p82-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: Class C alignment and the Rika charge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p110-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the elevator fuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p95-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho ichinose-honami morishige-takurou takemoto-shigeru machida-kouji","q":"ch 3  3 1 3 4  the fair intervention and the second gathering snicker called over by karuizawa mid fight  rules manabe in the wrong on pictures  then reappears in the second discussion as ichinose s baited target   i agree  manabe  karuizawa has told you that she doesn t want you to take her picture  stop it  machida added   from what i ve heard just now  i think you re the one in the wrong here  manabe  karuizawa told you she doesn t know what you re talking about  so it s wrong for you to forcefully take her picture  don t you agree  i think it s best to talk to your friend again and confirm if the story is true   all i did was the right thing  machida blushed slightly   after karuizawa s gratitude  narration floats a love line   she already has hirata   you re free to do whatever you want  but you probably won t find the vip    devising a way to gain points for themselves    how can you trust these guys  he asked   the snicker after ichinose s optimism   of course i can   on trusting his allies  looks at morishige beside him  then refocuses on ichinose s calm class a image   we have no reason to fuss over finding the vip  we have more than 100 000 points deposited into our accounts every month  no one in our class would lie just to get a mere 500 000   that s stupid  go ahead and keep being delusional  you re just grasping at straws","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html#sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p95-1\">Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: the fair intervention and the second-gathering snicker<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.95, p.107–108<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Called over by Karuizawa mid-fight, rules Manabe in the wrong on pictures, then reappears in the second discussion as Ichinose’s baited target.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morishige-takurou\">Morishige Takurō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#takemoto-shigeru\">Takemoto Shigeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “I agree. Manabe, Karuizawa has told you that she doesn’t want you to take her picture. Stop it,” Machida added.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “From what I’ve heard just now, I think you’re the one in the wrong here, Manabe. Karuizawa told you she doesn’t know what you’re talking about, so it’s wrong for you to forcefully take her picture. Don’t you agree? I think it’s…”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “All I did was the right thing.” Machida blushed slightly. (after Karuizawa’s gratitude; narration floats a love line — she already has Hirata)<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From what I’ve heard just now, I think you’re the one in the wrong here, Manabe. Karuizawa told you she doesn’t know what you’re talking about, so it’s wrong for you to forcefully take her picture. Don’t you agree? I think it’s best to talk to your friend again and confirm if the story is true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judged correctly by the narrator; Takemoto and the other Class A are not interested in the sideshow.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re free to do whatever you want, but you probably won’t find the VIP. … devising a way to gain points for themselves. … How can you trust these guys?” he asked. (the snicker after Ichinose’s optimism)<span class=\"pg\">p.107-108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Trying to shake the room up — the narration says so outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I can.” (on trusting his allies; looks at Morishige beside him, then refocuses on Ichinose’s calm Class A image)<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have no reason to fuss over finding the VIP. We have more than 100,000 points deposited into our accounts every month. No one in our class would lie just to get a mere 500,000.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s stupid. Go ahead and keep being delusional. You’re just grasping at straws.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Says he will not participate, then takes Ichinose’s bait anyway — the narration notes the only problem is when he notices her ploy.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The girl whose picture he defends.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The girl he stops.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The bait partner of the second gathering.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishige Takurō<\/b> The Class A seatmate he glances at on “Of course I can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Takemoto Shigeru<\/b> Named in the room as the uninterested Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p81-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the Class A no-discussion pitch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the protection offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 3  3 2 3 5  strategy talk and the kouenji explosion eager to start the class d strategy huddle after the first discussion  back for the second gathering and the cabin when kouenji ends the monkey group   she s always acting strangely  he replied   on karuizawa  the straightforward answer ayanokoji did not want   i don t think we need a breakthrough right now  but we do need a discussion  class a might be breaking away from this test  but i think we need to pinpoint the vip  said yukimura   i understand  karuizawa san  but doesn t that just depend on your point of view  i mean  the test on the island was also a surprise to the students  said yukimura   so you can t trust us  hirata  if you know  then i have the right to know  too  besides  if you know who a vip is  that might give us some kind of hint  we should all be sharing information with each other in the first place  it s only natural  after all  said yukimura   i see  murmured yukimura  he was careful not to say too much   after the two vip names   speaking of rabbit group  it s equally possible for the vip to be from any of the four classes  so in class d  there are two vips that we know about  there should be one more vip keeping his or her identity secret  said yukimura   you just faked being ill to get out of it   troublesome  you re not even thinking about this test at all  countered yukimura   what did you just do  kouenji  shouted yukimura   the school notification   y you ve got to be kidding me  we re despe","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\">Ch.3 §3.2–§3.5: strategy talk and the Kouenji explosion<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.96–97, p.107, p.112–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Eager to start the Class D strategy huddle after the first discussion; back for the second gathering and the cabin when Kouenji ends the Monkey group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “She’s always acting strangely,” he replied. (on Karuizawa; the straightforward answer Ayanokōji did not want)<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I don’t think we need a breakthrough right now, but we do need a discussion. Class A might be breaking away from this test, but I think we need to pinpoint the VIP,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I understand, Karuizawa-san. But doesn’t that just depend on your point of view? I mean, the test on the island was also a surprise to the students,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His words “helped motivate us somewhat”; Ayanokōji then wonders if he is the target using camouflage.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Misses the “surprise”/“Sunrise” collision with the Professor entirely.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you can’t trust us, Hirata? If you know, then I have the right to know, too. Besides, if you know who a VIP is, that might give us some kind of hint. We should all be sharing information with each other in the first place. It’s only natural, after all,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see,” murmured Yukimura. He was careful not to say too much. (after the two VIP names)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Speaking of Rabbit Group, it’s equally possible for the VIP to be from any of the four classes. So in Class D, there are two VIPs that we know about. There should be one more VIP keeping his or her identity secret,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Bolts out of his chair at Kouenji’s humming: “Kouenji, stop the happy-go-lucky act already! I’m not going to tell you to take things seriously, but you need to at least participate. We don’t want you to screw everything up like you did back on the island,” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just faked being ill to get out of it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Troublesome? You’re not even thinking about this test at all!” countered Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What did you just do, Kouenji?!” shouted Yukimura. (the school notification)<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-you’ve got to be kidding me! We’re desperately trying to think of a way out of this, and that guy, he just…”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re being way too generous! That guy will screw anyone over, so long as he’s able to enjoy himself and take it easy. This sucks!” shouted Yukimura. (to Hirata’s restraint)<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn it. Thanks to Kouenji, things have escalated,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The target of every shout in the cabin.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Pushed for the VIP names, then called too generous on Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Strategy partner and cabin witness.<span class=\"pg\">p.97, 112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His flat read on her mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: from the convenient plan to Ichinose<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p131-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the roommate’s VIP probe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 2  the bow with sakura meets sakura behind a pillar on the quiet bow deck  she stress mutters  hands him the cow group list  and they compete over who has fewer friends   sakura  what s the matter  i asked  trying not to surprise her   i didn t really hear anything  i just got here now   so  why did you call me out here  i asked   sorry  i don t really have any friends  either  i said   by the way  there was something i wanted to ask you  sakura   has yamauchi gotten in touch with you at all since the discussion ended   for the time being  contact me if something s bothering you  you can tell me anything  i said   yeah  that s the least i can do","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the bow with Sakura<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.97–102<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Sakura behind a pillar on the quiet bow deck; she stress-mutters, hands him the Cow group list, and they compete over who has fewer friends.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sakura? What’s the matter?” I asked, trying not to surprise her.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I didn’t really hear anything. I just got here now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “So, why did you call me out here?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the Cow roster — Sawada, Shimizu, Nishi, Yoshida / Kobashi, Ninomiya, Watanabe / Tokitou, Nomura, Yashima / Ike, Sakura, Sudou, Matsushita — and feels sympathy for her with Sudou and Ike as the Class D boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Weighs helping her secretly against acting unnaturally: “In a test like this, breaking the rules could mean death.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. I don’t really have any friends, either,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, there was something I wanted to ask you, Sakura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Has Yamauchi gotten in touch with you at all since the discussion ended?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Island after-action: he used Sakura while using Horikita, and manipulated Yamauchi with a promise of her email he had not yet asked her for — “Since I’d planted the seeds myself, if Yamauchi made a move, I would have to act.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the time being, contact me if something’s bothering you. You can tell me anything,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. That’s the least I can do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches her develop quickly since the island — more assertive, eyes sparkling — and notes she has learned to stay positive without transforming completely.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The loner pact and the standing contact offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The unasked-for favour that is about to explode.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> One of only two people who could help Sakura from another class — already taken by his own group.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> The other name; not available either.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the first discussion breaks up<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: the Yamauchi redirect<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki sudou-ken ike-kanji matsushita-chiaki sakura-airi","q":"ch 3  3 2  the bow stress talk waits behind a pillar on the bow deck after moving from the crowded elevator route  mutters to herself  hands ayanokoji the cow roster  and finds the one person who will take her call   i was thinking about it  but h how do i do it  she murmured out loud   before he arrives   self talk over the wind   aaaieeeeeeeeeeee  sakura yelped  practically jumping out of her own skin  seemed like i d surprised her after all   wh wh when did you get here  how much did you hear  she asked frantically   were you listening  did you hear what i was saying  sakura shouted   um  well  you see  it s ah  i was s stressing out over the test  she shouted   i thought i might know someone from another class but amazingly enough  i don t know anyone  no one who would remotely consider me a   friend  said sakura   ah  it s okay  you don t need to apologize  it s just that i don t have any friends  sakura responded   huh  me  what is it   yamauchi kun  no  he hasn t  is something the matter  she asked   on yamauchi contact   is that okay  asked sakura   after he offers to be her contact   i ll definitely contact you  she said","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the bow stress-talk<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.97–102<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits behind a pillar on the bow deck after moving from the crowded elevator route; mutters to herself, hands Ayanokōji the Cow roster, and finds the one person who will take her call.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#matsushita-chiaki\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “I was thinking about it, but…h-how do I do it?” she murmured out loud. (before he arrives — self-talk over the wind)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Aaaieeeeeeeeeeee!” Sakura yelped, practically jumping out of her own skin. Seemed like I’d surprised her after all. “Wh-wh-when did you get here? How much did you hear?” she asked frantically.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Were you listening?! Did you hear what I was saying?!” Sakura shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Um, well. You see, it’s…ah… I was s-stressing out over the test!” she shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands him a list — the Cow group names by class — looking incredibly depressed.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought I might know someone from another class but…amazingly enough, I don’t know anyone. No one who would remotely consider me a … friend,” said Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.100-101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, it’s okay. You don’t need to apologize. It’s just that…I don’t have any friends!” Sakura responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Me? What is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yamauchi-kun? No, he hasn’t. Is something the matter?” she asked. (on Yamauchi contact)<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that okay?” asked Sakura. (after he offers to be her contact)<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll definitely contact you!” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Eyes sparkle like a child’s; a little different from her usual self — overjoyed, more vigor, maybe more assertive; the island test “changed her life in unexpected ways” and she has learned to stay positive.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The loner pact, the contact offer, and the secret he keeps about Yamauchi’s email promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Names him as not having been in touch; does not know the email promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> On her Cow roster as a Class D boy she is stuck with.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The other Class D boy on the roster.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> The fourth Class D name on her list.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the roommate appeal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p183-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.5: the Cow group ends<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p97-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 3  3 2 3 4  hunger and the sunrise gag last out of the first rabbit room with the class b trio and ibuki  back for the second gathering s one comic beat   i m hungry again  i wonder if there s a lunch buffet  mused the professor   if it s sunrise  leave it to me  that s my specialty  i m fired up  shouted the professor   on yukimura s  surprise","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p97-1\">Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: hunger and the Sunrise gag<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.97, p.107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Last out of the first Rabbit room with the Class B trio and Ibuki; back for the second gathering’s one comic beat.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “I’m hungry again. I wonder if there’s a lunch buffet,” mused the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “If it’s Sunrise, leave it to me! That’s my specialty. I’m fired up!” shouted the Professor. (on Yukimura’s “surprise”)<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator: how can he be hungry again after three heavy lunches in an hour — “What kind of body lets you digest all that food in just an hour?!” — and doubts the heartfelt advice will reach him.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands up slowly to leave; last people in the room are the three Class B students and Ibuki with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The mishearing gets the narration’s flat “No, I thought. No, they said ‘surprise,’ not ‘Sunrise.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Leaves with him; feeds him the line he mangles.<span class=\"pg\">p.97, 107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The one who doubts the diet advice will land.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the Professor in Rabbit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the VIP alibi and the card heat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 3  the yamauchi redirect choked by yamauchi haruki the moment he re enters the ship  the sakura email lie becomes a camera and points pep talk   wh what s the matter  i knew the reason  but asked as a formality   i never meant to go after her  well  this is kind of hard to say  but i lied to you before  i croaked   do you really think that a loner like me would know sakura s email address  i turned toward him  trying to show my sincerity   yeah  sorry   can you give me just a little more time  i asked   then are you going to make sakura tell you  i asked   you know  sakura said she hates guys that are all talk   of course she hates me  but it should be obvious why i couldn t give you her contact information  i don t want you to make the same mistake i did  yamauchi  if you forcibly asked her  it wouldn t go anywhere  it d be pointless   yeah  and i m sorry  but i know for sure that she doesn t hate you  i answered   did you know that sakura loves digital cameras  i ve heard that her camera doesn t work  and she doesn t have enough points to buy a new one  but what if you got one for her  yamauchi  if you gave it to her as a present  i asked   well  there a few options in this special test  if you were the vip and managed to make it through without being found out  or if you became a traitor and sold out your group  or if you managed to guide your group to clear the test  you d get enough points to buy tons of digital cameras  right   now  yamauchi haruki  you need to ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: the Yamauchi redirect<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.103–105<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Choked by Yamauchi Haruki the moment he re-enters the ship; the Sakura-email lie becomes a camera-and-points pep talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Wh-what’s the matter?” I knew the reason, but asked as a formality.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I never meant to go after her. Well, this is kind of hard to say, but…I lied to you before,” I croaked.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Do you really think that a loner like me would know Sakura’s email address?” I turned toward him, trying to show my sincerity.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can you give me just a little more time?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then are you going to make Sakura tell you?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, Sakura said she hates guys that are all talk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course she hates me. But it should be obvious why I couldn’t give you her contact information. I don’t want you to make the same mistake I did, Yamauchi. If you forcibly asked her, it wouldn’t go anywhere. It’d be pointless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. And I’m sorry. But I know for sure that she doesn’t hate you,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you know that Sakura loves digital cameras? I’ve heard that her camera doesn’t work, and she doesn’t have enough points to buy a new one. But what if you got one for her, Yamauchi? If you gave it to her as a present?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there a few options in this special test. If you were the VIP and managed to make it through without being found out, or if you became a traitor and sold out your group, or if you managed to guide your group to clear the test, you’d get enough points to buy tons of digital cameras. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now, Yamauchi Haruki, you need to achieve real results. Work hard, and show Sakura how manly you are. Only then would you be a guy who deserves to go out with a former idol.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right, Yamauchi. You can definitely do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Redirects the rage into the test as “a temporary fix”; worries Yamauchi might get too fired up and miss the VIP, then deliberately withholds the caution — a missed target is fine, the bigger picture matters more.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The mark, the lie, and the stimulus.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Her camera and her idol past become the bait; her contact stays protected.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the bow with Sakura<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the second gathering and the Manabe fuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 3  3 3  the neck grab and the camera stimulus ambushes ayanokoji inside the ship over sakura s email  nearly chokes him  then walks out of the cabin door with a mission   what s the matter  my ass  you said you d tell me sakura s email address  for chrissakes  and you were talking with sakura just now  i knew it  you were after her all along  he shouted   wait  you lied   so  wait  so just now you were trying to ask sakura for her email address   so  you didn t know her email address at all  ayanokouji  you lied to me  he sputtered   so how d it go  did you get sakura s email address   sorry  what does that mean  i m not looking for an apology  i m looking for her email  yamauchi muttered to himself  reflecting the depth of his disappointment   how are you  how dare you trick me  he shouted   more time   show me a liar and i will show you a thief  he shouted   the proverb that shocks the narrator   yeah  that s right   on making sakura tell him   probably blinded by anger  willing to get the contact by force   you mean guys like you  ayanokouji  he shouted   on sakura hating guys that are all talk   you re just making excuses  you never knew her info in the first place  yamauchi lowered his head   but what the hell should i do  he asked   oh  she d be happy  for sure  but i don t have any points  either   so if i do my best  there s a chance i can get a new camera for sakura  he asked  yamauchi was about to burst   i ll do it  i ll do it  i ll do it  i ll do it  i ll give ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: the neck-grab and the camera stimulus<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.103–105<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ambushes Ayanokōji inside the ship over Sakura’s email, nearly chokes him, then walks out of the cabin door with a mission.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “‘What’s the matter’ my ass! You said you’d tell me Sakura’s email address, for chrissakes! And you were talking with Sakura just now! I knew it. You were after her all along!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Wait. You lied?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “So… Wait, so just now you were trying to ask Sakura for her email address?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs Ayanokōji from behind and tightens on his neck until he taps out — “looking like some sort of oni or an asura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So… You didn’t know her email address at all, Ayanokouji. You lied to me?” he sputtered.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So how’d it go? Did you get Sakura’s email address?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry? What does that mean? I’m not looking for an apology, I’m looking for her email!” Yamauchi muttered to himself, reflecting the depth of his disappointment. “How are you… How dare you trick me!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “More time?! ‘Show me a liar and I will show you a thief’!” he shouted. (the proverb that shocks the narrator)<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, that’s right.” (on making Sakura tell him — probably blinded by anger, willing to get the contact by force)<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean guys like you, Ayanokouji?!” he shouted. (on Sakura hating guys that are all talk)<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re just making excuses. You never knew her info in the first place.” Yamauchi lowered his head.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what the hell should I do?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, she’d be happy, for sure, but…I don’t have any points, either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So if I do my best, there’s a chance I can get a new camera for Sakura?” he asked. Yamauchi was about to burst.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll do it, I’ll do it, I’ll do it, I’ll do it! I’ll give it everything I’ve got and win Sakura!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah! I’m definitely going to win!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What?” he asked. (when Ayanokōji starts “Let me tell you something, just in case…”)<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course.” (on not letting other classes beat him to the VIP)<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Blinded by anger at first, then coachable the moment the camera-and-points route appears; the narrator redirected his energy into the test as a temporary fix and worries he might fire past the target.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The liar, then the coach.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The crush whose email and camera drive every line he speaks.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: the contrast name<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei machida-kouji hamaguchi-tetsuya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 4  the second gathering and the manabe fuse sits the gloomy second rabbit discussion with class a absent  watches ichinose bait machida  then lies to manabe about seeing karuizawa fight to light a fuse   to be perfectly honest  i m the type to just sit things out  i m just a bystander  i said   to ichinose","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the second gathering and the Manabe fuse<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.106–111<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits the gloomy second Rabbit discussion with Class A absent, watches Ichinose bait Machida, then lies to Manabe about seeing Karuizawa fight to light a fuse.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “To be perfectly honest, I’m the type to just sit things out. I’m just a bystander,” I said. (to Ichinose)<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the alliance map: only Class A guaranteed advancement, so B+D against C+A — “like putting carnivores and herbivores together in the same cage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Class A’s phone use is legal and calm is Katsuragi’s maintained image — “an exceptionally effective strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> On being a lone wolf inside Class A’s walls.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The Karuizawa write-up: off since the test started — the Ibuki reunion, the Manabe confrontation, background-character quiet where Hirata and Kushida stay themselves; she is irreplaceable for Class D cohesion and he needs to know if she is useful, “even if it meant being forceful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Trails Manabe’s group to the elevator and plants the lie: “I’m not 100% sure, but I think I saw Karuizawa fight with a girl from another class,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps it vague on purpose; had seen nothing and would have been exposed if he kept talking — “Now that the fuse was lit, Manabe and the others would react. How would the newly docile Karuizawa respond? I wanted to find out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Reads her bait of Machida through Yukimura and Karuizawa; charms him enough that he admits he would have had a crush if she were his classmate.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The liar’s target.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The subject of both the write-up and the planted story.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Watches him take Ichinose’s bait despite the no-talk policy.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> The Class B off-switch when the hour ends — “No, we didn’t do much of anything. Well, shall we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: the Yamauchi redirect<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5: the cabin, the VIP sheet, Kouenji’s exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p106-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke hamaguchi-tetsuya","q":"ch 3  3 4  the class b off switch second gathering  named with the other class b students as ready to make alliances without hesitation  then closes the hour with the group s flip to off   no  we didn t do much of anything  well  shall we  said hamaguchi   when ichinose says they re done for today","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html#sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p106-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the Class B off-switch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.106, p.110<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second gathering: named with the other Class B students as ready to make alliances without hesitation, then closes the hour with the group’s flip to OFF.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “No, we didn’t do much of anything. Well, shall we?” said Hamaguchi. (when Ichinose says they’re done for today)<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Hamaguchi and the other Class B students were exactly like that, too. They were ready to make alliances without hesitation. It was like how Hirata operated. They were similar, but still fundamentally different.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The three Class B students relax at once “almost as if someone had flipped their switches to OFF”; Ayanokōji still does not know the deal with them or their aims.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Follows her lead into the room and out of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.106, 110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The operating style the narration compares them to.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p82-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the Class B counter<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p138-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the card table and the corridor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"machida-kouji kouenji-rokusuke katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 3  the calm image and the surprise reaction still not in the room   his maintained image runs class a s second gathering phones  and his name surfaces when kouenji ends a group","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\">Ch.3: the calm image and the surprise reaction<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.106, p.115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still not in the room — his maintained image runs Class A’s second-gathering phones, and his name surfaces when Kouenji ends a group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “I thought their loss during the test on the island would’ve changed them, but Katsuragi had them maintaining their calm … image. It was an exceptionally effective strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106-107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Named with Ryūen and Ichinose as the leaders who “would all be surprised” by Kouenji’s early traitor move — “Probably no one had imagined that someone would turn traitor so soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The front man keeping the calm Class A image.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> One of the three the Monkey exit blindsides.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named as the island strategist and the no-discussion plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the castle gate holds<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p107-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka manabe-shiho hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 3  3 4  the background character file second gathering  complains the vip hunt is unfair  gets ichinose s comfort  then sighs back to her phone while ayanokoji writes her up as off pattern   but can we really find the vip by talking  i just don t think we can  it s just  like  this test is so unfair  it s too hard  the vip has way too much of an advantage  said karuizawa   sunrise  karuizawa looked puzzled   on yukimura s  surprise   well  yeah  it is pretty fun  said karuizawa   agreeing with ichinose s ship life pitch","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p107-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p107-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the background-character file<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.107–109<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second gathering: complains the VIP hunt is unfair, gets Ichinose’s comfort, then sighs back to her phone while Ayanokōji writes her up as off-pattern.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “But can we really find the VIP by talking? I just don’t think we can. It’s just, like, this test is so unfair. It’s too hard. The VIP has way too much of an advantage,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Sunrise?” Karuizawa looked puzzled. (on Yukimura’s “surprise”)<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Well, yeah. It is pretty fun,” said Karuizawa. (agreeing with Ichinose’s ship-life pitch)<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sighs and goes back to fiddling with her phone mid-discussion — rude in a VIP hunt, or maybe CIA-line to Hirata, the narrator jokes; either way out of character for someone who never puts in effort.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The full write-up: off since the test started — Ibuki reunion, Manabe confrontation, background character where Hirata and Kushida stay themselves; answer-then-shrink; group hierarchy would put her below Manabe and the Class C girls; for Class D cohesion “Karuizawa Kei was irreplaceable” and he expected her to dominate the field.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Gets the comfort speech and the perception lesson.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The subject of the file that ends in “I needed to stir the pot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Named as above her in the room’s hierarchy.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The contrast who “was always Hirata.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The contrast who “was always Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the phone fight resolves<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the lunch history and the Machida seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p110-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho","q":"ch 3  3 4  the elevator fuse trailing class c out of the second discussion  ayanokoji stops her with the fabricated karuizawa cafe story   i heard about your problem with karuizawa  something about her pushing someone at the cafe  right   ayanokoji s opener  recorded here as the row that lands on her   yeah  why do you ask  snapped manabe   that s  are you sure  asked manabe  her voice was stiff  and she drew nearer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p110-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p110-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the elevator fuse<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.110–111<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Trailing Class C out of the second discussion, Ayanokōji stops her with the fabricated Karuizawa café story.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “I heard about your problem with Karuizawa. Something about her pushing someone at the café, right?” (Ayanokōji’s opener; recorded here as the row that lands on her)<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Yeah. Why do you ask?” snapped Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “That’s… Are you sure?” asked Manabe. Her voice was stiff, and she drew nearer.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Goes on guard, then closer — the topic has her and two classmates focused on him “like they were checking me out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The fuse is lit; how she and the others react is left for the next pages of the volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The liar who chose her as the match.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The subject of the planted story.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: beaten back, then handed the fuse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the threat across the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 5  the cabin  the vip sheet  kouenji s exit returns near midnight to hirata  yukimura and a push uping kouenji  gets the two known vip names by phone  then walks out after kouenji ends the monkey group   yeah  a bit  ah  that reminds me  i wanted to talk to you for a minute  if you have the time   oh no  that s okay  you go first  hirata  we can talk about my thing later   what  who  i asked   after hirata s two classmate vip whisper   hey  hirata  wouldn t it be better to give us that information by phone  we don t know who s listening in on our conversations  i said   it s impossible  i muttered   i m stepping out for a bit  i said","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\">Ch.3 §3.5: the cabin, the VIP sheet, Kouenji’s exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.112–116<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns near midnight to Hirata, Yukimura and a push-uping Kouenji; gets the two known VIP names by phone, then walks out after Kouenji ends the Monkey group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yeah, a bit. Ah, that reminds me. I wanted to talk to you for a minute, if you have the time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Oh no, that’s okay. You go first, Hirata. We can talk about my thing later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “What? Who?” I asked. (after Hirata’s two-classmate VIP whisper)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Meant to ask Hirata about Sakayanagi — a popular guy should have information — but waits.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Hirata. Wouldn’t it be better to give us that information by phone? We don’t know who’s listening in on our conversations,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reads the two names Hirata turns the phone toward — Dragon/Kushida, Horse/Minami — then erases them.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Instant read: Kushida as Dragon VIP is an enormous advantage and terrifying — “Once they knew her identity, she was at their mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Admits his own limit: three days left, not enough eyes and ears even with Hirata and Kushida as ringleaders — “It’s impossible,” I muttered — and resolves to get more people on his side, Horikita and Sakura included.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s impossible,” I muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m stepping out for a bit,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The trusted conduit for the VIP sheet; rule-reader who notes participation penalties.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Cabin partner; both read the VIP math and both erupt at Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Watched end his own group with a traitor submission and walk into the bathroom — “Adieu.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Named Dragon VIP on the erased screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her message: “I’m sorry. Things seem really confusing right now. I’m going to give you a call.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> One of the few eyes-and-ears he still counts on.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: the second gathering and the Manabe fuse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.6: the starlit hug and the teachers’ table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 3  3 5  the trusted conduit waiting when ayanokoji returns near midnight  shares the yukimura info chat  whispers the two known vips  and shows them by phone   good work today  ayanokouji kun  you re rather late  said hirata   i m sure you re tired  but if you re up for it  do you mind talking with me  he asked   the simultaneous ask with ayanokoji   huh  what did you want to ask me  said hirata   i just chatted a bit with yukimura kun  we decided to share information about the test  said hirata   i would ve been glad if kouenji kun participated  but he unfortunately declined  said hirata   kouenji is participating in a group  after all  students are required to participate  and points are taken away if a student fails to participate  said hirata   trust hirata to read the rules thoroughly   to tell you the truth  i got word that two of our classmates have been selected as the vips in their groups  he whispered   that s  i can t say  they only told me because they trust me   yeah  you re right  wait just a moment   agreeing to phone for the names   don t worry  everything is all right  said hirata   yeah  i think your logic follows  they certainly haven t talked to me about it  but they might ve consulted someone else  after all  there s a high risk of being discovered if you talk  hirata said   we still don t know anything yet  he probably had his own ideas  replied hirata   on kouenji s sudden traitor move","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\">Ch.3 §3.5: the trusted conduit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.112–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waiting when Ayanokōji returns near midnight; shares the Yukimura info chat, whispers the two known VIPs, and shows them by phone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Good work today, Ayanokouji-kun. You’re rather late,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I’m sure you’re tired, but if you’re up for it, do you mind talking with me?” he asked. (the simultaneous ask with Ayanokōji)<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Huh? What did you want to ask me?” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just chatted a bit with Yukimura-kun. We decided to share information about the test,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I would’ve been glad if Kouenji-kun participated, but he unfortunately declined,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kouenji is participating in a group. After all, students are required to participate, and points are taken away if a student fails to participate,” said Hirata. (trust Hirata to read the rules thoroughly)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To tell you the truth, I got word that two of our classmates have been selected as the VIPs in their groups,” he whispered.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s… I can’t say. They only told me because they trust me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, you’re right. Wait just a moment.” (agreeing to phone for the names)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Puts two names on the screen for Yukimura and Ayanokōji — “Dragon Group, Kushida-san. Horse Group, Minami-kun.” — and erases them immediately after.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. Everything is all right,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I think your logic follows. They certainly haven’t talked to me about it, but they might’ve consulted someone else. After all, there’s a high risk of being discovered if you talk,” Hirata said.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We still don’t know anything yet. He probably had his own ideas,” replied Hirata. (on Kouenji’s sudden traitor move)<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His phone starts beeping continuously as classmates demand to know what happened; he stays the generous reader of the situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The info-chat partner before Ayanokōji arrived.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Declined the huddle, then ended his own group under him.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Named Dragon VIP on his screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Trusts him with the erased screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster and in the Ichinose comparison<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p131-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the absent roommate and the corridor pass<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 3  3 5  push ups  refusal  and the monkey exit naked from the waist up doing push ups in the cabin  declines the huddle  then ends the monkey group with a traitor submission while the others watch   i did say that it was pointless to include you  ayanokouji  added kouenji  how nice   sorry  hirata boy  i m far too busy with the pursuit of physical beauty   well  i couldn t exactly help it  i was in awful shape  i couldn t force myself to do the impossible  answered kouenji   on the island   my  this test will be nothing but troublesome  wouldn t you say  kouenji sniffed   well  there isn t any point to continuing a test that isn t interesting  is there  finding a liar is simple","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\">Ch.3 §3.5: push-ups, refusal, and the Monkey exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.112–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Naked from the waist up doing push-ups in the cabin, declines the huddle, then ends the Monkey group with a traitor submission while the others watch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I did say that it was pointless to include you, Ayanokouji,” added Kouenji. How nice.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Sorry, Hirata Boy. I’m far too busy with the pursuit of physical beauty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Well, I couldn’t exactly help it. I was in awful shape. I couldn’t force myself to do the impossible,” answered Kouenji. (on the island)<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Soaked with sweat, no ordinary high schooler could keep that pace — “He really was exceptional in every way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My, this test will be nothing but troublesome, wouldn’t you say?” Kouenji sniffed.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there isn’t any point to continuing a test that isn’t interesting, is there? Finding a liar is simple.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Phone in hand, fiddles until all four cabin residents get the school notice: the Monkey group’s test has ended; “Of course. And now, I finally have my freedom once again. Adieu.” — tosses the phone and slips into the bathroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration: remarkably perceptive and observant under the clowning — if “simple quiz to find the liar” is true, “he’d probably hit the mark.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The shouting match he mostly ignores.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Hirata Boy,” then the restraint he calls too generous.<span class=\"pg\">p.112, 115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Pointless to include you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p125-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the traitor act on everyone’s lips<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 3  3 5 3 6  the vip name and the starlit hug named dragon vip on hirata s erased screen  four pages later alone on the night deck among the couples  she hugs ayanokoji and flees   huh  oh  ayanokouji kun   yeah  i am  i just couldn t seem to sleep   i m fine  what about you  ayanokouji kun  are you all alone   so we re both alone  i admit  i felt a little ashamed being alone  this makes me feel better   you re already leaving   i see  well  i ll see you tomorrow  good night  ayanokouji kun   i m sorry  i i just felt so lonely  i think  she whispered   small voice after the   pause  the words hit him  like a fighter smacking me right in the jaw   s sorry  i  um i just hugged you so suddenly  ayanokouji kun  good night  she stammered   then quickly scurries away  might be blushing in the dark","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\">Ch.3 §3.5–§3.6: the VIP name and the starlit hug<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.113, p.117–121<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named Dragon VIP on Hirata’s erased screen; four pages later alone on the night deck among the couples, she hugs Ayanokōji and flees.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Huh? Oh, Ayanokouji…kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Yeah, I am. I just couldn’t seem to sleep.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I’m fine. What about you, Ayanokouji-kun? Are you all alone?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “Dragon Group, Kushida-san.” — the VIP position in the extremely well-stacked Dragon group is an enormous advantage and terrifying: “Once they knew her identity, she was at their mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Hirata’s reassurance rides on the three Class D Dragon members being “the best we had to offer” — they would not reveal her.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So we’re both alone? I admit, I felt a little ashamed being alone. This makes me feel better.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re already leaving?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, I’ll see you tomorrow. Good night, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Unexpectedly wraps her arms around his chest — “Even in this cold, I felt the warmth of her body through her jersey.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. I…I just felt so lonely, I think,” she whispered. (small voice after the “…” pause; the words hit him “like a fighter smacking me right in the jaw”)<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-sorry. I, um…I just hugged you so suddenly, Ayanokouji-kun. Good night!” she stammered. (then quickly scurries away; might be blushing in the dark)<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Jersey after a bath, complimentary-shampoo scent that somehow is not that scent; alone among couples; the narrator’s chest tightens imagining a boyfriend.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The night-deck encounter and the hug neither of them can explain.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the invitation inside<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  the confused call message one message in the cabin chaos after kouenji ends the monkey group   i m sorry  things seem really confusing right now  i m going to give you a call   horikita messaged me   printed as her text","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\">Ch.3: the confused-call message<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One message in the cabin chaos after Kouenji ends the Monkey group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’m sorry. Things seem really confusing right now. I’m going to give you a call.” (Horikita messaged me — printed as her text)<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Reaches him in the cabin minutes after the traitor notice; the call itself is not printed on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The recipient of the promise to call.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0: the Blue Ocean briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p125-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hoshinomiya-chie katsuragi-kouhei ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 3  named twice  absent both times two second half mentions   the kouenji shock list and the teachers  dragon roster talk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\">Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.115, p.123<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two second-half mentions — the Kouenji shock list and the teachers’ Dragon roster talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “Katsuragi, Ryuuen, and Ichinose would all be surprised by this” — grouped with them as a leader who had not imagined an early traitor.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Hoshinomiya’s Class C complaint: “If we evaluated the Class … C students properly, another student should’ve been placed into Dragon. But they threw Ryuuen in there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122-123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The teacher who thinks the Dragon pick was a Class C evaluation failure.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The other surprised leader on the same line.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The third name on the surprise list.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the shade meeting and the planted phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou chabashira-sae hoshinomiya-chie mashima-tomonari ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 6  the starlit hug and the teachers  table wanders the dark deck alone  stumbles into kushida among the couples  takes her sudden hug  then overhears chabashira  hoshinomiya and mashima at the vending machines   that voice  kushida   are you alone  i asked  perhaps she was waiting to meet her boyfriend  just imagining that made my chest tighten and ache   i i see  i answered   aren t you cold  i asked   i m getting tired  that was a total lie  i didn t want to sleep in the slightest   good night  kushida   k k ku kushida  wh what s the matter  i squeaked   when she wraps her arms around his chest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.6: the starlit hug and the teachers’ table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.117–124<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wanders the dark deck alone, stumbles into Kushida among the couples, takes her sudden hug, then overhears Chabashira, Hoshinomiya and Mashima at the vending machines.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “That voice… Kushida?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Are you…alone?” I asked. Perhaps she was waiting to meet her boyfriend. Just imagining that made my chest tighten and ache.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I-I see,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Aren’t you cold?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m getting tired.” That was a total lie. I didn’t want to sleep in the slightest.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good night, Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “K-K-Ku…Kushida? Wh-what’s the matter?” I squeaked. (when she wraps her arms around his chest)<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Totally flustered — “I couldn’t understand what was happening” — then stands hand on chest with the warmth still there and cannot return to the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hides and draws nearer to the teachers’ sofa at the first-level vending machines.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Overhears the three homeroom teachers: Hoshinomiya’s date talk, the ten-year grudge, Ichinose deliberately kept out of Dragon and dropped into Rabbit, Ryuuen thrown into Dragon because the Class C grades would not justify another pick, and Sakagami named as part of the Class C evaluation problem.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Files the reconnaissance: “Apparently I was under heavy scrutiny.” — Hoshinomiya was watching him from the island endgame onward.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The starlit encounter and the hug she apologises for.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> At the teachers’ table; the subject of Hoshinomiya’s “Sae-chan” needle.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The Class B homeroom who admits removing Ichinose from Dragon and watching him.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The third teacher; orders Hoshinomiya to stop spying on colleagues’ classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The student Hoshinomiya placed in Rabbit on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–123<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.5: the cabin, the VIP sheet, Kouenji’s exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p125-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p121-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami chabashira-sae mashima-tomonari sakagami ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka hoshinomiya-chie","q":"ch 3  3 6  the class b homeroom at the sofa with chabashira and mashima at the first level vending machines  she drinks whiskey neat  owns the ichinose to rabbit move  and is ordered to stop spying   ah ha ha  we broke up two weeks ago  i m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious  it s just like  see ya later  hoshinomiya sensei said   huh  what are you talking about  what d i do   the answer to  what are you planning  chie    speaker of the question untagged   i m not screwing around or anything  it s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned  ichinose san is number one  however  someone s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone  i determined that she needed a challenge  and besides  rabbits are just so cute  aren t they  the way they hop around  doesn t that suit ichinose san  hoshinomiya sensei asked   oh  are you still talking about what happened ten years ago  i thought that was all water under the bridge   the ten year grudge  speaker untagged in the exchange   recorded under her as the chie being addressed   note  keeps the gap   i genuinely thought that ichinose needed to learn a lesson  so i removed her from the dragon group  you know  by the way  sae chan  i couldn t help but notice you ve been focusing on ayanokouji kun  anyway  it s just a coincidence  coincidence  coincidence  when the island test ended and ayanokouji kun became a kind of leader  you weren t surprised at all  were you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html#sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p121-1\">Ch.3 §3.6: the Class B homeroom at the sofa<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.121–123<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With Chabashira and Mashima at the first-level vending machines, she drinks whiskey neat, owns the Ichinose-to-Rabbit move, and is ordered to stop spying.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakagami.html\">Sakagami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “Ah ha ha! We broke up two weeks ago. I’m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious. It’s just like, see ya later!” Hoshinomiya-sensei said.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “Huh? What are you talking about? What’d I do?” (the answer to “What are you planning, Chie?” — speaker of the question untagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “I’m not screwing around or anything. It’s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned, Ichinose-san is number one. However, someone’s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone. I determined…”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Also addresses Mashima as “Mashima-kun” and is called “Chie” back; most of the date-talk lines are untagged — recorded on the volume attribution list.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pours whiskey into an empty glass and downs it in one gulp — “Must’ve been a drinker.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not screwing around or anything. It’s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned, Ichinose-san is number one. However, someone’s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone. I determined that she needed a challenge. And besides, rabbits are just so cute, aren’t they? The way they hop around. Doesn’t that suit Ichinose-san?” Hoshinomiya-sensei asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, are you still talking about what happened ten years ago? I thought that was all water under the bridge.” (the ten-year grudge, speaker untagged in the exchange — recorded under her as the Chie being addressed; [note] keeps the gap)<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I genuinely thought that Ichinose needed to learn a lesson, so I removed her from the Dragon group. You know? By the way, Sae-chan, I couldn’t help but notice you’ve been focusing on Ayanokouji-kun. Anyway, it’s just a coincidence. Coincidence, coincidence. When the island test ended and Ayanokouji-kun became a kind of leader, you weren’t surprised at all, were you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Agh, it’s like you don’t trust me at all. Well, I’m not the only one to blame. Sakagami-sensei is part of the problem, too. If we evaluated the Class C students properly, another student should’ve been placed into Dragon. But they threw Ryuuen in there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Admits she is watching Ayanokōji — the reconnaissance Ayanokōji files as “Apparently I was under heavy scrutiny.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The Class B student she deliberately kept out of Dragon and put in Rabbit.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Sae-chan” — the focus of her “coincidence” needle.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Ordered to stop spying on colleagues’ classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakagami<\/b> Named as part of the Class C evaluation problem.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The Class C student “they threw” into Dragon.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The student she has been watching since the island endgame.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p125-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the spy order in the brief<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p121-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 3  3 6  the teachers  sofa one of three homeroom instructors on the first level sofa   chabashira with a cocktail  hoshinomiya with whiskey  mashima beside them   while ayanokouji hides and listens   ah ha ha  we broke up two weeks ago  i m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious  it s just like  see ya later  hoshinomiya sensei said   her own tagged line  kept here because the table is the scene   i m not screwing around or anything  it s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned  ichinose san is number one  however  someone s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone  i determined that she needed a challenge  and besides  rabbits are just so cute  aren t they  the way they hop around  doesn t that suit ichinose san  hoshinomiya sensei asked   the ichinose in rabbit admission  tagged   i see  mashima sensei nodded as though convinced of something  however  he then strictly addressed hoshinomiya sensei   there s no rule against this  but i want to be clear  stop spying on other colleagues  classes   both halves tagged to mashima","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p121-1\">Ch.3 §3.6: the teachers’ sofa<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.121–123<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One of three homeroom instructors on the first-level sofa — Chabashira with a cocktail, Hoshinomiya with whiskey, Mashima beside them — while Ayanokouji hides and listens.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Ah ha ha! We broke up two weeks ago. I’m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious. It’s just like, see ya later!” Hoshinomiya-sensei said. (her own tagged line; kept here because the table…”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “I’m not screwing around or anything. It’s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned, Ichinose-san is number one. However, someone’s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone. I determined…”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “I see.” Mashima-sensei nodded as though convinced of something. However, he then strictly addressed Hoshinomiya-sensei. “There’s no rule against this, but I want to be clear. Stop spying on other colleagues’ classes.” (both…”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening lines of the table are untagged in the translation: “You know, it’s been a long time since the three of us all got together.” / “It is what it is. Fate. After bouncing around from one thing to the next, we all chose the teacher’s life.” / “Enough. There’s no point talking about that.” / the Mashima playboy needle / “Chie, what happened to the man you were with?” — only Hoshinomiya’s break-up line and Mashima’s “Relax. I’m not worried about that.” are safely assigned by address or tag; the volume attribution list keeps the rest.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah ha ha! We broke up two weeks ago. I’m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious. It’s just like, see ya later!” Hoshinomiya-sensei said. (her own tagged line; kept here because the table is the scene)<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “What are you planning, Chie?” addresses Hoshinomiya; the speaker is not printed — likely Chabashira or Mashima, not assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not screwing around or anything. It’s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned, Ichinose-san is number one. However, someone’s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone. I determined that she needed a challenge. And besides, rabbits are just so cute, aren’t they? The way they hop around. Doesn’t that suit Ichinose-san?” Hoshinomiya-sensei asked. (the Ichinose-in-Rabbit admission, tagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “We wouldn’t want you to base your judgment on personal grudges.” and the ten-year-bridge exchange sit between untagged speakers at the table.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see.” Mashima-sensei nodded as though convinced of something. However, he then strictly addressed Hoshinomiya-sensei. “There’s no rule against this, but I want to be clear. Stop spying on other colleagues’ classes.” (both halves tagged to Mashima)<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hoshinomiya’s reply names Sakagami over the Class C Dragon pick and says “they threw Ryuuen in there”; the closing “That’s certainly true. This isn’t your average year. The students seem rather special.” is untagged.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The drinking partner she needles and who orders her to stop spying colleagues’ classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The third seat; the strict order lands on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named as the student Hoshinomiya moved out of Dragon.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The student Hoshinomiya admits watching since the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the phrasing he still hears<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p125-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke yukimura-teruhiko karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 4  4 0  the karuizawa brief and the planted phone face to face with horikita on day two  the kouenji traitor act is public  then he asks her for karuizawa intelligence and a recording phone sits under ryuuen s chair   unfortunately  it s the truth  kouenji just ended the test for his group  i said   that s an impossible task  besides  there s nothing i can do about it now  no use crying over spilt milk   it s true that my group is filled with troublesome opponents  but i ve no intention of falling behind  said horikita   reported  her line   i want information on karuizawa   yes  exactly  i nodded   i d like to know more about the people in my group  but it s not easy  i should be able find out whatever i need to about the professor and yukimura  but i m at a complete loss with karuizawa   there s that  but more than that  i can t understand karuizawa s behavior  that s why i m worried   horikita  i don t think it s good to write people off like that   you and karuizawa don t get along at all because you re both willful  so you see her as nothing more than a nuisance  you understand that she may also have strong points  too   but that s still just as superficial as their outside appearance  their innermost thoughts aren t going to be immediately apparent from that  for example  take kushida  ibuki  or even me  there s a difference between a person s outer and inner selves   almost everyone does  they may not be aware of it themselves  you do  too   i still can t really des","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p125-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p125-1\">Ch.4 §4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.125–133<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Face-to-face with Horikita on day two; the Kouenji traitor act is public, then he asks her for Karuizawa intelligence and a recording phone sits under Ryuuen’s chair.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Unfortunately, it’s the truth. Kouenji just ended the test for his group,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “That’s an impossible task. Besides, there’s nothing I can do about it now. No use crying over spilt milk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s true that my group is filled with troublesome opponents, but I’ve no intention of falling behind,” said Horikita. (reported; her line)<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>24 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He files Ichinose and the Class B trio as Hoshinomiya’s spies on him and keeps the subject off Kouenji by changing it.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want information on Karuizawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, exactly.” I nodded. “I’d like to know more about the people in my group, but it’s not easy. I should be able find out whatever I need to about the Professor and Yukimura, but I’m at a complete loss with Karuizawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s that. But more than that, I can’t understand Karuizawa’s behavior. That’s why I’m worried.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita, I don’t think it’s good to write people off like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You and Karuizawa don’t get along at all because you’re both willful, so you see her as nothing more than a nuisance. You understand that she may also have strong points, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Outer/inner self lecture — Kushida, Ibuki, himself as examples; anyone can have a secret self, Horikita included (her brother, tagged by narration).<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But that’s still just as superficial as their outside appearance. Their innermost thoughts aren’t going to be immediately apparent from that. For example, take Kushida, Ibuki, or even me. There’s a difference between a person’s outer and inner selves.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Almost everyone does. They may not be aware of it themselves. You do, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I still can’t really describe it, but so far I’d say it’s her ability to assume control. She can take the initiative. In fact, her position in Class D is unshakeable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> In the Rabbit group that part of Karuizawa stayed hidden — the reason he needs her true nature fast.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, you two. Having yourselves a nice date in the shade? Let me in on the fun.” (Ryuuen’s approach, reported)<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Lets Ryuuen sit in and listen; works the phone under the chair with Horikita without commenting on it.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Reads Ryuuen’s “fundamentals” speech as the same rule-logic as midterms and the island test — he must have noticed the VIP-class pattern.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> If Ryuuen’s claim holds, he already has three VIPs and probably every class’s — “a quiz where you could turn the page over and find the answer written on the back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flips Ryuuen off after the parting; leaves the recording phone alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Easy for you to say. It’s not like I can find them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re not expecting too much, I’ll do what I can,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Plans to mine Hirata for Dragon-group detail instead of Horikita — a different perspective.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Room scene: answers the VIP probe, trades mutual denial, notes Yukimura warming up while he fakes a chameleon’s sociability.<span class=\"pg\">p.131-133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if I did deny it and said you’re wrong, what’s the point in checking?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Unfortunately, I’m not the VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not the VIP. Can I believe that you’re not the VIP, Yukimura?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Yukimura reports Karuizawa’s denial of the VIP role; Ayanokōji does not press it.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.6: the starlit hug and the teachers’ table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the deck VIP exchange<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p125-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke karuizawa-kei ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune","q":"ch 4  4 0  the karuizawa brief and the planted phone she meets ayanokoji face to face about kouenji s traitor exit  then argues karuizawa s worth while ryuuen s recording phone sits under his chair   you re joking  right   are you an idiot  why didn t you stop him  wasn t that your responsibility as his roommate  she asked   when i see him next time  i ll reprimand him myself  i ll make him beg for mercy   you already know that s pointless  right  he won t listen  he ll just confuse you and waste your time  it ll be a headache  for the time being  we should concentrate on our own groups   you want to talk to me about karuizawa   i turned her down  though  you know that  i have no interest in karuizawa san  if you want information on her  why not talk to hirata kun  if he s helping you  you ll be able to contact her easily   do you think she s the vip  is that what you re worried about  horikita asked   well  isn t that none of your business  besides  her behavior isn t logical  i think it s a waste of time  she countered   write them off  what are you talking about   she has strong points  i can t really imagine any  isn t she just flawed   so karuizawa has some secret self   i m still not entirely convinced  however  i imagine you ll learn more about her by spending time together  she said   so  what are karuizawa san s good points  horikita asked   okay  let s say for the sake of argument that you re right  and she has that ability  what do you intend to do  are you thinkin","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p125-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p125-1\">Ch.4 §4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.125–133<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She meets Ayanokōji face-to-face about Kouenji’s traitor exit, then argues Karuizawa’s worth while Ryuuen’s recording phone sits under his chair.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You’re joking, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Are you an idiot? Why didn’t you stop him? Wasn’t that your responsibility as his roommate?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “When I see him next time, I’ll reprimand him myself. I’ll make him beg for mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You already know that’s pointless, right? He won’t listen. He’ll just confuse you and waste your time. It’ll be a headache. For the time being, we should concentrate on our own groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Blames Ayanokōji as Kouenji’s roommate; accepts the roommate-can’t-stop-him answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You want to talk to me about Karuizawa?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I turned her down, though. You know that. I have no interest in Karuizawa-san. If you want information on her, why not talk to Hirata-kun? If he’s helping you, you’ll be able to contact her easily.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think she’s the VIP? Is that what you’re worried about?” Horikita asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, isn’t that none of your business? Besides, her behavior isn’t logical. I think it’s a waste of time,” she countered.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Write them off? What are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She has strong points? I can’t really imagine any. Isn’t she just flawed?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Refuses the lunch invite history, calls her illogical, then listens to the outer/inner-self lecture and concedes time-together may help.<span class=\"pg\">p.126-127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So Karuizawa has some secret self?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m still not entirely convinced. However, I imagine you’ll learn more about her by spending time together,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, what are Karuizawa-san’s good points?” Horikita asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. Let’s say for the sake of argument that you’re right, and she has that ability. What do you intend to do? Are you thinking of making her your ally, too?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The shade meeting: refuses to share plans, calls his no-support claim out, snaps at the phone-seizure idea, then works the planted-phone cue with Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like you have an awful lot of free time. Not that I care, but there’s nothing for you here,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whatever my plans may be, I’ve no intention of telling you,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s an interesting thing to say. Are you saying that you know who the VIP is?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I wouldn’t. You don’t have any support like Ichinose-san and Katsuragi-kun do. You only have enemies. I can’t imagine you have reliable information,” she countered.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Anyone could think of that. But are they going to answer honestly? If the school has a rule that guarantees your anonymity, all they need to do is lie and gain 500,000 points, right?” Horikita countered.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Where someone can’t lie?”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you insane? The school doesn’t allow that. If you were discovered, you’d be expelled,” snapped Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. But you haven’t got the answer yet. If you had, you would’ve sent an email to the school immediately,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t know when someone else is going to figure it out. You shouldn’t be so laid-back,” Horikita snapped.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ryuuen-kun. While you’re here, I’d like to ask you something. The test ended for the Monkey group yesterday. What do you think about that?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Probes Ryuuen on the Monkey-group early end; he waves it off as small fry.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know how much of what he said is true,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Spots the silent recording phone under Ryuuen’s chair; texts Ayanokōji the caution line.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> If that phone is his, we probably shouldn’t say anything careless. (chat message, p.130)<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have to wonder. I can’t say I’m 100% sure. But…there’s a possibility. I don’t think we can keep up this test much longer, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve got a lot of work for you to do. I need you to find the group’s VIP as soon as possible,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t expect too much from you. I just want information about the Rabbit group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Ryuuen’s phone plant as reason to keep talking carefully; still assigns Ayanokōji the Rabbit VIP hunt as cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.130-131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the confused-call message<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the night meet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p125-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami hoshinomiya-chie","q":"ch 4  4 0  the spy order in the brief named only as the teacher who secretly sent ichinose and the class b trio to watch ayanokoji   his private inventory of problems for the day","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p125-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html#sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p125-1\">Ch.4 §4.0: the spy order in the brief<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as the teacher who secretly sent Ichinose and the Class B trio to watch Ayanokōji — his private inventory of problems for the day.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The Class B three in the Rabbit group are filed as her agents on him, not as random group-mates.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence this range; the row records the brief’s attribution of the spy order.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p121-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.6: the Class B homeroom at the sofa<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p167-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the drunk interruption<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p125-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 4  4 0  the traitor act on everyone s lips the chapter opens on the aftermath of his monkey group traitor submission   the classes are in an uproar and horikita wants ayanokoji to answer for it as roommate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p125-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p125-1\">Ch.4 §4.0: the traitor act on everyone’s lips<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.125–130<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The chapter opens on the aftermath of his Monkey-group traitor submission — the classes are in an uproar and Horikita wants Ayanokōji to answer for it as roommate.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Kouenji’s treasonous act has circulated around the ship; the classes were in an uproar.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She blames the roommate and vows to reprimand him herself; the “make him beg for mercy” line is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The roommate who says there is nothing he can do now — no use crying over spilt milk.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryuuen waves off the Monkey-group end as small fry when Horikita asks.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No direct appearance in this range; every row is other people reporting the act.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.5: push-ups, refusal, and the Monkey exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p237-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the automated calibration and the saviour<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p126-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko sotomura-hideo ichinose-honami machida-kouji manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 4  4 0 4 1  the lunch history and the machida seat named across the horikita brief as the person ayanokoji needs  then first on scene in the afternoon rabbit room   disgust  a rinocchi call  a vip check  and a seat by machida   oh hi  rinocchi  how are things with you right now  me  ah  things here suck so bad  like  i m seriously fed up with everything  said karuizawa   that reminds me  so  are you the vip  it seems like yukimura kun and that soto kun aren t  said karuizawa   ah  okay  that s fine   huh  you said you re not  didn t you   thank you  machida kun  she replied","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p126-1\">Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the lunch history and the Machida seat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.126–137<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named across the Horikita brief as the person Ayanokōji needs, then first on scene in the afternoon Rabbit room — disgust, a Rinocchi call, a VIP check, and a seat by Machida.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Oh hi, Rinocchi? How are things with you right now? Me? Ah, things here suck so bad. Like, I’m seriously fed up with everything,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “That reminds me. So, are you the VIP? It seems like…Yukimura-kun and that Soto…kun aren’t,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ah, okay. That’s fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The rejected lunch invite after the island test is the fact Ayanokōji uses; Horikita says she has no interest in her.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Averts her eyes the moment she sees him, moves as far away as she can, and fiddles with her phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The most bothersome dislike — no reason to improve, pure instinct, no breakthrough (his read of the room).<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Overheard only by him: she wove joy and melancholy in one call — the skillful performance of misery for a friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Cites his and Sotomura’s denials; can’t quite say Sotomura’s name.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “that Soto…kun” — the name she won’t finish.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? You said you’re not, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Unlike Yukimura she doesn’t double-check; she takes the denial at face value — noted as useful for his assessment of her.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Ichinose greets her; she stays on the phone and doesn’t respond.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Crosses the room to sit beside Machida as a defensive measure against Manabe; accepts his protection offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you, Machida-kun,” she replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The Class C girls’ side of the room is why the Machida seat is the correct decision (his read).<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p107-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: the background-character file<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2–4.4: the seat, the stairwell, the breakup<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ch 4  4 0  not at the shade meeting named once as absent from ryuuen s side when he drops into the horikita conversation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\">Ch.4 §4.0: not at the shade meeting<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.128<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as absent from Ryuuen’s side when he drops into the Horikita conversation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “He wasn’t with Ibuki, apparently” — the usual pair is split for this scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue and no further presence in the range.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the absent buffer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 4  4 0  the shade meeting and the planted phone he drops into horikita and ayanokoji s shade conversation  claims class c can win by rule logic  and leaves a silent recording phone under his own chair   hey  you two  having yourselves a nice date in the shade  let me in on the fun   that s for me to decide  well then  have you decided how to find the vip  he asked   i ve already started to discover the vip s identity  would you believe me if i told you that   well  you re right that i m not a professional friend collector  but making friends has nothing to do with whether or not i can gather information   unfortunately for you  i ve already gotten a handle on the fundamentals of this test  depending on how things go  class c will win by an overwhelming majority   it s an extremely simple matter  all you need to do is find out what   class the vip is from  then  your next move is to analyze the group  said ryuuen   you just have to make sure it s a situation where someone can t lie  he said   i take everyone s cell phones  so if someone lies to me  all i have to do is check everyone s email  one by one  said ryuuen   it s not really a problem at all  actually  i m here because it s not a problem  do you get what i mean   looks like you finally understand   maybe i m just playing around   now  then  suppose i m about to reach checkmate  he said   i don t think about it at all  i don t really care about small fry  see you again  suzune","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\">Ch.4 §4.0: the shade meeting and the planted phone<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.128–131<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He drops into Horikita and Ayanokōji’s shade conversation, claims Class C can win by rule-logic, and leaves a silent recording phone under his own chair.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Hey, you two. Having yourselves a nice date in the shade? Let me in on the fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “That’s for me to decide. Well then, have you decided how to find the VIP?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I’ve already started to discover the VIP’s identity. Would you believe me if I told you that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, you’re right that I’m not a professional friend-collector, but making friends has nothing to do with whether or not I can gather information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately for you, I’ve already gotten a handle on the fundamentals of this test. Depending on how things go, Class C will win by an overwhelming majority.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s an extremely simple matter. All you need to do is find out what … class the VIP is from. Then, your next move is to analyze the group,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just have to make sure it’s a situation where someone can’t lie,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I take everyone’s cell phones. So if someone lies to me, all I have to do is check everyone’s email, one by one,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not really a problem at all, actually. I’m here because it’s not a problem. Do you get what I mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Brute-force phone seizure as a Class C method — no complaints means consent; narration reads it as operating within the rules and as three VIPs already identified.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you finally understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe I’m just playing around?”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now, then. Suppose I’m about to reach checkmate?” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think about it at all. I don’t really care about small fry. See you again, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Dismisses the Monkey-group early end as small fry.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Leaves; a silent phone set to record audio stays under his chair with the chat line “Sorry for yesterday!”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Parting “See you again, Suzune” — first-name basis, reported.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.0: the frontal assault still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p131-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 4  4 0 4 1  the absent roommate and the corridor pass named as the better source on dragon group detail while ayanokoji walks back to an empty room  then passes ayanokoji in the dragon doorway on day two","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p131-1\">Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the absent roommate and the corridor pass<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.131–144<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the better source on Dragon-group detail while Ayanokōji walks back to an empty room, then passes Ayanokōji in the Dragon doorway on day two.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The planned mining target — “Hirata would likely approach this test from a different perspective than Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Set up as the alternate Dragon-group lens beside her.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> brief exchanged looks as they pass in the doorway — no line.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Leaves the room with her before the three-way opens to Ichinose and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.5: the trusted conduit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p170-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: the farce ends at the vending machine<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p131-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"sotomura-hideo karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 4  4 0  the roommate s vip probe alone in the room looking grave  he rants about the group draw rumor  then runs the mutual vip denial with ayanokoji   for crying out loud  why did we get stuck with this group  why am i partnered with karuizawa and sotomura  we can t win  he mumbled   didn t you hear  there s a rumor going around saying that they use guidelines to create the groups  when i heard that all the superior students got grouped into the dragon group  i knew it was true  he answered   ayanokouji  you aren t the vip  are you  he asked   cooperation is vital in this test  we need to adhere to that  if we cooperate  we won t lose   are you sure  you re not being selfish and trying to hoard points  are you   yes  of course you can  i m not the vip  neither is sotomura  by the way","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p131-1\">Ch.4 §4.0: the roommate’s VIP probe<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.131–133<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Alone in the room looking grave; he rants about the group-draw rumor, then runs the mutual VIP denial with Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “For crying out loud, why did we get stuck with this group? Why am I partnered with Karuizawa and Sotomura? We can’t win,” he mumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Didn’t you hear? There’s a rumor going around saying that they use guidelines to create the groups. When I heard that all the superior students got grouped into the Dragon group, I knew it was true,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Ayanokouji. You aren’t the VIP, are you?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Treats the Dragon “best of the best” roster as proof the draw was fixed; dissatisfied at Rabbit’s middle placement; academic ability not inferior to Hirata or Horikita (narration).<span class=\"pg\">p.131-132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cooperation is vital in this test. We need to adhere to that. If we cooperate, we won’t lose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you sure? You’re not being selfish and trying to hoard points, are you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, of course you can. I’m not the VIP. Neither is Sotomura, by the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Vouches Sotomura is not the VIP without being asked for proof.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Reports her VIP denial and adds he may not believe it — disdain as the standing attitude.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doubts everyone as a rule; satisfied for the time being and settles into sighs while Ayanokōji naps.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.5: strategy talk and the Kouenji explosion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the stairwell<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p132-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami hamaguchi-tetsuya sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 4  4 0 4 1  the vip alibi and the card heat named as yukimura s rabbit group partner in the room rant  then one of the five at ichinose s card table where the professor fires up and cools off   i shall play as well  i am currently at liberty  said the professor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p132-1\">Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the VIP alibi and the card heat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.132–139<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as Yukimura’s Rabbit-group partner in the room rant, then one of the five at Ichinose’s card table where the Professor fires up and cools off.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “I shall play as well. I am currently at liberty,” said the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Yukimura vouches he is not the VIP in the same breath as his own denial — “Neither is Sotomura, by the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The partner pair Yukimura names as unwinnable: “Why am I partnered with Karuizawa and Sotomura?”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Huge otaku but games fire him up — “Once more!” mid-hand; calms the moment the game ends; Ichinose reads the pattern as one of the group’s tells.<span class=\"pg\">p.138-139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> His heat and cool-down are exactly the characteristic she was collecting from the five-player hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Both Class B-adjacent players in the five with Ichinose and Ayanokōji — Hamaguchi focused on the endgame, the Professor on the next hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: hunger and the Sunrise gag<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the chair and the exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p137-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hamaguchi-tetsuya ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune ichinose-honami","q":"ch 4  4 1  cards  the castle gate  and the deck pledge arrives with the class b trio  proposes cards over silence  walks ayanokoji to katsuragi  sits in on the ryuuen three way  and ends on the deck telling him she is not the vip   you two sure are early  said ichinose   now then  i m sure we all discussed this amongst ourselves last night  but i think we should try and find the vips after all  said ichinose   i don t think that s true  though  it s a problem of trust  that s why today  i d like us all to play cards together  of course  i won t force anyone to participate  only jump in if you want to  said ichinose   you can say it s stupid  but if you give it a try you might like it  besides  spending an hour in complete silence sounds awfully boring  why not kill some time   five people  then  well  i thought we could play daifugo  but does anyone here not know the rules  asked ichinose   well  i suppose i ll be going now  said ichinose   i can t let class a just get away from us like this   hmm  sure  that s fine with me  do you want to talk to katsuragi kun  too  ayanokouji  asked ichinose   ah  okay  well then  let s go together  see you later  hamaguchi kun  said ichinose   looks like they re really taking their time  said ichinose   i think i know what you re planning  katsuragi kun  you ordered your classmates to refuse to participate in discussions  yes  would you possibly reconsider  we need communication to get through this test  after all   i have my own situation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p137-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: cards, the castle gate, and the deck pledge<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.137–151<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives with the Class B trio, proposes cards over silence, walks Ayanokōji to Katsuragi, sits in on the Ryuuen three-way, and ends on the deck telling him she is not the VIP.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “You two sure are early,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Now then. I’m sure we all discussed this amongst ourselves last night, but I think we should try and find the VIPs after all,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “I don’t think that’s true, though. It’s a problem of trust. That’s why today, I’d like us all to play cards together. Of course, I won’t force anyone to participate. Only jump in if you want to,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>48 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cards as a trust probe: she plays opponents’ hands, watches the Professor fire up and cool off, and uses the hour to learn how the group talks — talking was useless, the game wasn’t.<span class=\"pg\">p.137-139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can say it’s stupid, but if you give it a try you might like it. Besides, spending an hour in complete silence sounds awfully boring. Why not kill some time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Five people, then. Well, I thought we could play Daifugō, but does anyone here not know the rules?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Includes him in the five; he asks where she’s going when she leaves for Katsuragi; she waves him off with a “see you later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138-140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Lets him tag along to Katsuragi without wariness — curiosity, not suspicion; later walks him to the deck alone with the VIP pledge.<span class=\"pg\">p.139-141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose I’ll be going now,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t let Class A just get away from us like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm? Sure, that’s fine with me. Do you want to talk to Katsuragi-kun, too, Ayanokouji?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, okay. Well then, let’s go together. See you later, Hamaguchi-kun,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The castle-gate interview: she asks him to reopen discussion, takes the “ears are going to fall off” brush-off, and leaves understanding there will be no budging.<span class=\"pg\">p.140-143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like they’re really taking their time,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think I know what you’re planning, Katsuragi-kun. You ordered your classmates to refuse to participate in discussions, yes? Would you possibly reconsider? We need communication to get through this test, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have my own situation to deal with. Katsuragi-kun. I don’t think forcing people to be quiet is a good strategy. Would you reconsider?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But, Katsuragi-kun, your idea is basically a rejection of the test itself,” countered Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If this test were a direct competition between the classes, sure. I’d agree. But in this test, when all the classes are blended together, do you really think that’s right?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So. Like the old saying goes, an immovable object meets an irresistible force?” Ichinose wore a wry, pained smile as she rubbed the back of her head.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. This is a test,” answered Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm…I wonder. Well, I can’t really consider things from Class A’s perspective. If you’re being chased, I imagine it would be better to have experience with chasing. Always running is pretty tough, isn’t it?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> In response, Ichinose smiled softly. “I’m sorry for taking up your time. I think I understand now. Understand your thoughts and ideas, I mean,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This test is easier if you’re playing defense. I guess I’ll have to do even more,” she mused.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Waits outside for him with Ayanokōji; notes his type doesn’t take the spotlight.<span class=\"pg\">p.143-144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The three-way: thanks him for the group-formation tip instead of showing shock, refuses the Class B–C contract on trust grounds, and names the Class B harm his methods have already caused.<span class=\"pg\">p.144-149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Ayanokouji-kun, what are you doing here? Are you waiting for Horikita-san?” asked Kushida. (Kushida’s line, tagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re waiting for Horikita-san and Kanzaki-kun. Are they still talking?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh no, it’s all right. If they’re still in the middle of something, we can wait.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a rather interesting group. I want to know what you’re all talking about, especially since the required hour is up,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, Ryuuen-kun. You know that we can’t understand the school’s strategies. We’re just doing our best with the information we have and the situation we were placed into. But it sounds like you think there’s a reasoning behind the group formations. Do you think the school had some kind of plan in mind?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm thanks for unexpected information instead of shock — Ryuuen’s face changes; both sides gain a read.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A proposal? I suppose I’ll hear you out. What is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It sounds like a pretty bold idea, but I don’t think it’s realistic. How do we know for sure that you have all the Class C VIPs, Ryuuen-kun?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your thinking is solid, Horikita-san. If we don’t have a guarantee that Ryuuen-kun is telling the truth, then this is meaningless,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re giving me far too much credit. People don’t have that much trust in me. Besides, your proposal is high risk, low return. I can’t agree to it,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san rejected your proposal. Therefore, this plan is off to a bad start,” added Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Staying put is also a trap: if she betrays Class D here she is branded a traitor for the rest of high school — his read of why the refusal costs her nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.148-149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, Ryuuen-kun. But you’ve hurt people in Class B with your actions. Even if it’s possible for us to get more points, I can’t ally with you on that reason alone,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whew. I guess he saw through me,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Calls Ryuuen a snake after Horikita’s crack-under-pressure line; asks her the trust-between-classes question; ends “I was right to choose your side.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149-151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ryuuen might think himself a dragon, but he’s really a snake. He’s so tenacious that when he finds his prey, he’ll go to any lengths to bring it down. But don’t you have it worse than me right now, Horikita-san? Ryuuen-kun is naturally wary of Class A, after all. He probably thinks that Class B will one day be his enemy, too. But right now, he’s got you in his sights,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, Ayanokouji-kun. I wanted to ask you something. Do you think this test will create trust between people of different classes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Just like I’d expect of you, Horikita-san. You understand this test very well. Ryuuen-kun’s just full of hot air. I was right to choose your side.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Ryuuen-kun’s plan will fail. It’s probably best not to worry about it. The real problem is Katsuragi-kun’s iron fortress strategy. What do you think about it now that you’ve spoken to him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I think it’s hopeless, too. We have no choice but to find a different way,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand what Horikita-san said earlier, but I think there’s still room for cooperation,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I was surprised when Class A distanced themselves, but I think we have a chance. But to pull it off, we might have to reveal everything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This entire test boils down to finding the VIP. That’s the point, right? So if we play things by the book, we increase our chances by narrowing down the list and finding out who isn’t the target. So, I’ll tell you right now: I’m not the VIP. But I intend to find them and lead my group to victory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You might think that if I’m the target, I could just be hiding my identity. But Ayanokouji-kun, the reason I’m not is simple. Everything I do is for the sake of Class B,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Public VIP denial without showing the phone — his read: a fraction of doubt left, trust would need the screen; she doesn’t offer it.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It must sound strange,” said Ichinose, seemingly a little dissatisfied with my silence.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: bystander, closer, and the Machida bait<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the deck VIP exchange<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p137-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho machida-kouji","q":"ch 4  4 1  the protection offer karuizawa crosses to his class a corner  he accepts the seat and offers cover for the hour   don t worry  if anything happens  i ll help you  said machida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html#sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p137-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the protection offer<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.137<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Karuizawa crosses to his Class A corner; he accepts the seat and offers cover for the hour.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “Don’t worry. If anything happens, I’ll help you,” said Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Takes her dependence on him as something to be conscious of; the cute-girl protection logic is the narrator’s read, not a spoken line.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn’t participate in the discussion but his presence weighs on the room — Class A’s distance plus Machida in the circle is the power imbalance of the hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> His presence is what keeps the Class C girls from hounding her (the seat’s whole point).<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: the fair intervention and the second-gathering snicker<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the seat arbitration<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p137-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei machida-kouji manabe-shiho","q":"ch 4  4 1  the threat across the room named as the reason karuizawa seats herself beside machida   the class c girls  side has no one who can answer machida  and manabe is the hound to avoid","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p137-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the threat across the room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.137<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the reason Karuizawa seats herself beside Machida — the Class C girls’ side has no one who can answer Machida, and Manabe is the hound to avoid.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The defensive move is measured against her; had Karuizawa sat with a weak link, Manabe and the others could have hounded her (his read).<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The power imbalance: Manabe’s group versus Machida in the circle.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No line in this range; presence is narrated through the seating logic.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p110-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: the elevator fuse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the seat and the stairwell<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p138-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami sotomura-hideo hamaguchi-tetsuya","q":"ch 4  4 1  the card table and the corridor one of ichinose s five for daifugo and old maid  asks where she s going when the hour ends and watches her leave with ayanokoji   where are you going  asked hamaguchi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p138-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html#sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p138-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the card table and the corridor<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.138–140<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One of Ichinose’s five for Daifugō and Old Maid; asks where she’s going when the hour ends and watches her leave with Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “Where are you going?” asked Hamaguchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Plays under her deal; “Where are you going?” then nods them off — Class B’s mutual-respect pattern, set against Katsuragi and Ryuuen’s subject relationships (his read of the group).<span class=\"pg\">p.138-140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Focused on the endgame; gets worked up at times like the Professor, but Ichinose tags him as the endgame player of the five.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The other Class B-side regular at the table with the Professor’s “Once more!” energy.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: the Class B off-switch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p153-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the second denial<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p140-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 4  4 1  the castle gate holds leaves the dragon room into ichinose s ambush  refuses to reopen discussion for the fourth time running and walks away with the strategy intact   ichinose  what are you doing here   well  the testing period is three days long  i have several minutes available   that s extremely reasonable  but i ve heard this question so many times that i feel like my ears are going to fall off  unfortunately  ichinose  you ve wasted your time  said katsuragi   the answer will always be the same  i developed that strategy to win  my reasons are good  you think this test requires communication  that s why you don t agree with me  but you re wrong  this test is about thinking  if you miss that  it s a big problem  so  in keeping with the theme of the test  i ve decided to stifle discussion   what i ve said might sound bad  but it s not  i m looking out for my class  looking for ways to not only preserve our standing in this test  but in tests to come  do you agree that there s nothing wrong with me protecting my class   any further discussion is meaningless  ichinose  you can t change my mind  he said   do you still intend to fight  asked katsuragi   i m sorry  but the result s a foregone conclusion  if class a doesn t participate  there s not much you can do  there shouldn t be any way for you to win  said katsuragi   i want to ask you one thing  if you were class a s leader  what would you do  wouldn t you implement the same strategy  asked katsuragi   in my o","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p140-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the castle gate holds<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.140–143<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaves the Dragon room into Ichinose’s ambush; refuses to reopen discussion for the fourth time running and walks away with the strategy intact.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “Ichinose? What are you doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “Well, the testing period is three days long. I have several minutes available.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “That’s extremely reasonable. But I’ve heard this question so many times that I feel like my ears are going to fall off. Unfortunately, Ichinose, you’ve wasted your time,” said Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn’t ignore her — “looked happy to engage” with Class B’s leader; waves the other Class A students on and stays alone with the pair.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The answer will always be the same. I developed that strategy to win. My reasons are good. You think this test requires communication. That’s why you don’t agree with me, but you’re wrong. This test is about thinking. If you miss that, it’s a big problem. So, in keeping with the theme of the test, I’ve decided to stifle discussion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The no-disclosure strategy is re-stated as deliberate: thinking over talking, four outcomes, any one of them legitimate.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What I’ve said might sound bad, but it’s not. I’m looking out for my class, looking for ways to not only preserve our standing in this test, but in tests to come. Do you agree that there’s nothing wrong with me protecting my class?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Any further discussion is meaningless, Ichinose. You can’t change my mind,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you still intend to fight?” asked Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but the result’s a foregone conclusion. If Class A doesn’t participate, there’s not much you can do. There shouldn’t be any way for you to win,” said Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want to ask you one thing. If you were Class A’s leader, what would you do? Wouldn’t you implement the same strategy?” asked Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In my opinion, if you were standing in my position, you would’ve come up with the same strategy I did. If it’s to protect my class, I don’t particularly mind being criticized by others.” Katsuragi locked eyes with Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The immovable-object exchange; closes his eyes, crosses his arms, re-meets her gaze — no inch given before the exam ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.140-143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Still the man Ichinose came to counter; no mention of Ryuuen in this exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the calm image and the surprise reaction<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.0: the iron fortress still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p143-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 4  4 1  the dragon deadlock still inside the dragon room with horikita and ryuuen when ichinose and ayanokoji are waved in  the three way holds until ryuuen leaves   haven t you ever dreamed of rising up to class b  asked kanzaki   i said this yesterday  but katsuragi is completely unapproachable  he ll talk to you  but he won t give an inch  i doubt he ll change his mind before the exam ends  at this point  i think all of class a is taking the same stance  don t you  asked kanzaki","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p143-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p143-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the Dragon deadlock<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.143–150<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still inside the Dragon room with Horikita and Ryuuen when Ichinose and Ayanokōji are waved in; the three-way holds until Ryuuen leaves.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Haven’t you ever dreamed of rising up to Class B?” asked Kanzaki.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “I said this yesterday, but Katsuragi is completely unapproachable. He’ll talk to you, but he won’t give an inch. I doubt he’ll change his mind before the exam ends. At this point, I think all of Class A is taking the same…”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named as the one who should have taken his seat in the group — Ryuuen’s jab that she ended up elsewhere instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Kanzaki-kun isn’t the type to take the spotlight” — Ichinose’s read of why Class A’s refusal doesn’t land on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> One of the three holding the deadlock; adds the Class B–C doubt line when Ryuuen pushes the two-class version.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Names Katsuragi as completely unapproachable to her face — the shared Class A read after the interview.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I said this yesterday, but Katsuragi is completely unapproachable. He’ll talk to you, but he won’t give an inch. I doubt he’ll change his mind before the exam ends. At this point, I think all of Class A is taking the same stance. Don’t you?” asked Kanzaki.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Carries the no-inch finding out of the room with Ichinose’s interview as the evidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.143,150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: named in the VIP arithmetic<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p144-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 4  4 1  the invitation inside spots ayanokoji and ichinose in the dragon corridor  waves them into the three way  then exits when ryuuen leaves with  my friends are calling me   huh  ayanokouji kun  what are you doing here  are you waiting for horikita san  asked kushida   oh  ichinose san  hello  now  this is odd  well  i should say i didn t expect to see the two of you together  said kushida   oh  those two  they re still discussing things with ryuuen kun right now  maybe you could step inside  kushida gestured toward the door  as if inviting us in   oh  i think it s fine  besides  the test period is only one hour  any time after that  we re free to come and go as we please  besides  they may not be talking about the test   ah  i should be going  my friends are calling me  said kushida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p144-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the invitation inside<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.144–149<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spots Ayanokōji and Ichinose in the Dragon corridor, waves them into the three-way, then exits when Ryuuen leaves with “My friends are calling me.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Huh? Ayanokouji-kun, what are you doing here? Are you waiting for Horikita-san?” asked Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Oh! Ichinose-san! Hello. Now, this is odd. Well, I should say I didn’t expect to see the two of you together,” said Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Oh, those two. They’re still discussing things with Ryuuen-kun right now. Maybe you could step inside?” Kushida gestured toward the door, as if inviting us in.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Surprised Ayanokōji and Class B’s leader know each other — she didn’t know.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He stiffens at her approach, remembering yesterday’s scene; she has gone back to her usual self as though nothing changed.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, I think it’s fine. Besides, the test period is only one hour. Any time after that, we’re free to come and go as we please. Besides, they may not be talking about the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, I should be going. My friends are calling me,” said Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The Ryuuen conversation she reports is the reason she opens the door — “they may not be talking about the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Named in the corridor as the person Ayanokōji is waiting for; the excuse Ichinose accepts.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.5–§3.6: the VIP name and the starlit hug<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p185-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.5: the fallback contact<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p152-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hamaguchi-tetsuya yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 4  4 1  the deck vip exchange ends the deck walk with ichinose by denying his own vip role and vouching only for yukimura   karuizawa and sotomura left unsaid on purpose   i m not the vip  neither is yukimura  i can say that with absolutely certainty  unfortunately  i don t really know about karuizawa or the professor err  i mean  sotomura  it s not clear yet  personally  i agree with you on principle   you haven t checked with your own class yet  i observed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p152-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the deck VIP exchange<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.152–154<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ends the deck walk with Ichinose by denying his own VIP role and vouching only for Yukimura — Karuizawa and Sotomura left unsaid on purpose.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m not the VIP. Neither is Yukimura, I can say that with absolutely certainty. Unfortunately, I don’t really know about Karuizawa or the Professor…err, I mean, Sotomura. It’s not clear yet. Personally, I agree with you on…”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You haven’t checked with your own class yet,” I observed.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not the VIP. Neither is Yukimura, I can say that with absolutely certainty. Unfortunately, I don’t really know about Karuizawa or the Professor…err, I mean, Sotomura. It’s not clear yet. Personally, I agree with you on principle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Withholds Yukimura’s Karuizawa/Sotomura alibis — careless confirmation could cost Ichinose’s trust if either were the VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Accepts her “honest as much as possible” framing; decides the trap risk is smaller than the relationship cost of refusing.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Watches him take the confirmation and join the four non-VIP core — ten suspects left.<span class=\"pg\">p.152-154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Counts four cleared (himself, Ichinose, Hamaguchi, Yukimura) against ten remaining; the VIP will be concealing under pressure.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The alibi he keeps half-said — Yukimura’s denials accepted through attitude, not passed on wholesale.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p125-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: the Sugimura bargain<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p152-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hamaguchi-tetsuya ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ch 4  4 1  the deck vip exchange presses her own honesty after the pledge  accepts his partial answer  then pulls hamaguchi in without telling class b about the class d deal   i m not lying  i think that lying might be necessary in competition  but i like to be honest as much as possible  i do want my class to win  fair and square   ah  you don t have to tell me anything if you don t want to  ayanokouji kun  i just wanted to explain my feelings  i thought if i told you  things might be easier   even if perfect cooperation is impossible  trying to form solid relationships is no bad thing  if i don t answer now  it might hurt our relationship down the line   no  no  i don t think so  she sounded flustered  but this wasn t the time to hide   s sorry  it seems like i forced your answer  said ichinose   hey  hamaguchi kun  got a minute  asked ichinose   i prefer to let my classmates act autonomously  there are people in my class who want points  it s not like i can arbitrarily transfer the vip s rights to myself  said ichinose   this might sound impertinent  but i ll check with the remaining person myself  if that person answers me honestly  i ll tell you later  ayanokouji kun  she said   oh  don t worry  as long as i just have your cooperation  ayanokouji kun  i m happy  answered ichinose   well  isn t the point of this test for us to figure it out  asked ichinose","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p152-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the deck VIP exchange<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.152–154<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Presses her own honesty after the pledge, accepts his partial answer, then pulls Hamaguchi in without telling Class B about the Class D deal.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “I’m not lying. I think that lying might be necessary in competition, but I like to be honest as much as possible. I do want my class to win, fair and square.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Ah, you don’t have to tell me anything if you don’t want to, Ayanokouji-kun. I just wanted to explain my feelings. I thought if I told you, things might be easier.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Even if perfect cooperation is impossible, trying to form solid relationships is no bad thing. If I don’t answer now, it might hurt our relationship down the line.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, no, I don’t think so.” She sounded flustered, but this wasn’t the time to hide.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-sorry. It seems like I forced your answer,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Lowers her head as if guilty — his read: she will be the one owed an apology someday.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Hamaguchi-kun. Got a minute?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Fills him in but conceals the Class D cooperation — surprising for her character; he joins on Ayanokōji’s word alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.152-153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I prefer to let my classmates act autonomously. There are people in my class who want points. It’s not like I can arbitrarily transfer the VIP’s rights to myself,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This might sound impertinent, but I’ll check with the remaining person myself. If that person answers me honestly, I’ll tell you later, Ayanokouji-kun,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, don’t worry. As long as I just have your cooperation, Ayanokouji-kun, I’m happy,” answered Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Accepts his uneven disclosure without demanding Class D’s full hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, isn’t the point of this test for us to figure it out?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her move turns the once-hopeless hour into extraction from people who want to hide — his read of the shift.<span class=\"pg\">p.153-154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p137-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: cards, the castle gate, and the deck pledge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: cards, the dream question, the show<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p153-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka hamaguchi-tetsuya","q":"ch 4  4 1  the second denial called over by ichinose  denies the vip role on ayanokouji s confirmation  then asks how anyone can be made to talk   if ayanokouji s confirmed it  there s no reason for me to refuse  i m not the vip  said hamaguchi   how do you plan on finding the vip  even if we try asking people   directly  i can t imagine that they ll openly admit to anything  it ll probably be difficult to persuade them with words alone  said hamaguchi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html#sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p153-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the second denial<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.153–154<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Called over by Ichinose; denies the VIP role on Ayanokouji’s confirmation, then asks how anyone can be made to talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “If Ayanokouji’s confirmed it, there’s no reason for me to refuse. I’m not the VIP,” said Hamaguchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “How do you plan on finding the VIP? Even if we try asking people … directly, I can’t imagine that they’ll openly admit to anything. It’ll probably be difficult to persuade them with words alone,” said Hamaguchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.153-154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> His relationship with her is why Ayanokōji believes him — little merit in lying, big risk of fracturing the Horikita truce.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Takes the confirmation as the entry ticket into the four-person non-VIP core.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The practical objection that sets Ichinose’s point-of-the-test answer — extraction without force.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p138-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the card table and the corridor<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p217-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the Outcome #1 plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p155-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"machida-kouji manabe-shiho yukimura-teruhiko hirata-yousuke morofuji-rika shinohara-satsuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 4  4 2 4 4  the seat  the stairwell  the breakup evening room  seat war with manabe over machida  the corridor chase  the stairwell cornering over rika  then the 2 a m  vending machine meeting where the hirata farce ends   hey  aren t you sitting in my seat  asked karuizawa   well  that s the seat i want  that s my spot  move  urged karuizawa   hey  machida kun  could you please tell her that you want me next to you   how about we spend some time together  just the two of us  or have you promised that girl you ll go with her  i hate two timers  if you re going to mess around with that girl then that ll be the end of it  i guess  said karuizawa   look  i have plans later  can you please move  asked karuizawa   i have no idea what you re talking about  i ll call the teacher   w wait  karuizawa pleaded with them to not call   i just remembered something  i bumped into that girl before   no way  she was in the wrong  she s a complete airhead   whatever  you probably never planned on forgiving me   yukimura kun  these girls just abducted me and started getting all violent  they re seriously the worst  aren t they  they were being  like  super annoying  so i told them to get lost  said karuizawa   just leave me alone  if you don t  i ll call someone   just leave me alone  as yukimura drew nearer  karuizawa slapped his hand away   god  shut up  nobody asked you   what re you doing here  ayanokouji kun   you did  hirata kun  why  i told you i wanted to talk alone   but i said i wa","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p155-1\">Ch.4 §4.2–4.4: the seat, the stairwell, the breakup<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.155–176<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening room: seat war with Manabe over Machida, the corridor chase, the stairwell cornering over Rika, then the 2 a.m. vending-machine meeting where the Hirata farce ends.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morofuji-rika\">Morofuji Rika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Hey, aren’t you sitting in my seat?” asked Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Well, that’s the seat I want. That’s my spot. Move,” urged Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Hey, Machida-kun. Could you please tell her that you want me next to you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>37 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How about we spend some time together, just the two of us? Or have you promised that girl you’ll go with her? I hate two-timers. If you’re going to mess around with that girl then that’ll be the end of it, I guess,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Inserts herself between Manabe and him, grabs his hand, wins the seat choice; they exchange contact information when the hour ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.156-159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The seat war turns the stairwell corner: “You did push Rika, didn’t you?” — denial, the phone to Rika, Yamashita’s “unforgivable,” hair-grab and face taunts.<span class=\"pg\">p.156-161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Look, I have plans later. Can you please move?” asked Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have no idea what you’re talking about. I’ll call the teacher.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait!” Karuizawa pleaded with them to not call.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just remembered something. I bumped into that girl before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No way. She was in the wrong. She’s a complete airhead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whatever. You probably never planned on forgiving me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Refuses to apologize to Rika even cornered — maybe really innocent; the refusal knowing it will upset them.<span class=\"pg\">p.160-161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yukimura-kun, these girls just abducted me and started getting all violent. They’re seriously the worst, aren’t they? They were being, like, super annoying, so I told them to get lost,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Uses him as rescue cover, shoots him a “pathetic” look when he freezes, then slaps his hand away and screams him off.<span class=\"pg\">p.163-165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just leave me alone. If you don’t, I’ll call someone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just leave me alone!” As Yukimura drew nearer, Karuizawa slapped his hand away.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “God, shut up! Nobody asked you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Panting, head in hands, hyperventilating — the leader of the Class D girls shows the vulnerable side; the threats aren’t what terrified her (his read).<span class=\"pg\">p.161-165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The 2 a.m. call: joy at seeing him turns to anger at Ayanokōji; wants revenge on Manabe; “You said you’d protect me”; “Our relationship is over”; juice can down the hall.<span class=\"pg\">p.171-176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’re you doing here, Ayanokouji-kun?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You did, Hirata-kun? Why? I told you I wanted to talk alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But…I said I wanted to talk alone, just the two of us,” she repeated.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No.” (to Hirata’s “you were completely overwhelmed”)<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why did you tell him?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But your girlfriend’s suffering, right? You should want to help me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But that’s… I didn’t have any choice! Shinohara and the others were there, and—”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You shut your mouth!” she screamed.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please, I’m begging you. Help me. Hirata-kun. You said you’d protect me, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m telling you, it’s not possible! If I could do that, I wouldn’t need your help!”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You liar! You said you’d protect me!” she shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What?! Wh-why are you saying all of this now?!” Karuizawa was horrified.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So are you saying…it’s better for me to get violent with them?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t want to!” Karuizawa had come to Hirata in order to take revenge on Manabe and her friends, and that spoke to her true personality—her real self. More than anything else, Karuizawa was afraid.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whatever! If you’re not going to listen to me, then I don’t need you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Our relationship is over. It’s over!” she shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> The old bump is why the corner exists; Hirata names Morofuji-san as the real issue — “Rika” was her last name.<span class=\"pg\">p.160-174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Named in the “I didn’t have any choice!” excuse — Shinohara and the others were there.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The overbearing Machida seat as caste maintenance: leader of the Class D girls, Hirata’s girlfriend, now the palm of Machida’s hand — root cause still unreadable to him until the “to protect herself” answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.157-158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Fury at his presence in the private meeting; later throws the juice and flees both of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the lunch history and the Machida seat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p189-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.6–4.7: the lowest level<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p155-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho ichinose-honami machida-kouji","q":"ch 4  4 2  the seat arbitration invited out by the class c girls  then made to choose between them and karuizawa   he picks her and keeps the no discussion policy   i see  replied machida   to the hang out invite   excuse me  but would you please move  that s the seat karuizawa s been sitting in  said machida   of course we won t  feel free to talk amongst yourselves  though  we haven t changed our policy  answered machida   class a no discussion  to ichinose","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html#sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p155-1\">Ch.4 §4.2: the seat arbitration<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.155–159<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Invited out by the Class C girls, then made to choose between them and Karuizawa — he picks her and keeps the no-discussion policy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “I see,” replied Machida. (to the hang-out invite)<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “Excuse me, but would you please move? That’s the seat Karuizawa’s been sitting in,” said Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “Of course we won’t. Feel free to talk amongst yourselves, though. We haven’t changed our policy,” answered Machida. (Class A no-discussion, to Ichinose)<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pleased by the female attention; “a little troubled” picking a girl until Karuizawa removes the choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.155-156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Obeys her hand-grab logic, keeps her glued to his side, exchanges contact information at the hour’s end — falling for her, narrator’s read.<span class=\"pg\">p.156-159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Rules against her seat claim for Karuizawa; the Class C girls leave upset.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The second refusal of her cards proposal — policy unchanged.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p137-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the protection offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p218-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the flat refusal and the audit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p155-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"machida-kouji karuizawa-kei morofuji-rika yamashita-saki yabu-nanami manabe-shiho","q":"ch 4  4 2  the seat and the stairwell holds the machida hang out invite over karuizawa s seat claim  loses the seat  then leads the emergency stairwell cornering over rika with yamashita and yabu   hey  machida kun  after we re done here  do you want to hang out with us  the three of us were looking to have some fun   huh  i m talking to machida kun right now  he promised to hang out with me tonight  said manabe   huh  what the hell  ugh  this is bull  manabe whined   stop playing dumb  you did push rika  didn t you  start talking   okay  let s confirm it right now  i m going to call rika  if it wasn t you  we ll forgive you   and what will you tell the teacher  exactly  it s not like we re being violent with you or anything  besides  if you talk to the teacher  we ll tell on you  too  we ll say you pushed rika  you ll also get in trouble   you re seriously pissing us off  we might ve forgiven you if you d actually apologized to rika  but now  we definitely won t forgive you   act as girly as you want  we re still not going to forgive you   i ve always hated your face  karuizawa  i mean  don t you girls think she s just butt ugly   st stop it  she says  what happened to your big attitude   well  i m just talking with karuizawa about her problem  what she did to rika  you heard how karuizawa slammed into her  right   you shut up  this has nothing to do with you   who are you going to call  hirata kun  machida kun  i mean  i guess a slut like you has a hundred guys on speed dia","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p155-1\">Ch.4 §4.2: the seat and the stairwell<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.155–164<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Holds the Machida hang-out invite over Karuizawa’s seat claim, loses the seat, then leads the emergency-stairwell cornering over Rika with Yamashita and Yabu.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morofuji-rika\">Morofuji Rika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yamashita-saki\">Yamashita Saki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yabu-nanami\">Yabu Nanami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Hey, Machida-kun. After we’re done here, do you want to hang out with us? The three of us were looking to have some fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Huh? I’m talking to Machida-kun right now. He promised to hang out with me tonight,” said Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Huh? What the hell? Ugh, this is bull,” Manabe whined.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The invite that starts the seat war; “He promised to hang out with me tonight” loses to Karuizawa’s hand-grab.<span class=\"pg\">p.155-156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Seat loss → stairwell: the Rika charge, the teacher threat, the hair-grab taunts, Yukimura’s glare into silence — “This has nothing to do with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156-164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop playing dumb! You did push Rika, didn’t you? Start talking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, let’s confirm it right now. I’m going to call Rika. If it wasn’t you, we’ll forgive you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And what will you tell the teacher, exactly? It’s not like we’re being violent with you or anything. Besides, if you talk to the teacher, we’ll tell on you, too. We’ll say you pushed Rika. You’ll also get in trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re seriously pissing us off. We might’ve forgiven you if you’d actually apologized to Rika. But now, we definitely won’t forgive you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Act as girly as you want, we’re still not going to forgive you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve always hated your face, Karuizawa. I mean, don’t you girls think she’s just butt-ugly?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “‘St-stop it’, she says. What happened to your big attitude?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’m just talking with Karuizawa about her problem, what she did to Rika. You heard how Karuizawa slammed into her, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You shut up. This has nothing to do with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who are you going to call? Hirata-kun? Machida-kun? I mean, I guess a slut like you has a hundred guys on speed dial, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You better bow your head and apologize to Rika.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> The name the whole corner is about — “Rika,” called to confirm on the phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.160-164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamashita Saki<\/b> Yamashita loses patience first; Manabe answers “Why don’t we bully her for real?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yabu Nanami<\/b> Named with Manabe and Yamashita as the three who tear the face apart.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “She should understand exactly how Rika felt. Why don’t we bully her for real?” — the line that crosses from cornering to striking.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p137-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the threat across the room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p185-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.5–4.6: the anonymous buyer and the subject<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-morishige-takurou-y1v4-p155-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu machida-kouji morishige-takurou","q":"ch 4  4 2  the silent class a seat enters alone after machida and takemoto  sits far end by the class c girls  and shows no human emotion for the whole hour","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-morishige-takurou-y1v4-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2: the silent Class A seat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.155–158<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morishige-takurou\">Morishige Takurō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Enters alone after Machida and Takemoto, sits far end by the Class C girls, and shows no human emotion for the whole hour.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Morishige came in by himself” — apart from the group he still keeps the corner.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Morishige, who had erased all semblance of human emotion from his expression” — silent for two days under orders.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> One of those who turned against Katsuragi on the island; would not normally follow him — Sakayanagi’s absence left no choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> His leader was sick and absent from the trip; without her he does as he is told.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Comes in with the Class A pair and keeps their far-end seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-morishige-takurou-y1v4-p233-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the predicted traitor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p155-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 4  4 2  the chair and the exit arrives coincidentally with karuizawa  earns her disgust  then gives the pompous non notice answer before heading back to the room   you think so  i can t say that i noticed anything of the sort  answered the professor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p155-1\">Ch.4 §4.2: the chair and the exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.155–160<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives coincidentally with Karuizawa, earns her disgust, then gives the pompous non-notice answer before heading back to the room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “You think so? I can’t say that I noticed anything of the sort,” answered the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Open disgust at his presence; she moves to the back the moment they enter together.<span class=\"pg\">p.155-156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “You think so? I can’t say that I noticed anything of the sort,” answered the Professor — tone ridiculously pompous; Yukimura’s vibe read called right.<span class=\"pg\">p.159-160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Heads back to his room instead of following the stairwell chase — the Professor opts out.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the VIP alibi and the card heat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: named in the cover trio<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-takemoto-shigeru-y1v4-p155-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"machida-kouji takemoto-shigeru","q":"ch 4  4 2  with machida enters the evening room with machida as the class a pair and takes the far end by the class c girls","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-takemoto-shigeru-y1v4-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2: with Machida<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.155<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#takemoto-shigeru\">Takemoto Shigeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Enters the evening room with Machida as the Class A pair and takes the far end by the Class C girls.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The no-discussion pair — Class A’s distance is kept as a two-man block.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No line in this range; presence is narrated only.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p155-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 4  4 2  the stairwell sits near ayanokoji in the evening room  mutters the vip worry  then follows the class c trio into the emergency stairwell and breaks the corner with a shout   this isn t good   yeah  if things continue like this  the vip will get away   yukimura  next to ayanokoji   hey  did you get a weird vibe from those three just now  asked yukimura   you think they have a bone to pick with her  asked yukimura   let s follow them  i don t think there ll be violence  but it could lead to an uproar   damn karuizawa  she s always making people hate her  i wanted us to spend our precious time finding the vip  yukimura grumbled   what are you doing  yukimura shouted   don t you think it s better to just let things go  they bumped into   each other  it s not like karuizawa was at fault  yukimura said   are you okay  asked yukimura  who seemed unable to leave karuizawa to their mercy   hey  what the hell  i only came to check on you because i was worried   jeez  what s with her  she s always  always causing trouble for people","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p155-1\">Ch.4 §4.2: the stairwell<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.155–165<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits near Ayanokōji in the evening room, mutters the VIP worry, then follows the Class C trio into the emergency stairwell and breaks the corner with a shout.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “This isn’t good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Yeah. If things continue like this, the VIP will get away.” (Yukimura, next to Ayanokōji)<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Hey. Did you get a weird vibe from those three just now?” asked Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Spots the three girls on her tail, grumbles she always makes people hate her, throws the stairwell door open, tries to check on her, gets slapped away, and leaves exhausted.<span class=\"pg\">p.159-165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You think they have a bone to pick with her?” asked Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s follow them. I don’t think there’ll be violence, but it could lead to an uproar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn Karuizawa. She’s always making people hate her. I wanted us to spend our precious time finding the VIP,” Yukimura grumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you doing?!” Yukimura shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you think it’s better to just let things go? They bumped into … each other. It’s not like Karuizawa was at fault,” Yukimura said.<span class=\"pg\">p.163-164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Glared into silence by the trio under their weight — falls silent, then takes Karuizawa’s “pathetic” look for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.163-164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you okay?” asked Yukimura, who seemed unable to leave Karuizawa to their mercy.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, what the hell? I only came to check on you because I was worried!”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jeez, what’s with her? She’s always, always causing trouble for people!”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Exhausted from the ordeal, leaves without another word — resentment and the failed rescue both in one exit.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The Professor’s pompous “I can’t say that I noticed anything of the sort” answer next to him — Yukimura’s vibe read called right on the money by narration.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p131-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the roommate’s VIP probe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: the VIP steps forward<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p158-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"morishige-takurou katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu","q":"ch 4  4 2  the absent faction leader named in morishige s class a background   one of the two factions led by katsuragi and her  she was sick and absent from the trip","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p158-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html#sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p158-1\">Ch.4 §4.2: the absent faction leader<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.158<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Morishige’s Class A background — one of the two factions led by Katsuragi and her; she was sick and absent from the trip.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morishige-takurou\">Morishige Takurō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishige Takurō<\/b> Without her presence he has no choice but to follow Katsuragi’s no-discussion orders.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The other faction leader; Morishige had turned against him on the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; the row records the faction fact as the pages print it.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p75-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the rumoured name in the café<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p233-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the faction behind the traitor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho ibuki-mio","q":"ch 4  4 2  the absent buffer named as the class c girl who might have mitigated the trio on karuizawa s tail   and she wasn t around","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1\">Ch.4 §4.2: the absent buffer<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.159<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the Class C girl who might have mitigated the trio on Karuizawa’s tail — and she wasn’t around.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Her absence is why the three can close on Karuizawa alone in the corridor.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The buffer between Manabe’s set and Karuizawa is missing for the stairwell.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue in this range; presence is the narrator’s counterfactual.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: not at the shade meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p222-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the lone girl agrees<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-morofuji-rika-y1v4-p160-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho morofuji-rika","q":"ch 4  4 2 4 4  the name behind the corner named as the girl karuizawa is said to have pushed   the whole stairwell charge and hirata s morning plan run on her name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-morofuji-rika-y1v4-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2–4.4: the name behind the corner<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.160–174<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morofuji-rika\">Morofuji Rika<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the girl Karuizawa is said to have pushed — the whole stairwell charge and Hirata’s morning plan run on her name.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The charge: “You did push Rika, didn’t you?” — Manabe’s group will call her to confirm.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The old bump is why they want an apology; Hirata finally says Morofuji-san — “That must’ve been her last name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160-174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Manabe offers forgiveness only if the phone call clears Karuizawa — or only if she bows and apologizes when it doesn’t.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; every row is other people speaking her name. Bare “Rika” is the form the stairwell uses; Hirata’s Morofuji-san is the surname printed once.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-morofuji-rika-y1v4-p189-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.6: the reluctant hand<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamashita-saki-y1v4-p161-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei morofuji-rika yamashita-saki","q":"ch 4  4 2  the stairwell trio loses patience first in the cornering    karuizawa s unforgivable    and strikes her shoulder with extra force   shiho chan  i ve had enough  karuizawa s unforgivable   yeah  for sure  don t you just want to cut her face","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamashita-saki-y1v4-p161-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2: the stairwell trio<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.161–163<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yamashita-saki\">Yamashita Saki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Loses patience first in the cornering — “Karuizawa’s unforgivable” — and strikes her shoulder with extra force.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morofuji-rika\">Morofuji Rika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamashita Saki<\/b> “Shiho-chan. I’ve had enough. Karuizawa’s unforgivable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamashita Saki<\/b> “Yeah, for sure. Don’t you just want to cut her face?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Shiho-chan. I’ve had enough. Karuizawa’s unforgivable.” — the Manabe address that starts the strike.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The shoulder hit, then the face taunts with Manabe and Yabu — “don’t you just want to cut her face?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161-163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> Speaks for Rika’s feeling — “She should understand exactly how Rika felt.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yabu-nanami-y1v4-p163-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho yabu-nanami","q":"ch 4  4 2  the face taunts one of the three in the stairwell who tear karuizawa s looks apart while she is held against the wall","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yabu-nanami-y1v4-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2: the face taunts<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.163<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yabu-nanami\">Yabu Nanami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One of the three in the stairwell who tear Karuizawa’s looks apart while she is held against the wall.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Named with Manabe and Yamashita as the group that “wouldn’t be satisfied until they’d verbally torn Karuizawa’s pretty face apart.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The trio’s shared line of attack — Manabe leads, Yamashita and Yabu answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No separately tagged line; the “Yeah, for sure” is the group voice in the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p166-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"ch 4  4 3  the midnight point question meets ayanokoji by the night pool after his call  answers the buy anything exceptions question  survives hoshinomiya s drunk interruption  and gets asked for a future favour   sorry to keep you waiting  ayanokouji   it s okay  i m sorry for calling you so late   his line  in exchange   an instructor is obligated to consult with a student  it s nothing out of the ordinary  besides  for better or worse  this is the first time you ve actually called me   don t worry about it  adult issues  anyway  what did you want to ask   yes  exceptions exist  naturally  for example  if you request to buy the life of a teacher or student  we cannot honor that request   you re drunk  aren t you  chabashira sensei said   to hoshinomiya   jeez  you can really hold your liquor  you handled yourself today  and you re fine now  too   about hoshinomiya s iron liver   a big problem  as a teacher  it s only natural for me to consult my students and soothe their anxieties  answered chabashira sensei   good  now hurry up and leave already  i ll head back soon myself   sorry  she s troublesome   well  i can only speak from my own experience  but it was when someone wanted   to change the school rules  of course  you re limited to a certain realistic scope  for example  you could change the class start time in order to avoid being late to class  she answered   are you dissatisfied with my answer   you could have just emailed me that question  i don t understand why y","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p166-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p166-1\">Ch.4 §4.3: the midnight point question<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.166–169<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ayanokōji by the night pool after his call; answers the buy-anything exceptions question, survives Hoshinomiya’s drunk interruption, and gets asked for a future favour.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Sorry to keep you waiting, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “It’s okay. I’m sorry for calling you so late.” (his line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “An instructor is obligated to consult with a student. It’s nothing out of the ordinary. Besides, for better or worse, this is the first time you’ve actually called me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn’t treat Class D with love; students wouldn’t normally come to her — his read of why the first call matters.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry about it. Adult issues. Anyway, what did you want to ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pale, alcohol on her breath — “adult issues” waved off while he works the exceptions question.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Exceptions exist, naturally. For example, if you request to buy the life of a teacher or student, we cannot honor that request.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Private points cannot buy a life — the standing exception to “anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re drunk, aren’t you?” Chabashira-sensei said. (to Hoshinomiya)<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jeez. You can really hold your liquor. You handled yourself today, and you’re fine now, too.” (about Hoshinomiya’s iron liver)<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Grabs her by the nape and drags her off; stays calm under the sneaking-around bait; “Ayanokouji requested this location. He wanted to consult me in private.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167-168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A big problem? As a teacher, it’s only natural for me to consult my students and soothe their anxieties,” answered Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good. Now hurry up and leave already. I’ll head back soon myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. She’s troublesome.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I can only speak from my own experience, but it was when someone wanted … to change the school rules. Of course, you’re limited to a certain realistic scope. For example, you could change the class start time in order to avoid being late to class,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.168-169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The largest point spend she has seen: a system change within a realistic scope — hypotheticals only, no facts.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you dissatisfied with my answer?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You could have just emailed me that question. I don’t understand why you wanted me to meet you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Accepts the no-email reason (no record); eyes him with suspicion when he calls the future favour over his shoulder.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll ask you for a favor in the near future,” I called. (his line, her reaction recorded)<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The teacher rivalry read: competing and deceiving for the top class — salaries or a school-days grudge, he can’t tell.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the Class A leverage, named twice<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p167-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae ichinose-honami hoshinomiya-chie","q":"ch 4  4 3  the drunk interruption follows chabashira to the night pool  hugs ayanokoji smelling of alcohol  baits the private meeting as suspicious  and leaves with a  no sexy times  shot   yoohoo  sae chan  how you feeling   hmm  oh no  of course i m not  i m not drunk  i was just acting all sleepy  you know   jeez  you can really hold your liquor   chabashira s line  tagged in exchange   good evening  ayanokouji kun  how are you doing   that answer was so not cute that i m impressed  so  ayanokouji kun  do you love the tsuntsun older sister types  like sae chan  asked hoshinomiya sensei   so what were you two talking about in the middle of the night  isn t that in itself a really big problem  asked hoshinomiya sensei   if that s true  wouldn t it be better for you to do it with more people around  if you look like you re sneaking around  i can t help but think it s suspicious   hmm  well  i suppose you re not violating any rules  muttered hoshinomiya sensei   okay  okay  but remember  no sexy times  teased hoshinomiya sensei","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p167-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html#sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p167-1\">Ch.4 §4.3: the drunk interruption<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.167–168<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Follows Chabashira to the night pool, hugs Ayanokōji smelling of alcohol, baits the private meeting as suspicious, and leaves with a “no sexy times” shot.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “Yoohoo, Sae-chan! How you feeling?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “Hmm? Oh no, of course I’m not, I’m not drunk. I was just acting all sleepy, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “Jeez. You can really hold your liquor.” (Chabashira’s line, tagged in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Iron liver — handled herself today and still fine; “acting all sleepy” denied drunk to Chabashira’s face.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good evening, Ayanokouji-kun. How are you doing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That answer was so not-cute that I’m impressed! So, Ayanokouji-kun, do you love the tsuntsun older sister types, like Sae-chan?” asked Hoshinomiya-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Hand on his shoulders, a tight hug, alcohol smell — overly familiar by design.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The night-pool chase: baits her on sneaking around, gets the “Ayanokouji requested this location” answer, mutters no rules broken, exits under “hurry up and leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167-168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what were you two talking about in the middle of the night? Isn’t that in itself a really big problem?” asked Hoshinomiya-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s true, wouldn’t it be better for you to do it with more people around? If you look like you’re sneaking around, I can’t help but think it’s suspicious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm. Well, I suppose you’re not violating any rules,” muttered Hoshinomiya-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, okay. But remember, no sexy times,” teased Hoshinomiya-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Bad at hiding emotions — his read that Ichinose may soon wonder why she is in Rabbit and discover the spy order.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Followed Chabashira deliberately; “Was it just a coincidence? Unlikely.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p125-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the spy order in the brief<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p230-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the unlock authority<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p170-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei morofuji-rika manabe-shiho horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 4  4 4  the farce ends at the vending machine slips out of the room at 2 a m  into ayanokoji s hallway trap  takes him to karuizawa s meeting  and ends the fake dating on the spot when revenge is refused   did i wake you  or were you already awake  he asked   why would you think that  this was the first time i ve left the room at night   karuizawa contacted you  didn t she   ayanokoji  reported exchange   do you happen to know something about it  he asked   she asked me to report on everything that happens in the rabbit group  including karuizawa s situation   his paraphrase of horikita s order   reported   what kind of information does she want  he asked   i don t know what i can tell you  honestly  i have to consider karuizawa san s feelings   ayanokouji kun  i m sure you won t say anything unnecessary  but what i m about to tell you is extremely delicate  also  karuizawa san might refuse to talk and head back to her room  please understand that first  he said   i asked him to come  said hirata   you did  hirata kun  why  i told you i wanted to talk alone   her line  tagged to him in exchange   i know  but karuizawa san  i was worried about what you told me earlier  that s why i thought it might be a good idea to bring ayanokouji kun  since he seems to understand the situation  i m sorry for not telling you first   if you want  we can be alone  but when we spoke earlier  you never said anything about it having to be just the two of us   you were telling me about a fight ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p170-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p170-1\">Ch.4 §4.4: the farce ends at the vending machine<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.170–178<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Slips out of the room at 2 a.m. into Ayanokōji’s hallway trap, takes him to Karuizawa’s meeting, and ends the fake dating on the spot when revenge is refused.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morofuji-rika\">Morofuji Rika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Did I wake you? Or were you already awake?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Why would you think that? This was the first time I’ve left the room at night.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Karuizawa contacted you, didn’t she?” (Ayanokōji; reported exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>40 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The night walk: “Did I wake you?” → “Karuizawa contacted you, didn’t she?” → tasks him with saving her — then “I honestly find you a little weird. You kind of creep me out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170-178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you happen to know something about it?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She asked me to report on everything that happens in the Rabbit group, including Karuizawa’s situation.” (his paraphrase of Horikita’s order — reported)<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What kind of information does she want?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what I can tell you, honestly. I have to consider Karuizawa-san’s feelings.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun, I’m sure you won’t say anything unnecessary, but what I’m about to tell you is extremely delicate. Also, Karuizawa-san might refuse to talk and head back to her room. Please understand that first,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Brings Ayanokōji against her “alone” wish; holds the no-violence line; reveals the farce — “I’ve told you from the start that we aren’t really boyfriend and girlfriend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171-176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I asked him to come,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You did, Hirata-kun? Why? I told you I wanted to talk alone.” (her line, tagged to him in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know. But Karuizawa-san, I was worried about what you told me earlier. That’s why I thought it might be a good idea to bring Ayanokouji-kun, since he seems to understand the situation. I’m sorry for not telling you first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you want, we can be alone. But when we spoke earlier, you never said anything about it having to be just the two of us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You were telling me about a fight with Manabe-san from Class C. Is it true?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun, did you know about the fight with Manabe-san and the others?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From what Karuizawa-san has told me, it seems like the girls were … making false accusations. They took her to a deserted spot and started hounding her for answers. They were on the verge of using violence,” Hirata said.<span class=\"pg\">p.172-173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If Manabe-san and her friends got violent with you, we definitely need to take action. I absolutely cannot allow violence,” he continued.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. So that’s why you told me,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa-san asked me to take revenge on Manabe-san and her friends.” (his report of her request)<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Because this isn’t like you, Karuizawa-san. You aren’t a violent … person,” Hirata answered. — refuses eye for an eye while still claiming allyship.<span class=\"pg\">p.173-174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, I do. But I don’t believe in an eye for an eye. You know that, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s think this through. If possible, let’s find a way to get along with Manabe-san and her friends,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No reason? Didn’t this start because you had an issue with Morofuji-san, Karuizawa?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> Names Morofuji-san as the origin — “Hirata said Morofuji, but he probably meant Rika. That must’ve been her last name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Morning plan: tell them to stop, and tell them Karuizawa will apologize — she refuses, so he will not help on her terms.<span class=\"pg\">p.174-176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’ll protect you. But I can’t just hurt Manabe-san and her friends for no real reason. Let’s try to find a way to resolve things peacefully, through discussion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s the case, then I can’t help you. I’m sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t matter what the reason is. I can’t do what you want. You’re one of my classmates, Karuizawa-san. If you’re in trouble, I’ll help you, protect you. But I can’t hurt someone else to do that, even if they’re from Class C,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “‘Liar’? You’ve known this was my stance since the beginning.” He stood up.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve told you from the start that we aren’t really boyfriend and girlfriend. I don’t mind pretending to go out with you, but I definitely won’t fight a war for you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because we need a new option now. I want to help you,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun, do you have any ideas?” asked Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun. I have my limits. I can’t do everything. Please understand that,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I’m Karuizawa-san’s ally, and I’m your ally as well, Ayanokouji-kun. However, my priorities might change depending on the situation. You’re far more capable than everyone thinks,” Hirata observed.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re exactly right. We weren’t really dating. We were going out because we both felt that it was necessary. I suppose you consider that contradictory,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The bridge story is the cover he accepts; “saving Karuizawa-san will give our class a lead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170-178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun. I have to be very honest, but… Well, this is going to sound very rude, but I honestly find you a little weird. You kind of creep me out. I’m sorry if that offends you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve been watching you since school started. The Ayanokouji-kun back then and the Ayanokouji-kun now are like two different people. Your presence, the words you use… It’s like you have two different personalities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Frighteningly observant — the two-personality read is the sharpest student diagnosis of Ayanokōji so far in the volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well. I suppose Horikita-san must’ve determined that saving Karuizawa-san will give our class a lead,” he reasoned.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The four-month farce as mutual necessity: she proposed, he honored; “host” and “parasite” is Ayanokōji’s caste reading of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p131-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the absent roommate and the corridor pass<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: Sugimura and the last Class D VIP<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p174-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei shinohara-satsuki","q":"ch 4  4 4  the excuse name named in karuizawa s  i didn t have any choice  outburst at the vending machine   shinohara and the others were there","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p174-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p174-1\">Ch.4 §4.4: the excuse name<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.174<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Karuizawa’s “I didn’t have any choice!” outburst at the vending machine — Shinohara and the others were there.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The witness list she uses to justify the old Rika incident; Ayanokōji cuts her off with “What does that mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; one spoken name in Karuizawa’s line.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: named as Sakura’s roommate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p179-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 4  4 4  the sugimura bargain takes hirata s backstory and the fake dating motive  buys his silence for the karuizawa plan  and receives the class d vip s identity as a parting gift   but i do think you re amazing  ayanokouji kun  you re different from ike kun and yamauchi kun   hirata s line  in exchange   i m worse than them   is that really the truth  i asked   what was in it for me  karuizawa san wasn t being bullied  that s all i needed   hirata s line  reported   i believe you  but is there some deeper reason as well  i asked   you  hirata  i have a hard time imagining that   i understand what you re feeling  but the world isn t that simple    right  at this very moment  there s someone being bullied somewhere  and they might try to take their own life  just like sugimura kun  you can t stop them   so what are you going to do  then  you want to save both karuizawa and manabe  but that s not possible   if you promise not to get yourself involved  i m sure horikita will stay silent  i answered   hirata  since you have a large social network  i have a favor to ask  i handed hirata a piece of paper","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p179-1\">Ch.4 §4.4: the Sugimura bargain<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.179–183<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Takes Hirata’s backstory and the fake-dating motive, buys his silence for the Karuizawa plan, and receives the Class D VIP’s identity as a parting gift.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “But I do think you’re amazing, Ayanokouji-kun. You’re different from Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun.” (Hirata’s line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m worse than them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Is that really the truth?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Named with Yamauchi as the contrast class for “amazing” — he ranks himself under both.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Same contrast line.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The night’s full read: smarter than imagined, pathological saviour drive, then the confidentiality bargain and the paper favour.<span class=\"pg\">p.179-183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What was in it for me? Karuizawa-san wasn’t being bullied. That’s all I needed.” (Hirata’s line, reported)<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you. But is there some deeper reason as well?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You, Hirata? I have a hard time imagining that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand what you’re feeling, but the world isn’t that simple, … right? At this very moment, there’s someone being bullied somewhere. And they might try to take their own life, just like Sugimura-kun. You can’t stop them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181-182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what are you going to do, then? You want to save both Karuizawa and Manabe, but that’s not possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you promise not to get yourself involved, I’m sure Horikita will stay silent,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hirata. Since you have a large social network, I have a favor to ask.” I handed Hirata a piece of paper.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The paper favour accepted without a displeased look — the social-network lever for the Manabe plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Accepts the elementary/junior-high bullying as the reason for the hyperventilation; the façade read locked in.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The confidentiality pact runs through her; “Our philosophies are similar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Gains Hirata’s cooperation — “a power I’d always wanted”; each side feels they gained something.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the deck VIP exchange<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: the phone swap and the dam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p179-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 4  4 4  sugimura and the last class d vip explains the boyfriend farce as anti bullying penance  tells the sugimura window story  pledges confidentiality  then reveals he knows the last class d vip   yeah  but i do think you re amazing  ayanokouji kun  you re different from ike kun and yamauchi kun   even if you re just following horikita san s orders  you re still the one talking to me right now  ayanokouji kun  it isn t as though horikita gave you a list of prepared responses  i think that you show clear  well reasoned logic  that s not something you can pretend to have   you ve already said as much  but i agreed to act like karuizawa san s boyfriend so she could protect herself  that s what she wanted  she said she wanted me to save her  it might be a little difficult for you to imagine  but throughout her elementary and junior high years  she was viciously bullied   of course  i only met karuizawa san after she started school here  but i understood  people who are bullied give off a unique vibe  that s why i agreed to go out with her  that way  karuizawa san would free herself from her past by using her position as my girlfriend  i don t think that karuizawa san has been showing us her real personality  i think she s just desperately trying to act tough   what was in it for me  karuizawa san wasn t being bullied  that s all i needed   i know you re not convinced  but that s the reason i did it  he continued   until my second year of junior high i was  for lack of a bet","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p179-1\">Ch.4 §4.4: Sugimura and the last Class D VIP<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.179–183<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Explains the boyfriend farce as anti-bullying penance, tells the Sugimura window story, pledges confidentiality, then reveals he knows the last Class D VIP.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yeah. But I do think you’re amazing, Ayanokouji-kun. You’re different from Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Even if you’re just following Horikita-san’s orders, you’re still the one talking to me right now, Ayanokouji-kun. It isn’t as though Horikita gave you a list of prepared responses. I think that you show clear, well-reasoned…”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “You’ve already said as much, but I agreed to act like Karuizawa-san’s boyfriend so she could protect herself. That’s what she wanted. She said she wanted me to save her. It might be a little difficult for you to imagine, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>24 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you’re just following Horikita-san’s orders, you’re still the one talking to me right now, Ayanokouji-kun. It isn’t as though Horikita gave you a list of prepared responses. I think that you show clear, well-reasoned logic. That’s not something you can pretend to have.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The sharpest compliment of Ayanokōji’s performed normalcy — logic cannot be scripted.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve already said as much, but I agreed to act like Karuizawa-san’s boyfriend so she could protect herself. That’s what she wanted. She said she wanted me to save her. It might be a little difficult for you to imagine, but throughout her elementary and junior high years, she was viciously bullied.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, I only met Karuizawa-san after she started school here. But I understood. People who are bullied give off a unique vibe. That’s why I agreed to go out with her. That way, Karuizawa-san would free herself from her past by using her position as my girlfriend. I don’t think that Karuizawa-san has been showing us her real personality. I think she’s just desperately trying to act tough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The host bargain restated as protection; her real personality is the act.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What was in it for me? Karuizawa-san wasn’t being bullied. That’s all I needed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know you’re not convinced, but that’s the reason I did it,” he continued.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Until my second year of junior high I was, for lack of a better word, a nobody. I didn’t stand out at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I wouldn’t say that I was completely invisible. I did have friends. I had this one friend ever since I was little, a guy named Sugimura-kun. We were in the same class together for six years, throughout elementary school. We were neighbors, too. We walked to and from school together every day.” Hirata spoke like he was recalling some fleeting memory.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When we started junior high, we were put into separate classes for the first time. At first, we kept going to school together just like we always had. Gradually, we walked together less and less. I started to only hang out with other guys from my new class. That story probably sounds normal enough, I suppose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But you see, while I had my new friends, Sugimura-kun was getting bullied.” Hirata squeezed the can he was holding.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I didn’t do anything. I couldn’t. I was afraid I’d become their next target. I was afraid that my new, fun life would be destroyed. So I pretended not to see Sugimura-kun, my oldest friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That day’s burned into my memory, even now. After morning soccer practice, I returned to the classroom. When I got near the room, I saw that Sugimura-kun was already there, his face swollen. I decided to wait a bit before going in. … Perhaps Sugimura-kun saw how ugly my heart was. He didn’t say a word, but it was almost like he was sending out a plea for help. That day, he jumped out of the classroom window,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He was declared brain dead. But even now, Sugimura-kun’s parents believe he’ll recover. They’re waiting for him. … When Sugimura-kun jumped, I realized something. By selfishly focusing so much on my own desires, I helped drive a treasured friend to his death.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The origin of Hirata Yousuke — penance through saving others, named as the birth of the man.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think Sugimura-kun can be saved, but I wanted to atone. I figure the only way for me to do that is to save others,” Hirata said.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I know that. I’m not a hero or anything. But I want to save the people close to me, at the very least. I must help them. That’s my penance for the sin I committed,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand that. It’s probably why you’re here with me right now,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never thought I’d ever tell this story to anyone. Nobody here knows the truth. That’s why I chose this school,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will you and Horikita-san keep this confidential?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then I’ll believe in you two. Our philosophies are similar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The confidentiality is a two-person pact through her.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, Ayanokouji-kun. There is one more thing I’ve been hiding from you. I know the identity of the last VIP from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The Class D VIP count closed from his side — withheld until the bargain is sealed.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p170-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4: the farce ends at the vending machine<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p231-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: the paper, the survey, the model<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p179-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka ike-kanji","q":"ch 4  4 4  the contrast name named once in hirata s compliment   ayanokoji is  different from ike kun and yamauchi kun  and he ranks himself worse than both","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p179-1\">Ch.4 §4.4: the contrast name<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.179<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once in Hirata’s compliment — Ayanokōji is “different from Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun,” and he ranks himself worse than both.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The comparison class for “amazing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m worse than them” — his self-ranking under Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; one name in Hirata’s line.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p179-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 4  4 4  the contrast name named with ike in hirata s compliment   ayanokoji is  different from ike kun and yamauchi kun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p179-1\">Ch.4 §4.4: the contrast name<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.179<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named with Ike in Hirata’s compliment — Ayanokōji is “different from Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The comparison class for “amazing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m worse than them” — his self-ranking under Yamauchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; one name in Hirata’s line.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: the neck-grab and the camera stimulus<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p236-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the Rooster who hesitated<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sugimura-y1v4-p180-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke sugimura","q":"ch 4  4 4  the friend in the story named only inside hirata s night confession   the childhood friend whose bullying he ignored until the classroom window","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sugimura-y1v4-p180-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.4: the friend in the story<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.180–182<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sugimura\">Sugimura<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only inside Hirata’s night confession — the childhood friend whose bullying he ignored until the classroom window.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Six years of classes and neighbors; the SOS ignored for new junior-high friends; brain-dead after the jump, parents still waiting.<span class=\"pg\">p.180-182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Declared brain dead; “That day was so surreal, I still wonder if it was a hallucination.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; every row is Hirata’s recollection.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p183-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke sudou-ken katsuragi-kouhei sakura-airi","q":"ch 4  4 5  the cow group ends calls ayanokoji after the cow group early end email  denies the vip role  reports class a s silence  and waves goodbye   yeah  she replied   have i done something wrong  she asked   no  you haven t  this just means that someone in the cow group reported to the school who they think the vip is   his line  in exchange   sakura  were you the vip  or was it someone else   his line   no  i m not the vip  but i m not sure about sudou kun or  um  the others  she answered   okay  thank you  ayanokouji kun  i m happy you told me that   how are things with class a  i heard rumors that none of them are participating in the discussions   his line   yeah  it s just like what the others have been saying  none of them have talked at all  said sakura   if there s anything else  please let me know  you can talk to me anytime  i told sakura   thank you  ayanokouji kun  see you later","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p183-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p183-1\">Ch.4 §4.5: the Cow group ends<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.183–184<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Calls Ayanokōji after the Cow-group early-end email; denies the VIP role, reports Class A’s silence, and waves goodbye.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Yeah…” she replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Have I done something wrong?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “No, you haven’t. This just means that someone in the Cow group reported to the school who they think the VIP is.” (his line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The Cow group has ended — same notice the Monkey group got; she reads unease into it.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> His Monkey ending is the comparison Ayanokōji uses for the Cow email — two different betrayal motives (certainty vs impatience).<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sakura, were you the VIP? Or was it someone else?” (his line)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m not the VIP. But I’m not sure about Sudou-kun or, um, the others,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Names him in the uncertain Cow roster — no idea whether he or the others were the VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun. I’m happy you told me that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How are things with Class A? I heard rumors that none of them are participating in the discussions.” (his line)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, it’s just like what the others have been saying. None of them have talked at all,” said Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The Class A silence confirmed from her side — Katsuragi’s plan “rather thorough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If there’s anything else, please let me know. You can talk to me anytime,” I told Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun. See you later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Waves her hands adorably on the goodbye — the meek profile he filed against Karuizawa’s type.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the bow stress-talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p183-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi karuizawa-kei sudou-ken","q":"ch 4  4 5 4 7  the cow name and the warning named in sakura s cow group vip uncertainty  then again as ayanokoji s example that eye for eye brings a school investigation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p183-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p183-1\">Ch.4 §4.5–4.7: the Cow name and the warning<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.183, 195<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Sakura’s Cow-group VIP uncertainty, then again as Ayanokōji’s example that eye-for-eye brings a school investigation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “I’m not sure about Sudou-kun or, um, the others” — the only Cow-roster name she speaks.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The Sudou precedent cited to her: “You should know from what happened with Sudou that this isn’t a simple matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence in either range; both rows are other people speaking his name.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p235-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the sixth wheel<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p185-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 4  4 5  the fallback contact named once as the risk ayanokoji avoids   if hirata had not had manabe s info  he would have had to ask her for it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p185-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p185-1\">Ch.4 §4.5: the fallback contact<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.185<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the risk Ayanokōji avoids — if Hirata had not had Manabe’s info, he would have had to ask her for it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The cross-class contact info Hirata supplies saves the Kushida detour.<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; one line of planning in Ayanokōji’s narration.<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the invitation inside<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1–5.2: the Dragon VIP behind the swap<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p185-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka morofuji-rika karuizawa-kei ryuuen-kakeru manabe-shiho","q":"ch 4  4 5 4 6  the anonymous buyer and the subject accepts the sub account revenge pitch  brings rika into the switchboard room at four  runs the milgram frame on karuizawa  and invites rika to strike  who is this   chat  i m alone  but who are you   chat  look  who are you   chat  do you have the wrong number   chat  i don t know what you re talking about  please stop sending me messages   chat  i don t know what you re talking about  i m going to ignore you   chat  i don t need your help  i just need karuizawa san to talk to rika  then we ll know the truth   chat  what should i do  are you saying there s a way   chat  what guarantee do i have  it feels like you re trying to lure me into a trap  and then you ll tattle to the school  this smells like a sub account   chat  so if i show this chat log to the school  what then  it ll be all over for you   chat  i understand  i ll hear you out  at least   chat  so  what should i do   chat  i see  i see  so since you re her classmate  you can call karuizawa san   chat   it s all right  said manabe   i just happened to see you come in here  that s all  well  i suppose this is the perfect opportunity  let me introduce you  this is rika  do you remember her  karuizawa san  asked manabe   hey  rika  karuizawa san was the one who shoved you  right  asked manabe   apologize to rika  demanded manabe   still acting tough  you re a real piece of work  aren t you  but i think i understand now  more or less  snapped manabe   your behavior  yo","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p185-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p185-1\">Ch.4 §4.5–4.6: the anonymous buyer and the subject<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.185–193<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Accepts the sub-account revenge pitch, brings Rika into the switchboard room at four, runs the Milgram frame on Karuizawa, and invites Rika to strike.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morofuji-rika\">Morofuji Rika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Who is this? (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> I’m alone, but who are you? (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Look, who are you? (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>28 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The anonymous Class D classmate who hates the same person — trust won with “show this chat log to the teachers”; she never learns the sender.<span class=\"pg\">p.185-188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Do you have the wrong number? (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> I don’t know what you’re talking about. Please stop sending me messages. (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> I don’t know what you’re talking about. I’m going to ignore you. (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> I don’t need your help. I just need Karuizawa-san to talk to Rika. Then we’ll know the truth. (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> What should I do? Are you saying there’s a way? (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> What guarantee do I have? It feels like you’re trying to lure me into a trap, and then you’ll tattle to the school. This smells like a sub account. (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> So if I show this chat log to the school, what then? It’ll be all over for you. (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> I understand. I’ll hear you out, at least. (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> So, what should I do? (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> I see, I see. So since you’re her classmate, you can call Karuizawa-san? (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Intense desire to settle with Rika as the lever; wariness never quite cuts the contact — how much Karuizawa makes her blood boil.<span class=\"pg\">p.186-187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> Revenge framed as for her; in the room she pulls Rika forward, names the shove, and coaches the slaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.186-193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s all right,” said Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just happened to see you come in here, that’s all. Well, I suppose this is the perfect opportunity. Let me introduce you. This is Rika. Do you remember her, Karuizawa-san?” asked Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Rika. Karuizawa-san was the one who shoved you, right?” asked Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Apologize to Rika,” demanded Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Still acting tough. You’re a real piece of work, aren’t you? But I think I understand now, more or less,” snapped Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your behavior. You’re unusually fearful. Karuizawa-san, you were bullied, weren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hit the nail on the head, didn’t I? I knew it. I could feel it right from the start,” Manabe continued.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The perception is Ayanokōji’s gift — she knew because he told her everything beforehand.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you get down on your knees and beg right now, I might forgive you. How about it? I mean, you’re good at groveling, right? Being on your knees?” Manabe mocked Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Hair-snatch into the wall, knee to the stomach, the Milgram subject role — “Manabe’s greatest reward” is her pain.<span class=\"pg\">p.190-193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whoa, Shiho. Don’t you think you’re hitting her a little too much? Wow, you’re harsh.” (a friend’s line, tagged in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on Rika. You give it a try, too,” urged Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re doing this for your sake, right? Come on, there’s no one around,” replied Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, no, that’s no good at all. You need to put more force into it, like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His Class C is the external threat Ayanokōji cites — further harassment would land them in trouble with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p155-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the seat and the stairwell<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p222-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the shouted objection<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p189-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"manabe-shiho morofuji-rika hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka machida-kouji karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 4  4 6 4 7  the lowest level lured to the switchboard room early  cornered with rika and manabe s trio  beaten under the milgram frame  then broken open and bound to ayanokoji with the stairwell photo   what s going on  i can t connect to  there s no signal   wh what are you doing here  she asked  trembling   i just happened to see you come in here  that s all   manabe s line  in exchange   yeah  she s the one  said rika   rika s line  tagged in exchange   h huh  who s apologizing  i haven t done anything wrong  said karuizawa   understand what  asked karuizawa   wha   no  you re wrong  karuizawa denied it  but her words were weak   n no  i won t  i ve never done that kind of thing before  karuizawa shouted   ow  ow  it hurts  let me go  screamed karuizawa   agh  karuizawa shouted   s s s stop it  pleaded karuizawa   please  forgive me  karuizawa pleaded   wh why are  she stammered   when ayanokoji enters alone   a little   calmed down  still on the floor   where s hirata kun  she asked   manabe and her friends  i absolutely will not let them get away with that   you have to keep this a secret  if anyone finds out  i ll never forgive you  she warned me   you know  you could get back at manabe and the others  since they re girls  even someone like you could win  she suggested to me   what  are you scared of getting even with manabe and her friends  and you re supposed to be a guy  she chided   so you ll just lie down and take it  she asked   but they would  they ll continue","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p189-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p189-1\">Ch.4 §4.6–4.7: the lowest level<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.189–203<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lured to the switchboard room early, cornered with Rika and Manabe’s trio, beaten under the Milgram frame, then broken open and bound to Ayanokōji with the stairwell photo.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morofuji-rika\">Morofuji Rika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “What’s going on? I can’t connect to… There’s no signal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Wh-what are you doing here?!” she asked, trembling.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I just happened to see you come in here, that’s all.” (Manabe’s line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>54 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The arranged “settle things” becomes the corner: Rika introduced, the bullying past named to her face, hair-grab, knee, the invitation for Rika to join.<span class=\"pg\">p.189-193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, she’s the one,” said Rika. (Rika’s line, tagged in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “H-huh? Who’s apologizing? I haven’t done anything wrong,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Understand what?” asked Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wha—?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, you’re wrong!” Karuizawa denied it, but her words were weak.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “N-no, I won’t! I’ve never done that kind of thing before!” Karuizawa shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> Face to face with the girl she shoved; refuses to kneel; then takes Rika’s instructed slaps while begging forgiveness.<span class=\"pg\">p.189-193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ow, ow! It hurts! Let me go!” screamed Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Agh!” Karuizawa shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-s-s-stop it!” pleaded Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please, forgive me!” Karuizawa pleaded.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The “unusually fearful” tells Manabe the bullying past; Ayanokōji fed her the trauma details in advance — the read was planted, not perceived.<span class=\"pg\">p.190-193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-why are…” she stammered. (when Ayanokōji enters alone)<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A little.” (calmed down, still on the floor)<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Where’s Hirata-kun?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Expects him at four; accepts the teacher-alibi; then “D-did you hear this…from Hirata-kun?” when the past is spoken aloud.<span class=\"pg\">p.195-198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Manabe and her friends… I absolutely will not let them get away with that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have to keep this a secret. If anyone finds out, I’ll never forgive you,” she warned me.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The weakness named: cannot stand being seen as a victim — social standing outranks the wound.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, you could get back at Manabe and the others. Since they’re girls, even someone like you could win,” she suggested to me.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What, are you scared of getting even with Manabe and her friends? And you’re supposed to be a guy,” she chided.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’ll just lie down and take it?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But they would… They’ll continue to do awful things to me,” muttered Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-who are you talking about?!” she shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You, Karuizawa.” (his line)<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “H-hey, what are you doing?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wha—”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “D-did you hear this…from Hirata-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you… Why are you doing this, huh?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “D-don’t screw with me! Who the hell do you think you are?!” she shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What, what do you want with me?! You’re just after my body, aren’t you?” she screamed.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eek!”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You… Grr…” She sputtered.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll never bow to you. I won’t be bullied by the likes of you. You just want to mess with me! You think you can do whatever you want, you pervert?!” she shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, whatever. It’s not like this is the first time someone’s used force against me. So. Did you know about that, too? How do you think I should act in an impossible situation?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After a while, I gave up trying to resist. That’s right; I was everyone’s victim. I became cold, robotic. I could cry, scream, or thrash around, but it didn’t matter. I couldn’t do anything. All I could do was take it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What happened? All sorts of things. Everything and anything. They’d put tacks in my shoes or stuff my desk full of roadkill. When I went to the bathroom, I’d get splashed with dirty water. They wrote words like ‘whore’ on my uniform. They pulled my hair and punched and kicked me. Anything you could imagine, basically. I was bullied in every way. Countless times. What I’ve just told you was just a fraction of what I’ve experienced. Those were the ‘gentler’ ways I’ve been bullied, too. It makes me want to laugh. So, why aren’t you laughing? Why don’t you laugh at the pitiful loser who’s been bullied all her life?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The full inventory delivered as a dare to laugh — resilience named as the reason she enrolled.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-stop!” she shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “U-ugh!”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-what are you…you…” she stammered.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The blade scar on her left side — not simple bullying; a life-threatening attack she stayed tough through.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> From captive to tool: the photo threat, the Class D control offer, the unspoken VIP word — “a parasite couldn’t live without a host.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194-203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. You meant that you can stop Manabe and her friends?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s—” she began. (seeing the stairwell photo)<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? Assist? What do you want me to do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you trying to…”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How am I supposed to help lead them to—”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Named with Hirata as the hosts she used — “much more reliable than Hirata or Machida” is his offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Bound to him: the only way to go on living is with the new host — VIP knowledge implied, not spoken.<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p155-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2–4.4: the seat, the stairwell, the breakup<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p222-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the strap phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-morofuji-rika-y1v4-p189-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho morofuji-rika","q":"ch 4  4 6  the reluctant hand brought to the switchboard room behind manabe  identifies the shove  refuses the first invitation to strike  then slaps and punches under pressure   yeah  she s the one  said rika   n no  i m okay  answered rika   o okay  i ll try   l like that  asked rika","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-morofuji-rika-y1v4-p189-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.6: the reluctant hand<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.189–193<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morofuji-rika\">Morofuji Rika<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Brought to the switchboard room behind Manabe; identifies the shove, refuses the first invitation to strike, then slaps and punches under pressure.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> “Yeah, she’s the one,” said Rika.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> “N-no. I’m okay,” answered Rika.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> “O-okay. I’ll try.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Face to face with the girl who shoved her; “Yeah, she’s the one”; then the instructed slaps that grow forceful while Karuizawa begs.<span class=\"pg\">p.189-193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wanted to refuse the revenge — coerced because Manabe’s anger could redirect; “O-okay. I’ll try.” then Pap → Whap.<span class=\"pg\">p.192-193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “L-Like that?” asked Rika.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The coach: “We’re doing this for your sake”; Rika knew she could be next if she refused.<span class=\"pg\">p.192-193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Hits where marks won’t show — under the uniform, under the hair — fear converted into careful violence (his read of her as the new Milgram subject).<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “She seemed meek, rather like Sakura” — the narrator’s comparison, not a spoken line.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-morofuji-rika-y1v4-p160-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2–4.4: the name behind the corner<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"manabe-shiho yukimura-teruhiko horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 5  5 0 5 2  the phone swap and the dam final day  manabe kept obedient by the stairwell photo  ichinose s card hour  the 5 1 meet with horikita  the sleeping ichinose phone approach  then the group email show where his swapped phone opens the dam   there haven t been any significant changes  at this rate  it looks like the vip is going to get away  how about you   i ll win  she replied flatly   her line  tagged   you sure you haven t made a mistake  i asked   no need  make whatever moves you like   you can t keep being scared of ryuuen forever  you know  i said   in that case  show your face when we discuss things  even if you don t talk  you can follow along  right   i d like to introduce you to someone else later  hirata  too  make sure to keep some time open before they announce the results  i said   think of it as compensation for putting yourself on the front lines  anyway  this person will be useful to us   she must have gotten here early  huh  i asked out loud   oh  no  looks like you slept well   i should be asking you the same thing  when did you get here   any results  i asked   oh no  it s not a bother  i don t mind   well  yeah  of course i do  i ve thought about getting up to class a  no  wait i guess it d probably be more accurate to say that i must aim for class a   nowadays  you can t just enter college or get a job that easily  jobs  especially  i said   but this school  well  it does have an incredible amount of influence  right  most people who get anywh","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p205-1\">Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: the phone swap and the dam<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205–224<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Final day: Manabe kept obedient by the stairwell photo, Ichinose’s card hour, the 5.1 meet with Horikita, the sleeping-Ichinose phone approach, then the group email-show where his swapped phone opens the dam.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “There haven’t been any significant changes. At this rate, it looks like the VIP is going to get away. How about you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’ll win,” she replied flatly. (her line, tagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You sure you haven’t made a mistake?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>37 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Manabe’s constraint: the photo came “from a classmate,” so she cannot pin the sub-account on him or Yukimura with certainty.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The picture effect — obedient, no move against him.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The other stairwell witness she might suspect; both kept outside certainty.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The 5.1 night meet in person (chat leaves traces): “I’ll win,” her anxiety leaking, Hirata brought over, the introduce-someone-later plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.207-209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No need. Make whatever moves you like.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can’t keep being scared of Ryuuen forever, you know,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, show your face when we discuss things. Even if you don’t talk, you can follow along, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to introduce you to someone else later. Hirata, too. Make sure to keep some time open before they announce the results,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Think of it as compensation for putting yourself on the front lines. Anyway, this person will be useful to us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Already on their side; Ayanokōji will handle him so Horikita only has to keep up.<span class=\"pg\">p.207-208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The fear Horikita won’t name in detail — audience risk in the corridor.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Knows Kushida is the Dragon VIP from Hirata; treats Horikita’s confidence as solid victory for the 500,000.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Alone with her sleeping form; approaches the phone, abandons the peek, then takes the Class A dream talk and the points-screen admission.<span class=\"pg\">p.210-217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She must have gotten here early, huh?” I asked out loud.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The pervert-risk test with his foot — gives up the peek; “God, I’m pathetic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210-212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, no. Looks like you slept well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should be asking you the same thing. When did you get here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Any results?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh no, it’s not a bother. I don’t mind.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, yeah. Of course I do. I’ve thought about getting up to Class A. No, wait…I guess it’d probably be more accurate to say that I must aim for Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nowadays, you can’t just enter college or get a job that easily. Jobs, especially,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But this school… Well, it does have an incredible amount of influence, right? Most people who get anywhere in life succeed because … someone influential helps them. Or are you not interested in that, Ichinose?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214-215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Be that as it may, whether or not you can really earn twenty million points is another problem. Even if you score well on the exams and save your points, it probably wouldn’t be enough,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Class D’s financial situation is especially awful. Even though Horikita’s trying her hardest, the points from the island test have yet to be deposited. Actually, it’s entirely possible we’ll lose them in this test,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. When you were using your phone earlier, I just happened to look at the screen. I was a little curious, so I was thinking of asking you about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t plan on telling anyone else. Besides, I might’ve been mistaken. I won’t pry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Have you found a way to win this thing?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I have no idea. We haven’t really been able to talk, which means we haven’t been able to engage,” I said. (official answer)<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The phone-swap trap: Kushida–Horikita switch so a traitor submitting Horikita loses — Outcome #1 for Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re serious about this, huh? Well, if you’re all going to bet on that, I think I’ll join in, too,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sure. After hearing Hamaguchi out, I honestly don’t think we have another option. I’m really bad at communicating, so all I can do is show you the truth,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, Ayanokouji. There’s no way this kind of strategy is going to work,” said Yukimura. (his line)<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The dam image — his email-show opens the hole so the muddy stream can run.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The Professor’s “All alone with Ichinose-dono?” barrages with Yukimura on entry.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yukimura isn’t the VIP. I heard as much earlier,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Denying further would invite suspicion — stops because Yukimura is the swapped VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The withheld truth: he exchanged phones in secret; Class D’s 500,000 was already gambled on the swap.<span class=\"pg\">p.223-224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4: the Sugimura bargain<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: found out, then the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka hamaguchi-tetsuya machida-kouji ichinose-honami","q":"ch 5  5 0 5 2  cards  the dream question  the show fifth discussion still on old maid  lectures yukimura on self reliance  then the early nap  the class a dream talk  and joins hamaguchi s email show   gah  i drew it again  am i seriously this awful at old maid   isn t that excuse too convenient  yukimura kun  if you seriously want to win this thing  don t you think you should rely on yourself  rather than someone else   oh  good yawn to see you  ayanokouji kun  sorry  did my alarm startle you  she asked   ha ha ha  sorry about that  i just passed out  i slept like a log  you re here early  though  don t we have twenty minutes until the discussion  she asked   an hour ago  i think  i wanted some peace and quiet  since my friends are going in and out of my room  it s kinda noisy   besides  i wanted to gather my thoughts  she added   there s still some time left until the discussion starts  why don t we have a little chat  if it s not a bother  that is  she said   okay  to tell you the truth  ayanokouji kun  i want to ask you something  i ve asked all my classmates this question  including the boys  but i ve been thinking about asking the other classes for a while now  i ve just been kind of curious  ayanokouji kun  do you want to ascend to class a   i think so  too  but don t you think placing too must trust in the system could be dangerous  there s something about that 99 9  percent they re not telling us  something dangerous  ichinose said   no  i m not saying that  i want t","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p205-1\">Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: cards, the dream question, the show<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205–223<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fifth discussion still on Old Maid; lectures Yukimura on self-reliance; then the early nap, the Class A dream talk, and joins Hamaguchi’s email show.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Gah! I drew it again! Am I seriously this awful at Old Maid?”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Isn’t that excuse too convenient, Yukimura-kun? If you seriously want to win this thing, don’t you think you should rely on yourself, rather than someone else?”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Oh, good…yawn…to see you, Ayanokouji-kun. Sorry, did my alarm startle you?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>36 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fifth period cards again — no Class A counter to her, so the small group plays rather than sits silent.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “You’re being a downer today, Yukimura-kun. You ought to play with … us and shake off that gloom and doom. Come on, let’s have a rematch!” then the self-reliance rebuke.<span class=\"pg\">p.205-206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sleeping early alone; the thigh-and-phone approach abandoned; the Class A dream conversation; “you saw it, a while back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210-217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha ha, sorry about that. I just passed out; I slept like a log. You’re here early, though. Don’t we have twenty minutes until the discussion?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “An hour ago, I think. I wanted some peace and quiet. Since my friends are going in and out of my room, it’s kinda noisy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, I wanted to gather my thoughts,” she added.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s still some time left until the discussion starts. Why don’t we have a little chat? If it’s not a bother, that is,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. To tell you the truth, Ayanokouji-kun, I want to ask you something. I’ve asked all my classmates this question, including the boys. But I’ve been thinking about asking the other classes for a while now. I’ve just been kind of curious. Ayanokouji-kun, do you want to ascend to Class A?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think so, too. But don’t you think placing too must trust in the system could be dangerous? There’s something about that 99.9% percent they’re not telling us. Something dangerous,” Ichinose said.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The 99.9% placement rate read as a hidden pitfall — only a fraction achieve the dream they set out for.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m not saying that. I want to graduate from Class A. I have a dream I want to make real,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school system’s all well and good, but if you can’t graduate from Class A, it’s a mark of failure. This school is all about ability, and if your abilities can’t carry you here, it’s unlikely you’ll ever be labeled an elite. Students are ranked based on perceived superiority or inferiority. Right now, between the two of us, Ayanokouji-kun, only one can achieve their dream. Ah, but then again, we could both lose out on our goals.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm? You mean when someone manages to accumulate twenty million points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh yeah, for sure. I suppose if we factor that in, it’s possible for both of us to graduate from Class A,” she replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true. Even if you’re extremely economical, it’s unlikely someone could manage to save even half that amount,” Ichinose mused.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm, I wonder about that. Personally, I’ll use points sometimes and save them sometimes, just like anyone else would. Even though I’m in Class B, I don’t really have that many points saved.” Ichinose responded to my question with ease.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like you saw it, a while back,” she remarked.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Caught the screen glance; not angry — “it certainly is a lot of points, right?” — the insane first-semester pile he can’t match even saving every monthly drop.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha, you don’t need to feel guilty or anything. It’s not like I’m blaming you. I mean, it certainly is a lot of points, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I can’t really give you any details. Sorry,” she added.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, if you did manage to obtain that information, Ayanokouji-kun, and even if you shared it with Horikita-san, you wouldn’t go blabbing to everyone, would you? I mean, even though you saw my phone, if someone else decided to ask about it, you wouldn’t tell, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm, I think so. At least, I think I’ve found a hint.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We won’t know that until the end. My path to victory is—” (cut off by the room filling)<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> His Outcome #1 plan is “exactly the same” as hers; she backs the show and follows his lead to the punch.<span class=\"pg\">p.217-220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, what’s this? You’re here already, Ayanokouji?” (Yukimura’s line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that really true, Hamaguchi?” (her line in the group exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s hear him out first. Hamaguchi-kun isn’t the sort to speak without thinking,” offered Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it’s a surprisingly good strategy. I don’t have any objections,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve been agonizing over this for a long time now, but after hearing Hamaguchi’s plan, I get it.” (group exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun…are you okay with this?” Ichinose asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Explains her earlier “quiet about something” as wanting the same show — Class B’s representative jealous Hamaguchi beat her to it.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s too early to draw any conclusions. Yukimura-kun has a point,” Ichinose said.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I got a little caught up and missed my chance earlier, but I’ll show you now,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Proves not the VIP after the interruption — the calm repair under Machida’s probe.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, that? I had the same thing Hamaguchi said on my mind earlier, and wanted to talk about it. That’s it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As Class B’s representative, I’m a little jealous that Hamaguchi-kun beat me to the punch.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the deck VIP exchange<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the call that ends it<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 5  5 0  the iron fortress still running named in the final day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate   no counter to ichinose s cards  strategy unbroken","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p205-1\">Ch.5 §5.0: the iron fortress still running<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the final-day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate — no counter to Ichinose’s cards, strategy unbroken.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The pair of strategies the narration sets against Ichinose’s missing countermeasure — frontal assault versus iron fortress.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Still no counter from Class B to his silence; that is why cards win the hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence in this half; the row records the opening status line.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p140-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the castle gate holds<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p226-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: instructions, faction, the defensive vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 5  5 0  the frontal assault still running named in the final day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate   united frontal assault against katsuragi s fortress","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\">Ch.5 §5.0: the frontal assault still running<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the final-day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate — united frontal assault against Katsuragi’s fortress.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The two strategies Ichinose has not answered; the chapter opens between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Still the fear she won’t detail under listener risk at the 5.1 meet.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence in this half; the row records the opening status line.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the shade meeting and the planted phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the sixth guest<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio machida-kouji sotomura-hideo karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 5  5 0 5 2  the vip steps forward melancholy at the card table  the self reliance rebuke  then under the email show pressure he demands phones on the table and reveals himself as the rabbit vip   after ayanokoji s secret swap   is it okay to just sit here like this  yukimura sighed   no thanks  i don t really feel like it  really  is this okay  ichinose san  i mean  just doing this until the test ends  i thought you were the one leading the group here   yeah  good point  he answered   all alone with ichinose dono  my word  how suspicious  a clandestine rendezvous  wouldn t you say   professor s line  in exchange   wait  ayanokouji  there s no way this kind of strategy is going to work  said yukimura   wait  it s not just ayanokouji kun  you re going along with this  karuizawa  you agree with this  yukimura was puzzled   do you really think that   showing everyone your phone is the right move  he asked   to the professor  yukimura s expression stiffened   ibuki s vip jibe   before i do so  i want you to promise me one thing  he said   i don t want anyone here to turn traitor  especially you  class a  i want you to take out your phones and put them in front of you  that goes for everybody  everyone  put your phones where i can see them  he demanded   exactly what i said  nothing more  nothing less   i m sorry for lying to you  ayanokouji  he muttered   i m the vip","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p205-1\">Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: the VIP steps forward<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205–224<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Melancholy at the card table, the self-reliance rebuke, then under the email-show pressure he demands phones on the table and reveals himself as the Rabbit VIP — after Ayanokōji’s secret swap.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Is it okay to just sit here like this?” Yukimura sighed.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “No thanks. I don’t really feel like it. Really, is this okay, Ichinose-san? I mean, just doing this until the test ends. I thought you were the one leading the group here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Yeah. Good point,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Knows he can’t take the leadership thrust on him but still wants a way to change things; academic top ≠ natural leader (narration).<span class=\"pg\">p.205-206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The downer at her table; takes the “rely on yourself” rebuke.<span class=\"pg\">p.205-206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yukimura-dono” and the Professor’s joint barrage; tries to stop the show; then “I’m sorry for lying to you, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217, 220, 223-224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “All alone with Ichinose-dono? My word, how suspicious. A clandestine rendezvous, wouldn’t you say?” (Professor’s line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, Ayanokouji. There’s no way this kind of strategy is going to work,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. It’s not just Ayanokouji-kun? You’re going along with this, Karuizawa? You agree with this?” Yukimura was puzzled.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you really think that … showing everyone your phone is the right move?” he asked. (to the Professor)<span class=\"pg\">p.222-223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Yukimura’s expression stiffened. (Ibuki’s VIP jibe)<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Her “You’re not the VIP, are you?” freezes him — the jibe that starts the Class A stare.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Before I do so, I want you to promise me one thing,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t want anyone here to turn traitor. Especially you, Class A. I want you to take out your phones and put them in front of you. That goes for everybody. Everyone, put your phones where I can see them,” he demanded.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly what I said. Nothing more, nothing less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry for lying to you, Ayanokouji,” he muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m the VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Watches the private email and chat logs; confirms authenticity for the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Wha— Y-Yukimura-dono, you’re the VIP?!” the Professor stammers.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Her genuine shock is the cover for the swap — Class D’s surprise sells the lie.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The VIP email on screen; Class D’s 500,000 given up in the room — but the phones were already exchanged in secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “If I’d known things would turn out like this, I would’ve talked from the start…” — the regret that makes the reveal human.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p155-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the stairwell<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the cover holds, then cracks<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p207-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune","q":"ch 5  5 1  the night meet last pre final meeting with ayanokoji in person  claims the win flatly  refuses detail on listener risk  and takes the hirata recruitment plan with gritted teeth   i ll win  she replied flatly   i m not sure who might be listening to us right now  so i won t go into detail  i ll just ask that you believe in me  everything will be fine   did you want to consult with me  she asked   so what did you want to talk about  i thought we both agreed to avoid unnecessary contact   judging from how you phrased that  i m guessing you can do something about it   i don t particularly want that  she said   i don t really like how freely you re operating in the shadows  she answered   well  i suppose so  she sighed   okay  i really don t like this  i don t want you to just go ahead and recruit people as you see fit  she snapped   i have a general idea of what you re thinking  but  well  fine  at any rate  let s meet back here after the test is over   i wonder how many traitors will come forward in this test  said horikita   yes  i think so  too  horikita briefly averted her eyes  the sort of unconscious gesture people made when they were worried about something   nothing  it s just  well  something about this test doesn t make sense  but there shouldn t be any mistakes  i definitely shouldn t lose  she replied","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p207-1\">Ch.5 §5.1: the night meet<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.207–209<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Last pre-final meeting with Ayanokóji in person; claims the win flatly, refuses detail on listener risk, and takes the Hirata/recruitment plan with gritted teeth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’ll win,” she replied flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’m not sure who might be listening to us right now, so I won’t go into detail. I’ll just ask that you believe in me. Everything will be fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Did you want to consult with me?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Confidence despite the odds — Ayanokōji already knows Kushida is Dragon VIP and reads this as solid victory.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Person-to-person because chat leaves traces; “Make whatever moves you like”; snaps at free shadow operation.<span class=\"pg\">p.207-209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what did you want to talk about? I thought we both agreed to avoid unnecessary contact.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Judging from how you phrased that, I’m guessing you can do something about it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t particularly want that,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t really like how freely you’re operating in the shadows,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose so,” she sighed.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, I really don’t like this. I don’t want you to just go ahead and recruit people as you see fit,” she snapped.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have a general idea of what you’re thinking, but… Well, fine. At any rate, let’s meet back here after the test is over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The cooperation she does not want — “I don’t particularly want that” — Ayanokōji will handle him alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder how many traitors will come forward in this test,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, I think so, too.” Horikita briefly averted her eyes, the sort of unconscious gesture people made when they were worried about something.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing. It’s just, well… Something about this test doesn’t make sense. But there shouldn’t be any mistakes. I definitely shouldn’t lose,” she replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Anxiety finally leaking — the averted eyes, then the “doesn’t make sense” line; he stays quiet because kind words would be refused.<span class=\"pg\">p.208-209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His pursuit is the fear she won’t name under listener risk.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p125-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p230-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: the plan’s author, then the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p207-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 5  5 1  named in the vip arithmetic named only as one of the dragon group who surely worked to learn the vip   horikita s win still surprises ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p207-1\">Ch.5 §5.1: named in the VIP arithmetic<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.207<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as one of the Dragon group who surely worked to learn the VIP — Horikita’s win still surprises Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The pair he expects to have exhausted every angle on Kushida’s screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The Dragon VIP both sides were hunting — Hirata’s tip already gave Ayanokōji the answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; one line of the VIP arithmetic.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p143-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the Dragon deadlock<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p207-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 5  5 1 5 2  the dragon vip behind the swap named as the dragon group s vip from hirata s tip   the name ayanokoji s phone swap trap runs on  never spoken in the room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p207-1\">Ch.5 §5.1–5.2: the Dragon VIP behind the swap<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.207, 217<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the Dragon group’s VIP from Hirata’s tip — the name Ayanokōji’s phone-swap trap runs on, never spoken in the room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The source of the identification; “I’d already heard from Hirata that Kushida was the Dragon group’s VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The swap pairs her phone with Kushida’s so a traitor submitting Horikita fails.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The hidden mechanism of Outcome #1 — she never appears on screen in this half.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; the row records the fact the plan depends on.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p185-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.5: the fallback contact<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p239-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the name that broke the table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p217-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka machida-kouji ichinose-honami beppu-ryouta hamaguchi-tetsuya","q":"ch 5  5 2  the outcome  1 plan arrives with yukimura and the professor  then stakes the final hour on a voluntary email show   the plan that matches ayanokoji s swap by accident   this is the end  huh  so  have you found any hints  asked hamaguchi   for the past three days  i ve been thinking of how we could achieve outcome  1  he said   there is a way for everyone here to achieve outcome  1  he continued   yes  i came up with this idea after listening to everyone here  including ichinose san and machida kun   i m going to show you all my phone  of course  the school sent us all an email  i think you all understand what i m getting at  because we re prohibited from tampering with or misrepresenting the emails we ve received in any way  there s no way to deceive one another  that s why the answer is simple  we show each other our emails  and then we find out who the vip is  that s how we ll discover the truth   it s certainly true that if the vip knows they could be betrayed  they wouldn t show their phone  however  from the perspective of someone who isn t the vip  there s no risk in exposing your identity  the test will be over soon  if we don t make a move  we lose our chance of winning  suppose there s a class working together to cover for the vip  it s true that none of them would show their phones  but this way  it s possible to narrow down the list of candidates   in that case  please be quiet and just watch  if you don t participate  machida kun  it ll still be fine  h","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p217-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html#sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p217-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the Outcome #1 plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.217–220<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives with Yukimura and the Professor, then stakes the final hour on a voluntary email show — the plan that matches Ayanokōji’s swap by accident.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#beppu-ryouta\">Beppu Ryōta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “This is the end, huh? So, have you found any hints?” asked Hamaguchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “For the past three days, I’ve been thinking of how we could achieve Outcome #1,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “There is a way for everyone here to achieve Outcome #1,” he continued.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gentle lead-in; simultaneous “excuse me” with him; then the plan that shatters the swap timing.<span class=\"pg\">p.217-220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I came up with this idea after listening to everyone here, including Ichinose-san and Machida-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to show you all my phone. Of course, the school sent us all an email. I think you all understand what I’m getting at? Because we’re prohibited from tampering with or misrepresenting the emails we’ve received in any way, there’s no way to deceive one another. That’s why the answer is simple. We show each other our emails, and then we find out who the VIP is. That’s how we’ll discover the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Email-show logic: school messages cannot be tampered with, so the screen is the only proof.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The flat refusal exchange — Machida calls it dumb, Hamaguchi tells him to sit quiet if he won’t participate.<span class=\"pg\">p.218-219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s certainly true that if the VIP knows they could be betrayed, they wouldn’t show their phone. However, from the perspective of someone who isn’t the VIP, there’s no risk in exposing your identity. The test will be over soon. If we don’t make a move, we lose our chance of winning. Suppose there’s a class working together to cover for the VIP. It’s true that none of them would show their phones. But this way, it’s possible to narrow down the list of candidates.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, please be quiet and just watch. If you don’t participate, Machida-kun, it’ll still be fine,” Hamaguchi answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> His plan is “exactly the same” as hers and Ayanokōji’s — the three-way coincidence of the final hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.217-220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Beppu Ryōta<\/b> Beppu follows his phone first among Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The idea came “after listening to everyone” — Ichinose’s card-hour intelligence put to work.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p153-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the second denial<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p227-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the SIM experiment<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p218-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hamaguchi-tetsuya ichinose-honami yukimura-teruhiko machida-kouji","q":"ch 5  5 2  the flat refusal and the audit refuses hamaguchi s show as naive  then audits yukimura s revealed vip screen for the room   i can t believe it  there s no way we can arrive at outcome  1 without discussion  machida huffed   this is dumb  why would anyone show their phone just because you told us to  someone could betray us all the moment we show our emails  no one would do this  answered machida flatly   even if you find out the vip s identity or the class they belong to  the moment someone decides to betray you  it s over  the problem hasn t been resolved  or are you suggesting that the first to betray us wins  countered machida   wait  ichinose  earlier  you said you d been keeping quiet about something until now  machida clearly hadn t forgotten   the same thing   what are you talking about   to yukimura s phone demand   well  fine  whatever  if you want to see my phone  here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p218-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html#sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p218-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the flat refusal and the audit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.218–224<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Refuses Hamaguchi’s show as naive, then audits Yukimura’s revealed VIP screen for the room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “I can’t believe it. There’s no way we can arrive at Outcome #1 without discussion,” Machida huffed.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “This is dumb. Why would anyone show their phone just because you told us to? Someone could betray us all the moment we show our emails. No one would do this,” answered Machida flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “Even if you find out the VIP’s identity or the class they belong to, the moment someone decides to betray you, it’s over. The problem hasn’t been resolved. Or are you suggesting that the first to betray us wins?” countered…”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you find out the VIP’s identity or the class they belong to, the moment someone decides to betray you, it’s over. The problem hasn’t been resolved. Or are you suggesting that the first to betray us wins?” countered Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> The two-round refusal — Hamaguchi’s “please be quiet and just watch” ends it for Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.218-219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Naturally, Machida-kun was flabbergasted” at the hope on everyone’s faces.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Probes her earlier silence — “Earlier, you said you’d been keeping quiet about something until now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, Ichinose. Earlier, you said you’d been keeping quiet about something until now?” Machida clearly hadn’t forgotten.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The same thing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Stares inquisitively through the silence; then checks the private email and chat logs: “The email seems authentic. All of the other personal emails are Yukimura’s, so there’s no room for error.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you talking about?” (to Yukimura’s phone demand)<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, fine. Whatever. If you want to see my phone, here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The only student who verifies the VIP screen with logs — Class A’s technical audit of the reveal.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p155-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the seat arbitration<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the audit overturned<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-beppu-ryouta-y1v4-p219-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hamaguchi-tetsuya ichinose-honami beppu-ryouta","q":"ch 5  5 2  the second phone first class b student to follow hamaguchi s show after he opens his email","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-beppu-ryouta-y1v4-p219-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2: the second phone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.219<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#beppu-ryouta\">Beppu Ryōta<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">First Class B student to follow Hamaguchi’s show after he opens his email.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “I agree with Hamaguchi-kun. I’ll show mine, too.” — the coordinated Class B start, not a spur-of-the-moment idea.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Read as her strategy reaching the table — Hamaguchi and Beppu move as one.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> One line in the room; no further action in this half.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p222-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"manabe-shiho hamaguchi-tetsuya yukimura-teruhiko ibuki-mio","q":"ch 5  5 2  the lone girl agrees the unexpected first volunteer after ayanokoji   threatens manabe into the show with the vip or class logic   anyone who isn t the vip or who s not in the same class as a vip gains nothing if things keep going like this  class b understands that  if we sit around  we won t catch up to the classes above us  that s why they re showing everyone their phones  i agree with their idea  she answered   or maybe you re the vip  said ibuki   in that case  show everyone your phone   you know  you ve been really jumpy  you re not the vip  are you  ibuki asked","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p222-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the lone girl agrees<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.222–223<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The unexpected first volunteer after Ayanokōji — threatens Manabe into the show with the VIP-or-class logic.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “Anyone who isn’t the VIP or who’s not in the same class as a VIP gains nothing if things keep going like this. Class B understands that. If we sit around, we won’t catch up to the classes above us. That’s why they’re showing…”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “Or maybe you’re the VIP,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “In that case, show everyone your phone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyone who isn’t the VIP or who’s not in the same class as a VIP gains nothing if things keep going like this. Class B understands that. If we sit around, we won’t catch up to the classes above us. That’s why they’re showing everyone their phones. I agree with their idea,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Enemy tone, not ally: “Or maybe you’re the VIP” → “In that case, show everyone your phone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222-223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Backs his plan as Class B’s shared interest — the classes above only move if the lower ones show.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “a lone girl agreed” among the scoffers — the first volunteer after the swap phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “You know, you’ve been really jumpy. You’re not the VIP, are you?” Ibuki asked. — the jibe that freezes him.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, you’ve been really jumpy. You’re not the VIP, are you?” Ibuki asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the absent buffer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p222-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 5  5 2  the strap phone hands over the phone with the strap under the show  claims private points motive  shock at yukimura s vip email sells the room   i m doing this for my own sake  i want those private points  said karuizawa  karuizawa looked genuinely shocked and uneasy   narration of her face at the reveal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p222-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the strap phone<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.222–224<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hands over the phone with the strap under the show; claims private-points motive; shock at Yukimura’s VIP email sells the room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I’m doing this for my own sake. I want those private points,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Karuizawa looked genuinely shocked and uneasy. (narration of her face at the reveal)<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Puzzled at first that she joins; then genuine shock and unease at “I’m the VIP” — the cover performance Ayanokōji needs.<span class=\"pg\">p.222-224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her clean email supports the swap dam; no word to him in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The points line matches her standing greed — motive nobody questions for showing.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p189-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.6–4.7: the lowest level<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p231-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: named, then seated<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p222-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho","q":"ch 5  5 2  the shouted objection screams that the show gains nothing  then is ordered into it by ibuki and complies with her friends   are you nuts  we don t get anything out of this  shouted manabe","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p222-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the shouted objection<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.222–223<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Screams that the show gains nothing, then is ordered into it by Ibuki and complies with her friends.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Are you nuts? We don’t get anything out of this!” shouted Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The enemy-tone exchange: “Or maybe you’re the VIP” → “N-no. I…” → “In that case, show everyone your phone.” She and her friends obey.<span class=\"pg\">p.222-223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> In the same forced-show wave as Karuizawa’s strapped phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Accepts Ibuki’s order like a command — the cornering leader reduced to complying in the circle.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p185-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.5–4.6: the anonymous buyer and the subject<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the nod and the exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p225-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ichinose-honami karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke sudou-ken ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 5  5 2 5 3  found out  then the cafe the password show settles yukimura s cover in the room  ichinose s call and sim lock lecture strip the double swap bare  then the 11 p m  cafe with karuizawa  hirata  horikita  sudou and ryuuen  the twelve group results  and a warning over class c s lead   i m sorry  yukimura kun  this happened because i came up with this idea at the very last minute  i muttered   yeah  guess so  i answered   not especially  i can t do anything but believe  anyway  i m heading to my room   horikita  of course   a huge success  don t you mean a crushing defeat  we failed  hard  you saw through everything   i m sorry  sorry for trying to deceive you like that  especially after i agreed to be your ally  are you angry   i see  if you mean it  i m sure horikita will be relieved   the critical part   the same as you  i would ve tried to find out who the vip was  borrowed that person s phone  and had another one ready  then  i d step forward and claim to be the vip myself   so i ve been found out  huh   why did you think it was karuizawa  i asked   why didn t you say anything  at the very least  you could have exposed my lie  i said   machida   you ought to praise horikita  she just gave me directions  that s all   don t worry  i m positive that one of the guys from class a sent the school an email with my name  i answered   sorry for calling you so late   his line to karuizawa   she s the type to come at the very last second  we have another four minutes  i s","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p225-1\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: found out, then the café<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.225–243<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The password-show settles Yukimura’s cover in the room; Ichinose’s call and SIM-lock lecture strip the double swap bare; then the 11 p.m. café with Karuizawa, Hirata, Horikita, Sudou and Ryuuen, the twelve-group results, and a warning over Class C’s lead.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+3 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m sorry, Yukimura-kun. This happened because I came up with this idea at the very last minute,” I muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yeah. Guess so,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Not especially. I can’t do anything but believe, anyway. I’m heading to my room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>36 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Names the real weakness of the password theatre: judging whose phone it was stayed hard, but the six-digit unlock “wasn’t the result of deduction, but rather of preconceived notions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Takes the fall as the points-grabber everyone now believes him to be.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The long reveal chain: her call, the SIM lecture, the Hoshinomiya-sensei unlock, the Karuizawa guess, and the mutual “we’re even.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225-233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita, of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A huge success? Don’t you mean a crushing defeat? We failed, hard. You saw through everything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. Sorry for trying to deceive you like that, especially after I agreed to be your ally. Are you angry?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. If you mean it, I’m sure Horikita will be relieved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The critical part?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The same as you. I would’ve tried to find out who the VIP was, borrowed that person’s phone, and had another one ready. Then, I’d step forward and claim to be the VIP myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So I’ve been found out, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why did you think it was Karuizawa?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why didn’t you say anything? At the very least, you could have exposed my lie,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Machida?”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You ought to praise Horikita. She just gave me directions, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The full chain on the page: Hirata told him Karuizawa was the real VIP; Manabe’s bullying of Karuizawa opened the swap; he replicated email and call history, paid for a SIM lock release, transferred his number, then swapped that phone with Yukimura’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The trap’s shape on the page: a simple person misses the swap, a clever person accuses him, “But they never would have come to the conclusion that Karuizawa was the real VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The real VIP and phone owner — the fact kept even from Yukimura until Ichinose named her.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata’s withheld knowledge, then the café approach about “that piece of paper.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231, 234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I’m positive that one of the guys from Class A sent the school an email with my name,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry for calling you so late.” (his line to Karuizawa)<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s the type to come at the very last second. We have another four minutes,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re finally here. Hey, who’s that behind you?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The café fifth wheel; his “one step behind” on the email; Ryuuen’s arrival makes him half-threaten and then sink back on command.<span class=\"pg\">p.235-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Someone discovered his identity,” I reasoned. (Minami, Horse VIP)<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Minami-kun was the Horse group VIP” — two Minami rows exist in the roster; which one is not settled on this page.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is Yamauchi okay?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know who it was, but betraying the group before he could was a fine move,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The planted sixth guest; the Kushida reveal; the Class A VIP list; the explicit next-target threat; Ayanokōji’s quiet “we might be in trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237-243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I mean, it’s not really a difficult problem. If you just put your mind to it, it’s relatively simple,” I told everyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Putting aside how Ryuuen found out the VIPs’ identities, all he had to do was tell everyone ‘Kushida is the VIP’ before the end of the test, right? Of course, no one would believe what someone like Ryuuen says. Especially a group of such intelligent, gifted people. However, the final half hour was different. Even if you answered incorrectly, there wasn’t any risk to class points. As such, even someone who’d been playing defensively like Katsuragi could vote, right? If there was even a 1% chance that Kushida was really the VIP, then they would’ve gotten Outcome #1, which was the most convenient for everyone involved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The defensive player who could still vote in the riskless half hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Kouenji saved our asses” — his betrayal email kept Class C from taking everything; the stray bullets hit other VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita. I think that we might be in trouble,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve got a point. I’m probably overthinking things. Don’t worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The premonition named as “something like excitement” — first stirrings of wanting Ryuuen as an opponent.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The café debrief, the results, and the shared worry she talks him out of.<span class=\"pg\">p.235-243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: the phone swap and the dam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p225-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko machida-kouji hamaguchi-tetsuya hoshinomiya-chie karuizawa-kei morishige-takurou sakayanagi-arisu katsuragi-kouhei ichinose-honami","q":"ch 5  5 2  the call that ends it pleads with class a for outcome  1  then exposes the phone swap by calling it  lectures on the sim lock she confirmed with hoshinomiya sensei  and admits she never intended to clear or betray   please  cooperate with us  don t let yukimura kun s courage go to waste  i don t want you to betray us   the school said that altering or copying the emails is forbidden  that s true  that s why the email we saw was the real thing  however  there s no rule saying that you can t trick people with the phone itself  do you understand what i m getting at   the person this phone belongs to  the real vip that s you  isn t it  ayanokouji kun  i called you just now  not yukimura kun   that was all fake  he could ve easily gotten the password ahead of time by simply asking ayanokouji kun  besides  it s possible to replicate call history  email  apps  and so on  though it would take a bit of effort  said ichinose   but you see  there s a weak point to that strategy  a phone number  even if you perfectly duplicate everything from call history to apps  you can t change the number  hamaguchi and i had tried swapping sim cards once to see what would happen  but the sim cards are locked to their designated phones  if you d swapped them  i wouldn t have been able to call you  it doesn t matter who switches with whom  once i hear the phone ring  i can find the owner  if i couldn t do that  i wouldn t have proposed this idea in the first place  said ichinose   you did ev","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p225-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the call that ends it<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.225–233<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pleads with Class A for Outcome #1, then exposes the phone swap by calling it, lectures on the SIM lock she confirmed with Hoshinomiya-sensei, and admits she never intended to clear or betray.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morishige-takurou\">Morishige Takurō<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Please. Cooperate with us. Don’t let Yukimura-kun’s courage go to waste. I don’t want you to betray us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “The school said that altering or copying the emails is forbidden, that’s true. That’s why the email we saw was the real thing. However, there’s no rule saying that you can’t trick people with the phone itself. Do you understand…”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “The person this phone belongs to, the real VIP…that’s you, isn’t it? Ayanokouji-kun? I called you just now, not Yukimura-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Thanks his courage; he is already the sacrificial cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Extracts his trust promise for Outcome #1 before Class A leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.225-228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school said that altering or copying the emails is forbidden, that’s true. That’s why the email we saw was the real thing. However, there’s no rule saying that you can’t trick people with the phone itself. Do you understand what I’m getting at?”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The dropped phone, caller ID “Ichinose,” and the quiet hang-up — only Yukimura and Ayanokōji understand the trap as it fires.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was all fake. He could’ve easily gotten the password ahead of time by simply asking Ayanokouji-kun. Besides, it’s possible to replicate call history, email, apps, and so on, though it would take a bit of effort,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> The SIM-card test they ran together — the weak point of every swap strategy.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But you see, there’s a weak point to that strategy: a phone number. Even if you perfectly duplicate everything from call history to apps, you can’t change the number. Hamaguchi and I had tried swapping SIM cards once to see what would happen, but the SIM cards are locked to their designated phones. If you’d swapped them, I wouldn’t have been able to call you. It doesn’t matter who switches with whom: Once I hear the phone ring, I can find the owner. If I couldn’t do that, I wouldn’t have proposed this idea in the first place,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You did everything almost perfectly. But you didn’t anticipate that our SIM cards are locked to specific devices, did you?” Ichinose gloated.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, we’ve confirmed that Ayanokouji-kun is the VIP. Machidakun, promise me that we’ll aim for Outcome #1, and no one will betray anyone else,” urged Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s so much to gain by working together. That’s why we’ll never turn traitor. That’s why I want you in Class C to do the same. Please, just bear with it for thirty minutes,” Ichinose pleaded.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now all we can do is to trust everyone,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re really calm, Ayanokouji-kun. Aren’t you worried?”<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who came up with the idea of swapping phones?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Please tell Horikita-san something for me. Tell her that her plan was a huge success.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha ha. You didn’t expect us to have come up with the same plan, did you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course not. We went ahead with our own plan without telling you, so we’re even.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on. You’re surprisingly bad at dealing with people, Ayanokouji-kun. It’s true that the SIM cards are locked to their respective devices. But there is a way to release that lock. Isn’t that right? I checked with Hoshinomiya-sensei to confirm. She said that with enough points, you can unlock the device right away,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The teacher she consulted — enough points buys an instant SIM unlock.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After a falsehood comes to light, most people will take the answer that comes after it to be the truth. Yukimura-kun was determined not to be the … VIP, even after he showed everyone how he unlocked your phone using the password.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230-231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The moment that lie was revealed, the truth that you’re the VIP came to the surface. The SIM card was the deciding factor. No one would suspect anyone else as the VIP now. But that was the trap. I said the idea of swapping phones was an imperfect strategy, but that was a lie. That’s because swapping phones is extremely effective. Of course, it must be a doublelayered trap in order to work. In that case, the truth will remain in the darkness. There wouldn’t be any way for anyone to determine, with 100% accuracy, the real VIP’s identity.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the plan behind the plan — the double-layer trap Ayanokōji kept from Yukimura, named in one pass.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Names her as the real VIP in the typed message: “The real VIP is Karuizawa Kei-san. Am I right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.231-232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The behavioural read: Karuizawa “kept looking over at you, and her face tightened” — enough to type, not enough to send.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The same reason as Yukimura-kun. She’s been behaving unusually. She normally doesn’t seem to care much about you, Ayanokouji-kun, but she kept looking over at you, and her face tightened. But there’s still the possibility that she isn’t the VIP, so I couldn’t have sent that email.”<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s obvious. If either Class A or Class C makes a mistake, that’s a win for us. From the very beginning, I never intended to clear Outcome #1, or to turn traitor and get Outcome #3. The moment I knew the VIP wasn’t in Class B, I knew I would let another class betray us. I think the traitor was probably from Class A,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishige Takurō<\/b> Her traitor guess: Sakayanagi’s faction man who would not sit on Katsuragi’s plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Her faction named as the reason Morishige would break rank.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The plan Morishige was expected to disobey.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, no. Morishige-kun. He’s a member of Sakayanagi’s faction. I doubt he’d just quietly go along with Katsuragi’s plan. He probably figured that, if anything, it was better for him to betray the group and take the points. Don’t you think?”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun, you’re amazing. You know that? Our conversation just now proves how cunning you really are, doesn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-what does this mean?” asked Ichinose. (the four-note alert)<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The four-times-quick sound on both phones — the shock face before §5.3.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: cards, the dream question, the show<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p225-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"manabe-shiho katsuragi-kouhei yukimura-teruhiko ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka machida-kouji","q":"ch 5  5 2  the audit overturned accepts the yukimura verdict after the password show  then loses the argument to ichinose s call and sim lecture   his log check is declared fake   and leaves with a promise for outcome  1   so that means it s definitely yukimura kun  manabe nodded   he anchors the room s conclusion   we ve been acting on katsuragi san s instructions from the very beginning  we won t do anything on our own  answered machida   what are you doing  ichinose  there s no point in calling yukimura s phone at a time like this  said machida  looking suspicious   b but isn t that odd  yukimura unlocked the phone right in front of us  i checked his private email history just to be sure  said machida   too bad  yukimura  it was a surprisingly good try  though  said machida  he and the others laughed  furthering the mockery   yes  of course  you can trust me  let s go  machida said","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html#sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p225-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the audit overturned<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.225–228<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Accepts the Yukimura verdict after the password-show, then loses the argument to Ichinose’s call and SIM lecture — his log-check is declared fake — and leaves with a promise for Outcome #1.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “So that means it’s definitely Yukimura-kun.” Manabe nodded. (he anchors the room’s conclusion)<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “We’ve been acting on Katsuragi-san’s instructions from the very beginning. We won’t do anything on our own,” answered Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “What are you doing, Ichinose? There’s no point in calling Yukimura’s phone at a time like this,” said Machida, looking suspicious.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Her nod makes the verdict joint — Class A and C together.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The chain of command cited under pressure — no自主 action.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “B-but isn’t that odd? Yukimura unlocked the phone right in front of us. I checked his private email history just to be sure,” said Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His log audit — the exact check Ichinose demolishes as fakeable.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Too bad, Yukimura. It was a surprisingly good try, though,” said Machida. He and the others laughed, furthering the mockery.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The mockery after the drop; Class A’s amusement at the failed swap.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Takes her Outcome #1 promise and exits first with the other two Class A students.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, of course. You can trust me. Let’s go,” Machida said.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Glances at the complicit one on the way out — suspicion parked, not resolved.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p218-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2: the flat refusal and the audit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p225-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"machida-kouji yukimura-teruhiko ichinose-honami manabe-shiho","q":"ch 5  5 2  the nod and the exit ratifies the yukimura verdict  then leaves with her group once ichinose extracts the no betrayal pledge   so that means it s definitely yukimura kun   machida s line  with her nod","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p225-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the nod and the exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.225–228<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ratifies the Yukimura verdict, then leaves with her group once Ichinose extracts the no-betrayal pledge.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “So that means it’s definitely Yukimura-kun.” (Machida’s line, with her nod)<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The joint Class A/C conclusion — her nod is cited as the confirming beat.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Accepts him as the answer without testing whose phone it was.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration: the password-show worked because preconceived notions beat deduction — she never questions the owner.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Nods at the thirty-minute plea and leaves with the rest of Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No further line of her own; the row records her presence in the verdict and exit.<span class=\"pg\">p.225-228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p222-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2: the shouted objection<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p225-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 5  5 2  named in the cover trio yukimura cites him as one of the three who agree the reveal was for the best","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p225-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: named in the cover trio<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.225<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yukimura cites him as one of the three who agree the reveal was for the best.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I’m sure you, Sotomura, and Karuizawa would agree this was for the best.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The third of the trio — the real VIP neither of them knew about yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Mention only in this half; no line of his own.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p155-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the chair and the exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p225-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"sotomura-hideo karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami machida-kouji yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 5  5 2  the cover holds  then cracks accepts the blame as the points grabber  begs every class to trust outcome  1  and rages when ichinose s call exposes the swap    too bad  from machida is the last he hears before the room empties   no  it s okay  it s probably for the best  i thought i could lie my way out of this  but i was wrong  i m sure you  sotomura  and karuizawa would agree this was for the best  said yukimura   well  now everyone knows the answer  it s me  yukimura said   i want to believe  no  i do believe in everyone  yukimura begged fervently   damn it  shouted yukimura   i was wrong to go along with your plan  this sucks  he fumed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p225-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the cover holds, then cracks<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.225–228<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Accepts the blame as the points-grabber, begs every class to trust Outcome #1, and rages when Ichinose’s call exposes the swap — “Too bad” from Machida is the last he hears before the room empties.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “No, it’s okay. It’s probably for the best. I thought I could lie my way out of this, but I was wrong. I’m sure you, Sotomura, and Karuizawa would agree this was for the best,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Well, now everyone knows the answer. It’s me,” Yukimura said.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I want to believe… No, I do believe in everyone.” Yukimura begged fervently.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Named in the trio who all agree the reveal was for the best.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Same trio — the real VIP he still does not know about.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Everyone now pictures him hoarding points for himself — the role he agreed to play.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The joy at winning the cover dies the moment the phone vibrates; he lunges, drops it face-up, caller ID “Ichinose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226-228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn it!” shouted Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was wrong to go along with your plan. This sucks,” he fumed.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her call is what breaks him; Machida’s “Too bad, Yukimura” piles on the mockery.<span class=\"pg\">p.225-228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The mockery line after the drop — Class A laughs at the failed gambit.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Leaves the room visibly upset and shaking; the VIP cover traded for a public traitor face.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: the VIP steps forward<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p226-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"machida-kouji morishige-takurou sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 5  5 2 5 3  instructions  faction  the defensive vote the chain machida cites  the plan morishige was expected to disobey  and the defensive player example in ayanokoji s dragon outcome  1 explanation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p226-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p226-1\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: instructions, faction, the defensive vote<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.226, 233, 242<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The chain Machida cites, the plan Morishige was expected to disobey, and the defensive-player example in Ayanokōji’s Dragon Outcome #1 explanation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morishige-takurou\">Morishige Takurō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “We’ve been acting on Katsuragi-san’s instructions from the very beginning” — Class A’s no自主 line.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishige Takurō<\/b> Ichinose’s read: he would not quietly sit on Katsuragi’s plan — Sakayanagi faction first.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The faction Morishige answers to, not Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The defensive vote Ryuuen bent: even Katsuragi could vote in the riskless half hour on a 1% Kushida seed.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The seed question that would have convinced his bloc.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; three mention anchors only.<span class=\"pg\">p.226-242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.0: the iron fortress still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p227-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka hamaguchi-tetsuya","q":"ch 5  5 2  the sim experiment named in ichinose s lecture as her partner in the sim card swap test that found the lock","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p227-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html#sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p227-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the SIM experiment<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.227<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ichinose’s lecture as her partner in the SIM-card swap test that found the lock.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Hamaguchi and I had tried swapping SIM cards once to see what would happen, but the SIM cards are locked to their designated phones.”<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The experiment’s result — SIM locked to device — is the weak point he and Ichinose built their counter-swap on.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The victim of the lecture; his own SIM lock release is the answer she withholds until p.230.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Mention only; not at the café.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p217-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2: the Outcome #1 plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p230-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki karuizawa-kei kouenji-rokusuke ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 5  5 2 5 3  the plan s author  then the cafe gets the credit line from ichinose    her plan was a huge success    then runs the cafe debrief with hirata  absorbs ryuuen s kushida reveal and the class c blowout  and talks ayanokoji out of his premonition   ahh  when i see you people  i can t help but sigh  muttered horikita   ignore him  think of him as a ghost that attached itself to my back  horikita said flatly   you re in the way  get lost  she spat   in that case  do you believe you ll end up with good results   you re in the way  horikita grumbled   minami kun was the horse group vip  right  asked horikita   did one of us send an email for the other groups  asked horikita   ah  he s probably okay  yamauchi kun was in the rooster group  it seems he did try sending an email but agonized over it for too long  the test ended before he could actually send it  said horikita   this exam was all about testing our thinking  it s not like every single question would have an answer  said horikita   what i m worried about is that those four emails came in at almost the exact same time  the school said we had a timeframe of thirty minutes at the end of the test to betray someone  but all the emails came within one to two seconds of each other  she said   when kouenji kun sent the email to betray his group  the school responded without delay  if you think about how fast it was  it must have been automated  horikita began   yeah  and there s only one person i can imagine who d do su","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p230-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p230-1\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: the plan’s author, then the café<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.230–243<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gets the credit line from Ichinose — “her plan was a huge success” — then runs the café debrief with Hirata, absorbs Ryuuen’s Kushida reveal and the Class C blowout, and talks Ayanokōji out of his premonition.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Ahh. When I see you people, I can’t help but sigh,” muttered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Ignore him. Think of him as a ghost that attached itself to my back,” Horikita said flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You’re in the way. Get lost,” she spat.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>34 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The relayed verdict on the phone swap; Ayanokōji is told to say it was her plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Shuts him down repeatedly — “You’re in the way. Get lost,” “Sudou-kun, be quiet” — then lets him stay as chair-grabbing baggage.<span class=\"pg\">p.235-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, do you believe you’ll end up with good results?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re in the way,” Horikita grumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Minami-kun was the Horse group VIP, right?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did one of us send an email for the other groups?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, he’s probably okay. Yamauchi-kun was in the Rooster group. It seems he did try sending an email but agonized over it for too long. The test ended before he could actually send it,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The Rooster who froze on the send button — her prediction he would have guessed wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Accepts the girls-side report flatly — no social pull of her own, so she takes what controllers say.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This exam was all about testing our thinking. It’s not like every single question would have an answer,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What I’m worried about is that those four emails came in at almost the exact same time. The school said we had a timeframe of thirty minutes at the end of the test to betray someone, but all the emails came within one to two seconds of each other,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The automated-timing deduction with Hirata — four simultaneous betrayals = one class showing off.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When Kouenji-kun sent the email to betray his group, the school responded without delay. If you think about how fast it was, it must have been automated,” Horikita began.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> His earlier betrayal email is the calibration point for the school’s speed.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. And there’s only one person I can imagine who’d do such a thing.” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The sixth guest she expected; the Kushida reveal hits her confidence; the threat leaves her staring at the results without a comeback.<span class=\"pg\">p.237-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I chose this space because even an idiot like you would be able to find it quite easily. You should be grateful,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I disliked your persistent harassment. I was talking to them about it,” said Horikita flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou-kun, be quiet,” Horikita snapped.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “More or less. You look rather relaxed,” Horikita said.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m quite glad to hear that. I look forward to the results,” she replied with confidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I’m hearing the irritating whine of a loser. The test has already ended, and no one in the Dragon group has turned traitor. That can only mean one thing,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Her certainty that Ryuuen never got it — broken when he says the name.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “All right, tell me then. Who is the Dragon group VIP?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re joking, right? If that’s true, you would have turned traitor and sent an email. But the test didn’t end like that. That must mean you realized that fact after the exam had ended. There’s no other way. Am I wrong?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me?” she asked, dumbfounded.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop with the jokes!”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s… I’m sure you could’ve just heard it from someone else,” Horikita stammered.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? What did you do?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class C +150 cl and +5.5 Million pr — “Class C…came out on top,” stunned at the table.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class C…came out on top,” muttered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His trouble-warning; her calm rebuttal that Ryuuen’s win does not guarantee future danger.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By trouble, you mean Ryuuen-kun? It’s true he did very well in this test, but there’s no guarantee he’ll be dangerous in the future. Your group won their test, after all. Didn’t they?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The composed front after the humiliation — she keeps him from spiraling into the premonition.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p207-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1: the night meet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p230-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka hoshinomiya-chie","q":"ch 5  5 2  the unlock authority ichinose cites her confirmation  with enough points the sim device lock releases immediately","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p230-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html#sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p230-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the unlock authority<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.230<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ichinose cites her confirmation: with enough points the SIM device lock releases immediately.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “I checked with Hoshinomiya-sensei to confirm. She said that with enough points, you can unlock the device right away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> SIM lock release is a point purchase — the loophole that makes the double swap work on a ship at sea.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He had already paid for the same unlock on Karuizawa’s phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named only; no scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p167-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.3: the drunk interruption<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p231-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 5  5 2 5 3  the paper  the survey  the model the withheld vip knowledge named on the page  then the cafe approach about  that piece of paper  the group survey proving no class d betrayal  the timing deduction with horikita  and the puzzled dragon outcome  1 question   i m guessing you re talking about that piece of paper you gave me  right  ayanokouji kun  hirata s approach from behind made karuizawa jump in shock   excellent work on this test  both of you  may i sit  he asked   it s just about time  is horikita san still not here  shouldn t we contact her  asked hirata   ah  looks like she s here  said hirata   i was a little apprehensive about that  so i went around and asked people in the individual groups earlier  none of the guys said they turned traitor  hirata answered   so it s likely that all of the emails were sent together  in other words  the betrayal emails all came from one class  hirata finished her thought   they might have sent the emails at the exact same time as a way of showing off their supremacy  hirata added   how did you figure it out  asked hirata  his question contained a mixture of curiosity and fear   i understand that ryuuen kun managed to discover the vips in class a  sure  but i m not convinced he has some kind of preternatural talent  still  how did dragon group end up with that result  asked hirata   what do you mean","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p231-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p231-1\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: the paper, the survey, the model<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.231–242<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The withheld VIP knowledge named on the page; then the café approach about “that piece of paper,” the group survey proving no Class D betrayal, the timing deduction with Horikita, and the puzzled Dragon Outcome #1 question.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I’m guessing you’re talking about that piece of paper you gave me. Right, Ayanokouji-kun?” Hirata’s approach from behind made Karuizawa jump in shock.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Excellent work on this test, both of you. May I sit?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “It’s just about time. Is Horikita-san still not here? Shouldn’t we contact her?” asked Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Kept Karuizawa’s VIP status from him and Yukimura at first; the café line “that piece of paper you gave me” ties back to the earlier insurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.231, 234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Makes her jump — the breakup scream is still fresh; she shifts but does not refuse the seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, looks like she’s here,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was a little apprehensive about that, so I went around and asked people in the individual groups earlier. None of the guys said they turned traitor,” Hirata answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The boys-side survey across every group — the report Class D trusts for the no-betrayal read.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Natural rapport — he finishes her automation thought before she has to.<span class=\"pg\">p.236-237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So it’s likely that all of the emails were sent together. In other words, the betrayal emails all came from one class.” Hirata finished her thought.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “They might have sent the emails at the exact same time as a way of showing off their supremacy,” Hirata added.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How did you figure it out?” asked Hirata. His question contained a mixture of curiosity and fear.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The fear-curious question after the Kushida reveal; later the pushback that he is not convinced of preternatural talent.<span class=\"pg\">p.239, 242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand that Ryuuen-kun managed to discover the VIPs in Class A, sure, but I’m not convinced he has some kind of preternatural talent. Still, how did Dragon Group end up with that result?” asked Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The answer he protected all test sits at the centre of Ayanokōji’s 1% explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Named as the defensive voter who could still move in the riskless half hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No answer to his Dragon question from anyone but Ayanokōji — the table is stunned silent first.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4: Sugimura and the last Class D VIP<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p231-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 5  5 2 5 3  named  then seated the real vip whose name ichinose types   5 3 opens with her meek cafe arrival  the insurance question  and the girls side no betrayal report that settles horikita s worry   sorry to keep you waiting  she said   ah  um  i was just wondering if everything really went okay  she said   how can you say that for sure  she asked   i ve already checked  no one sent an email  said karuizawa without hesitation  as controller of the class d girls  she could be as certain as hirata of her information","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p231-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p231-1\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: named, then seated<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.231–241<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The real VIP whose name Ichinose types; §5.3 opens with her meek café arrival, the insurance question, and the girls-side no-betrayal report that settles Horikita’s worry.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Sorry to keep you waiting,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ah, um. I was just wondering if everything really went okay,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “How can you say that for sure?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The name on the betrayal message she never sends; the behavioural read — looking over, face tightening.<span class=\"pg\">p.231-232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The double swap ran on her phone; the café seat and the piece-of-paper insurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.231, 234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Something about her expression seemed different” — meek rather than her usual edge after the stairwell.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Jumps when he approaches; shifts in her seat but does not refuse him — the breakup still raw.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve already checked. No one sent an email,” said Karuizawa without hesitation. As controller of the Class D girls, she could be as certain as Hirata of her information.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Controller’s report — the girls-side certainty that pairs with Hirata’s boys-side survey.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her flat acceptance: without social pull Horikita must take what the controllers say.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ichinose’s guess on her: “The real VIP is Karuizawa Kei-san. Am I right?” — correct, unsent when the four notes sound.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p222-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2: the strap phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-morishige-takurou-y1v4-p233-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami sakayanagi-arisu katsuragi-kouhei morishige-takurou","q":"ch 5  5 2  the predicted traitor ichinose names him as her guess for class a s traitor   sakayanagi s faction  too independent for katsuragi s plan","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-morishige-takurou-y1v4-p233-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2: the predicted traitor<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.233<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morishige-takurou\">Morishige Takurō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ichinose names him as her guess for Class A’s traitor — Sakayanagi’s faction, too independent for Katsuragi’s plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her reasoning: he “probably figured that, if anything, it was better for him to betray the group and take the points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The faction tie that makes him disobey Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The plan he would not “quietly go along with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Rooster: Outcome #3 — the traitor answered correctly; Ichinose’s guess lands on the group Morishige was in. (her line + results list)<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She says “probably”; the page never confirms the traitor’s name — kept as her prediction.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-morishige-takurou-y1v4-p155-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the silent Class A seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p233-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"morishige-takurou ichinose-honami sakayanagi-arisu","q":"ch 5  5 2  the faction behind the traitor named as the faction morishige answers to in ichinose s traitor prediction","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p233-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html#sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p233-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the faction behind the traitor<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.233<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the faction Morishige answers to in Ichinose’s traitor prediction.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morishige-takurou\">Morishige Takurō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishige Takurō<\/b> “He’s a member of Sakayanagi’s faction” — the reason he would break Katsuragi’s plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The analyst making the guess from Class B’s side.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Mention only; no presence in this chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p158-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the absent faction leader<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p235-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru sudou-ken","q":"ch 5  5 3  the sixth wheel trails horikita into the cafe as the attached ghost  is told to get lost twice  stays anyway  chides ryuuen about the last results  and is ignored through the kushida reveal   aw  come on  don t say that  horikita  i just thought you might be nervous during the test  so i was worried about you  that s why i came to check on you   h hey  don t say that  i gave this test everything i had  you know   i was just one step behind  that s all  looks like someone else sent the email before me  he muttered   come on  it s fine  isn t it  i m just going to listen  you wouldn t cut out a classmate  right   isn t that just a coincidence  asked sudou  apparently  from sudou s perspective  everything was a coincidence   don t you hang all over horikita  roared sudou   and i remember that the last time they announced results  you were acting all high and mighty  but then you lost big  sudou chided  pointing a finger at ryuuen and laughing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p235-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p235-1\">Ch.5 §5.3: the sixth wheel<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.235–241<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Trails Horikita into the café as the attached ghost, is told to get lost twice, stays anyway, chides Ryuuen about the last results, and is ignored through the Kushida reveal.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Aw, come on. Don’t say that, Horikita. I just thought you might be nervous during the test, so I was worried about you. That’s why I came to check on you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “H-hey, don’t say that. I gave this test everything I had, you know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “I was just one step behind, that’s all. Looks like someone else sent the email before me,” he muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I just thought you might be nervous… I came to check on you”; she calls him a ghost, spat “Get lost,” and shuts him up — he sinks back obediently.<span class=\"pg\">p.235-238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The email he claims he almost sent — one step behind, someone beat him to it; then the chair-grab and “You wouldn’t cut out a classmate, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235-236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on. It’s fine, isn’t it? I’m just going to listen. You wouldn’t cut out a classmate, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Rises to threaten on sight, chides him about the last results loss, then is snapped down by Horikita’s “Sudou-kun, be quiet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237-238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t that just a coincidence?” asked Sudou. Apparently, from Sudou’s perspective, everything was a coincidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you hang all over Horikita!” roared Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And I remember that the last time they announced results, you were acting all high and mighty. But then you lost big,” Sudou chided, pointing a finger at Ryuuen and laughing.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Surprisingly docile” after the snap — the roar is all; he sinks back on command.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Present for the whole results scene; no role in the deductions — the row marks the unusual crowd.<span class=\"pg\">p.235-241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p183-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.5–4.7: the Cow name and the warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p236-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 5  5 3  the rooster who hesitated reported by horikita  rooster group  tried to send the betrayal email  agonized too long  test ended first","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p236-1\">Ch.5 §5.3: the Rooster who hesitated<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.236<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reported by Horikita: Rooster group, tried to send the betrayal email, agonized too long, test ended first.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her report and her prediction he would have guessed wrong — “the moment he hesitated to send that email, it was all over for him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “He wasn’t the cocksure guy he imagined himself to be” — the reckless image broken by one hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Is Yamauchi okay?” — asked and answered; no further stake.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Mention only; Rooster’s actual Outcome #3 comes from the results list.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4: the contrast name<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p237-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 5  5 3  the automated calibration and the saviour his earlier betrayal email fixes the school s response speed in horikita s timing deduction  p 242 names him as having saved class d s victory from total class c sweep","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p237-1\">Ch.5 §5.3: the automated calibration and the saviour<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.237–242<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">His earlier betrayal email fixes the school’s response speed in Horikita’s timing deduction; p.242 names him as having saved Class D’s victory from total Class C sweep.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The data point — school responded without delay, so the four simultaneous emails must be automated.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “Kouenji saved our asses” — without his group’s betrayal email the victory would have belonged exclusively to Class C; his action also sent stray bullets at other VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The four-email timing Kouenji’s single email helped expose as one-class showmanship.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named only; no presence at the café.<span class=\"pg\">p.237-242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p125-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the traitor act on everyone’s lips<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 5  5 3  the sixth guest invited as the deliberate sixth seat  slams a chair beside horikita  names kushida as dragon vip from her body language  shows the class a vip list  claims the four email timing  and declares horikita his next target   i thought i d enjoy finding out the results with you all  thanks so much for gathering in such an easy to find place  he said mockingly   anyway  suzune  you ve got a rather large group with you  have you grown more sociable  muttered ryuuen  looking out at the other four people gathered around the table and ignoring sudou completely   i didn t think you actually had any friends  ryuuen teased   the results will be announced any minute now  are you expecting any results  he asked   heh  i wouldn t be here if i wasn t  looks like the same crowd as the last time  replied ryuuen   stop it  suzune  you know if you get carried away now  you ll just be embarrassed later  i already know our group s vip  said ryuuen   there s no need to wait for the announcement  want me to tell you who the dragon group vip is  he asked   if you could only understand the depth of my mercy  you d be moved  so moved that you ll get wet between your thighs  ryuuen laughed  as though such vulgar language was funny   kushida kikyou   i m sorry  but i ve known kushida was the vip since the second day of the test  ryuuen said   i just felt so sorry for you  you were oh so incredibly confident in your victory that you looked down on others  you were desperate to get ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1\">Ch.5 §5.3: the sixth guest<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.237–243<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Invited as the deliberate sixth seat, slams a chair beside Horikita, names Kushida as Dragon VIP from her body language, shows the Class A VIP list, claims the four-email timing, and declares Horikita his next target.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I thought I’d enjoy finding out the results with you all. Thanks so much for gathering in such an easy-to-find place,” he said mockingly.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Anyway, Suzune, you’ve got a rather large group with you. Have you grown more sociable?” muttered Ryuuen, looking out at the other four people gathered around the table and ignoring Sudou completely.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I didn’t think you actually had any friends,” Ryuuen teased.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>27 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The whole set piece is aimed at her — teasing, the reveal, “you’re my next target… tear you to shreds, both in mind and body.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Ignored on arrival; Sudou’s chide about the last results is brushed into the Kushida play.<span class=\"pg\">p.238-239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The results will be announced any minute now. Are you expecting any results?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh. I wouldn’t be here if I wasn’t. Looks like the same crowd as the last time,” replied Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop it, Suzune. You know if you get carried away now, you’ll just be embarrassed later. I already know our group’s VIP,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need to wait for the announcement. Want me to tell you who the Dragon group VIP is?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you could only understand the depth of my mercy, you’d be moved. So moved that you’ll get wet between your thighs.” Ryuuen laughed, as though such vulgar language was funny.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida Kikyou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The name dropped cold — known since the second day of the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I’ve known Kushida was the VIP since the second day of the test,” Ryuuen said.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just felt so sorry for you. You were oh-so-incredibly confident in your victory that you looked down on others. You were desperate to get your stories straight, assuming no one would get the answer right. That’s why I went along with it until the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata’s “How did you figure it out?” carries curiosity and fear; the answer names Horikita, not him.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, the answer to that… Well, it involves you, Suzune,” answered Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I figured it out because of your body. The movements of your eyes and mouth. Your breathing. Your behavior. Your tone. Everything about you told me that you were lying,” continued Ryuuen in an eerie voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Body-language read of Horikita’s lie — the method that beat the VIP secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jokes? If it’s a joke, then how do I know the truth?”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand how you feel. You don’t want to admit that you’re the most incompetent person in the group. But don’t beat yourself up, Suzune. You merely chose the wrong opponent. Besides, this exam was supposed to be pure chaos. At any rate, Class A is in for an especially rude awakening. Relax.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ll understand soon enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The four simultaneous betrayal emails — Rat, Horse, Monkey, Rooster answered correctly; he played a major part; Class A VIP list on his screen for Rat, Rooster and Pig.<span class=\"pg\">p.240-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t this great, Suzune? Thanks to your blunder, the Dragon group managed to clear this test with Outcome #1. Because of that, all the classes should receive a boost in points,” Ryuuen crowed. He clapped his hands and wore a satisfied grin. “If you beg for it, I’ll tell you the answer. How about it?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ooh, that look you have. It’s pretty sexy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I made some adjustments and arrived at the root of the test. Then, I just focused on the Class A students,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Cleared without targeting Classes B or D at all — the Class A VIP harvest on one screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry to tell you, Suzune, but you’re my next target. I’m going after you with everything I’ve got. I won’t stop until I tear you to shreds, both in mind and body.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m looking forward to the second semester,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Walks away with his payback for the island — the threat Ayanokōji turns into quiet excitement.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The defensive vote he bent to 1% — named in Ayanokōji’s explanation of Dragon Outcome #1.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.0: the frontal assault still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p239-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 5  5 3  the name that broke the table named aloud as dragon group vip by ryuuen   known to him since day two   and the fact that dragon cleared outcome  1 without a traitor makes her the centre of ayanokoji s 1  explanation   kushida kikyou   his line  naming her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p239-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p239-1\">Ch.5 §5.3: the name that broke the table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.239–242<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named aloud as Dragon group VIP by Ryuuen — known to him since day two — and the fact that Dragon cleared Outcome #1 without a traitor makes her the centre of Ayanokōji’s 1% explanation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Kushida Kikyou.” (his line, naming her)<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He never turned traitor despite knowing; the reveal is saved for the café audience.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her confidence — “no one in the Dragon group has turned traitor” — is exactly what he weaponises.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Flabbergasted beside her; he had carefully protected her identity all test.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The seed-planted theory: tell everyone “Kushida is the VIP” in the riskless half hour and even Katsuragi votes for the 1%.<span class=\"pg\">p.241-242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Dragon: Outcome #1 — the entire group answered correctly at the end of the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is not at the café; the row records the public naming of her VIP status.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p207-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1–5.2: the Dragon VIP behind the swap<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
